[Term]
id: CL:0000552
name: orthochromatic erythroblast
namespace: cell
def: "The final stage of the nucleated, immature erythrocyte, before nuclear loss. Typically the cytoplasm is described as acidophilic, but it still shows a faint polychromatic tint. The nucleus is small and initially may still have coarse, clumped chromatin, as in its precursor, the polychromatophilic erythroblast, but ultimately it becomes pyknotic, and appears as a deeply staining, blue-black, homogeneous structureless mass. The nucleus is often eccentric and sometimes lobulated." []
synonym: "acidophilic erythroblast" EXACT []
synonym: "eosinophilic erythroblast" EXACT []
synonym: "late erythoblast" EXACT []
synonym: "orthochromatic normoblast" EXACT []
synonym: "pyknotic eto enrythroblast" EXACT []
xref: FMA:84646
