[Term]
id: CL:0000560
name: band form neutrophil
namespace: cell
def: "A late neutrophilic metamyelocyte in which the nucleus is indented to more than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin but in no area being condensed to a single filament. The nucleus is in the form of a curved or coiled band, not having acquired the typical multilobar shape of the mature neutrophil. These cells are fMLP receptor-positive, CD11b-positive, CD35-negative, and CD49d-negative." []
comment: Found in the Band 1 fraction.
synonym: "band" BROAD []
