[Term]
id: CL:0000570
name: parafollicular cell
namespace: cell
def: "A neuroepithelial cells that occurs singly or in small groups, close to the outer follicular borders but within the follicular basement membrane of the thyroid. Expresses a form of the neural cell adhesion molecule (N-CAM) on their surface. Secretes calcitonin, 5-hydroxytryptamine and dopamine." []
synonym: "C cell" EXACT []
synonym: "C cell of thyroid gland" EXACT []
synonym: "clear cell of thyroid gland" EXACT []
synonym: "parafollicular cell of thyroid gland" EXACT []
