creation_date: 2010-06-28T08:36:15Z

[Term]
id: CL:0002069
name: type II vestibular sensory cell
namespace: cell
def: "Mostly cylindrical, resemble Type 1 in their contents and the presence of a kinocilium and stereocilium apically; much greater variation in size, some almost span the entire thickness of the sensory epithelium, while others are smaller than Type 1; receive multiple efferent nerve boutons around their bases as well as afferent endings, which are small expansions rather than chalices." []
synonym: "type 2 vestibular hair cell" EXACT []
synonym: "type 2 vestibular sensory cell" EXACT []
synonym: "type II hair cell" EXACT []
