[Term]
id: CL:0002289
name: type I taste bud cell
namespace: cell
def: "A densely staining taste receptor cell that contains many dense vacuoles in their apical regions which project into the apical space and bear microvilli. This cell type serves as a supporting cell by surrounding and isolating the other cell types from each other; secrete a dense amorphous material that surrounds the microvilli in the taste pore. This cell type expresses a glial glutumate transporter, GLAST." []
synonym: "dark tongue cell" EXACT []
synonym: "type I taste cell" EXACT []
