[Term]
id: CTENO:0000062
name: quadrant
def: "One of of four nearly identical quadrants organized along the oral-aboral axis. Each of the four quadrants is derived largely from one cell of the four-cell-stage embryo. At the eight-cell stage each quadrant contains a single E (\"end\") and M (\"middle\") blastomere. Subsequently, micromeres are formed first at the aboral pole and later at the oral pole." [] {http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/core#source="PMID:10525332"}
is_a: UBERON:0000475 ! organism subdivision

