[Term]
id: FBbt:00000197
name: posterior spiracle primordium (Drosophila)
def: "Primordium of the posterior spiracle of the larva. Originates in the posterior half of the lateral ectoderm of abdominal segment 8 during stage 12. A a group of cells that are more basophilic that those surrounding them form a deep groove and fuse with the posterior arm of the tracheal primordium of A8 (tracheal metamere 10)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
