[Term]
id: FBbt:00001276
name: B-subperineurial glial cell of abdomen (Drosophila)
def: "Large subperineural glial cell that sits over the posterior commissure just medial to the longitudinal connectives (Klambt and Goodman, 1991; Ito et al., 1995). It sends processes in three directions: medially to the midline, anteriorly and posteriorly (Ito et al., 1995). Unlike the A-subperineural glial cell, the B-subperineural glial cell is only found in abdominal segments of the embryo and larvae, and lies at approximately the centre of the segment along the antero-posterior axis (Ito et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0054242, FlyBase:FBrf0057603, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "B glial cell of abdomen" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0054242]
synonym: "B subperineurial glial cell of abdomen" EXACT []
synonym: "B-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
