[Term]
id: FBbt:00001285
name: medial dorsal subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the ventral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord. It lies between the intersegmental nerve roots, at 30-60% along the medio-lateral axis, slightly antero-lateral to the medial intersegmental nerve root glial cell." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "MD-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001286
name: lateral dorsal subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the ventral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord. It lies near, but slightly above, the exit point of the peripheral nerve, at 80-90% along the medio-lateral axis." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "LD-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001287
name: dorsal lateral subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the lateral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord, and is located dorsal to the ventral lateral subperineurial glial cell. It lies at about 30% along the ventro-dorsal axis, and occasionally there are two of these cells per neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0053376, FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "belt glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0053376]
synonym: "DL-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001288
name: ventral lateral subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the lateral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord, and is located ventral to the dorsal lateral subperineurial glial cell. It lies at about 30% along the ventro-dorsal axis, and occasionally there are two of these cells per neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0053376, FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "belt glial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0053376]
synonym: "VL-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001289
name: lateral ventral subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the ventral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord, and lies antero-lateral to the medial ventral subperineurial glial cell. In the abdominal segments, it lies 0-10% along the antero-posterior axis and 60-90% along the medio-lateral axis." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "LV-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001373 ! neuroblast NB1-1 of abdomen (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001290
name: medial ventral subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, subperineurial glial cell located on the ventral surface of the embryonic/larval ventral nerve cord, and lies more medially than the lateral ventral subperineurial glial cell. In the abdominal segments, it lies 50% along the antero-posterior axis and 30-50% along the medio-lateral axis, but it lies slightly more medially in the thoracic segments." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "MV-SPG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00007598 ! embryonic/larval CNS subperineurial glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001292
name: dorsal channel glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, channel glial cell that lies at the dorsal-end of the channel above the neuropil. The cells send processes ventrally along the channel, while receiving processes from the A-SPG cells. There are two dorsal channel glial cells per hemisegment and their processes form, along with processes from the ventral channel glia, a sheath structure that covers the inner surface of the dorsoventral channel." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "D-CG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001255 ! channel glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001293
name: medial channel glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, channel glial cell that lies just beneath the ventral side of the cortex/neuropil interface. There are 3-4 medial channel glial cells and they send their processes to and along the dorsoventral channel." [FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "M-CG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001255 ! channel glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001294
name: medial channel glial cell 1 (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior-most of the two medial channel glial cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "M-CG1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001293 ! medial channel glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001295
name: medial channel glial cell 2 (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior-most of the two medial channel glial cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "M-CG2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001293 ! medial channel glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001296
name: ventral channel glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Surface-associated, channel glial cell that lies at the ventral-end of the channel above the neuropil. There are two of these cells per hemisegment and their processes form, along with processes from the dorsal channel glia, a sheath structure that covers the inner surface of the dorsoventral channel." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "V-CG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001255 ! channel glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001297
name: cortex associated CNS glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Glial cell lying amongst the neuronal cell bodies of the lateral and ventral cortex (Ito et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
is_a: FBbt:00001256 ! CNS glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007114 ! cell body rind of the central nervous system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001298
name: embryonic/larval cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Glial cell located amongst neuronal cell bodies in the cortex of the embryonic/larval central nervous system. In the abdominal and thoracic segments there are typically 3-4 and 4-5 cell body glia per hemineuromere, respectively, though their positions vary between individuals. The nuclei and cell bodies of the cell body glial cells have quite irregular shapes, and cytoplasmic protrusions fill the space between neighboring neuronal cell bodies (Ito et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "cell body glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "CoG" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00001251 ! embryonic/larval glial cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00001297 ! cortex associated CNS glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001919 ! embryonic/larval central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001299
name: medial-most cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell body glial cell that lies close to the midline in the center of the segment. It lies between 10-20% along the mediolateral axis, and at approximately 50% along the anterioposterior axis, and flanks the ventral unpaired median (VUM) neuron cluster on the midline. The thoracic hemineuromere has two medial-most cell body glial cells, whilst the abdominal hemineuromere has only one." [FlyBase:FBrf0054242, FlyBase:FBrf0068598, FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "MM-CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "VUM support cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0068598]
synonym: "VUM-support cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0054242]
is_a: FBbt:00001298 ! embryonic/larval cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001399 ! neuroblast NB6-4 (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001300
name: medial cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell body glial cell located in the ventral cortex, lateral to the medial-most cell body glia. Its position varies between 20% and 80% along the mediolateral axis." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "M-CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "medial CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
is_a: FBbt:00001298 ! embryonic/larval cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001399 ! neuroblast NB6-4 (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001301
name: ventrolateral cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Ventrolaterally located cell body glial cell, located in the lateral cortex more medial to the lateral cell body glial cell. This cell is not present in all animals." [FlyBase:FBrf0082171, FlyBase:FBrf0214261]
synonym: "ventrolateral CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
synonym: "VL-CBG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0082171]
