[Term]
id: FBbt:00001665
name: dorsal vessel primordium (Drosophila)
def: "Primordium that makes the inner, contractile layer of the embryonic/larval dorsal vessel. This primordium originates in the mesodermal crest on each side of the embryo. Its component cells (embryonic cardioblasts) become distinct by stage 14. The dorsal vessel is formed by fusion of left and right primordia during, and immediately following, dorsal closure." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0151925]
synonym: "dorsal vessel specific anlage" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0002050 ! embryonic structure
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6005461 ! circulatory system primordium
relationship: develops_from UBERON:6005541 ! cardiogenic mesoderm
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005331 ! dorsal closure embryo (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001667
name: embryonic/larval pericardial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell type forming the outer layer of the dorsal vessel in the embryonic/larval abdomen. These cells sequester macromolecules from the hemolymph." [FlyBase:FBrf0151925, PMID:18355807]
synonym: "larval pericardial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "nephrocyte" RELATED [PMID:18971929]
is_a: CL:0000474 ! pericardial nephrocyte
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005466 ! pericardial cell primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001664 ! embryonic/larval circulatory system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001669
name: primary lobe of embryonic/larval lymph gland (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior-most and largest of the 3-6 lobe pairs of the third instar embryonic/larval lymph gland. These lobes are bulbous. Three distinct zones are identified: the medullary zone in the center, the cortical zone in the periphery and the posterior signaling center. At the late third instar the medullary zone contains quiescent prohemocytes, the cortical zone the proliferating hemocytes and the posterior signalling center functions as a stem-cell niche." [FlyBase:FBrf0074444, FlyBase:FBrf0187467, FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
synonym: "anterior lymph gland pair" EXACT []
synonym: "primary lymph gland lobe" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0187467]
is_a: UBERON:6001668 ! embryonic/larval lymph gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001670
name: secondary lobe of embryonic/larval lymph gland (Drosophila)
def: "Second most anterior pair of lobes of the third instar larval lymph gland. They are bulbous like the anterior lobes, but smaller than them. It is composed of prohemocytes, and rarely it contains a differentiated cell." [FlyBase:FBrf0074444, FlyBase:FBrf0187467, FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
synonym: "middle lymph gland pair" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
is_a: UBERON:6001668 ! embryonic/larval lymph gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001671
name: tertiary lobe of embryonic/larval lymph gland (Drosophila)
def: "Pair of lymph gland lobes posterior to the secondary lobes. Unlike the more anterior lobes, these are small and elongate. The tertiary lobe is composed of prohemocytes. There may be multiple pairs of these lobes." [FlyBase:FBrf0074444, FlyBase:FBrf0187467, FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
synonym: "posterior lymph gland pair" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
synonym: "tertiary lobe" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208762]
is_a: UBERON:6001668 ! embryonic/larval lymph gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001672
name: alary cell (Drosophila)
def: "Twist expressing cell associated with the alary muscles in late stage embryos (present by late stage 15, early stage 16)." [FlyBase:FBrf0053819]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001664 ! embryonic/larval circulatory system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001673
name: embryonic/larval dorsal vessel (Drosophila)
def: "A contractile tube that extends from immediately behind the posterior commissure of T1 to the arthrodial membrane of A7, into which it inserts via two caudally directed muscles which connect to lateral apodemes in A8. Throughout its length, its lumen is enclosed by just two cardial cells. The cardial cell layer is only a single-cell thick, and is surrounded by a single-cell thick layer of pericardial cells, except in the posterior thorax, where it is surrounded by lymph gland in the anterior thorax where it passes through the ring gland. The whole tube is attached to the anterior of each abdominal segment boundary by alary muscles." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval dorsal vessel" EXACT []
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001664 ! embryonic/larval circulatory system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001674
name: embryonic/larval aorta (Drosophila)
def: "The embryonic/larval dorsal vessel from its anterior tip to the middle of segment 4, where it broadens to become the heart." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval aorta" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007323 ! embryonic aortic cardioblast (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001673 ! embryonic/larval dorsal vessel (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001675
name: embryonic/larval heart (Drosophila)
def: "The embryonic/larval dorsal vessel from the middle of A4 to its posterior tip. It is broader and has a larger lumen then the aorta." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval heart" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007322 ! embryonic heart cardioblast (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001673 ! embryonic/larval dorsal vessel (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001677
name: embryonic/larval ostia (Drosophila)
