[Term]
id: FBbt:00001694
name: embryonic/larval oenocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Embryonic/larval oenocytes are large, polyploid cells whose cytoplasm contains yellowish granules. They are arranged in clusters in abdominal segments 1-7, under the epidermis, to which they are attached by fine elastic cellular extensions. As the animal ages, the number of granules increases and the cells become highly enlarged relative to their neighbors. These cells have been shown to function in the breakdown of stored lipids and may also control feeding behaviour (Gutierrez et al., 2007). These cells degenerate during late pupal stages." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0192579]
synonym: "larval oenocyte" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000487 ! oenocyte
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007021 ! embryonic/larval oenocyte precursor (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001695 ! abdominal larval oenocyte group (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000323 ! late embryo

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001695
name: abdominal larval oenocyte group (Drosophila)
def: "A cluster of 4-9 larval oenocytes situated bilaterally in each of abdominal segments 1-7 in a space between the dorsoventral muscles and the body wall. Each cell group is closely associated with an 'abdominal lateral pentascolopidial chordotonal organ lch5' and is supplied by its own tracheal branch." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0134578]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00017020 ! oenocyte primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001746 ! larval abdomen

