id: FBbt:00001704
name: embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)
def: "Fat body of the embryo/larva." [FBC:SPR]
synonym: "larval fat body" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0003917 ! arthropod fat body
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005067 ! fat body primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001703 ! embryonic/larval adipose system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001705
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 1 (Drosophila)
def: "Most anterior region of the larval fat body. It is of triangular shape and located over the brain." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001706
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 2' (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, posterior to region 1. It consists of a descending band of cells extending over the salivary gland that joins with a ventral commissure that connects to the two main lateral sheets of the fat body. There are two of these similar branches per larvae (2' and 2'')." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001707
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 2'' (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, posterior to region 1. It consists of a descending band of cells extending over the salivary gland that joins with a ventral commissure that connects to the two main lateral sheets of the fat body. There are two of these similar branches per larvae (2' and 2'')." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001708
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 3' (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, dorsal and posterior to the ventral commissure that connects to the two main lateral sheets of the fat body." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001709
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 3'' (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, ventral and posterior to the ventral commissure that connects to the two main lateral sheets of the fat body." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001710
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 4 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, posterior to regions 3' and 3'', and anterior to the gonad." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001711
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 5 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, posterior to region 4 and to the gonad." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001712
name: embryonic/larval fat body region 6 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the larval fat body, that runs parallel to the heart and the tracheal trunks and dorsal to the gonad." [FlyBase:FBrf0031020]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001713
name: anterior fat body plate (Drosophila)
def: "Horizontal plate of the embryonic fat body from stage 13 that is located anteriorly, beneath the foregut." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001714
name: posterior fat body plate (Drosophila)
def: "Horizontal plate of the embryonic fat body from stage 13 that is located posteriorly, beneath the hindgut." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001704 ! embryonic/larval fat body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001715
name: embryonic/larval endocrine system (Drosophila)
def: "Endocrine system of the embryo/larva." [FBC:SPR]
synonym: "larval endocrine system" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000949 ! endocrine system
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000323 ! late embryo
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002548 ! larva

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001716
name: corpus allatum primordium (Drosophila)
def: "The primordium that will form the embryonic/larval corpus allatum, a substructure of the embryonic/larval ring gland. It is a paired structure that becomes distinct in early dorsal closure between the head mesoderm and the epidermis of the gnathal segments. During dorsal closure the paired primordia move dorsally to meet and fuse above the cardioblasts of the developing aorta." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00017009 ! ring gland primordium (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:6005541 ! cardiogenic mesoderm

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001717
name: corpus cardiacum primordium (Drosophila)
def: "The corpora cardiaca precursor first appear during stage 10 as two pairs of head mesoderm cells between the roof of the stomodeum and the inner surface of the brain primordium that derive from the anterior lip of the ventral furrow. Between stages 11 and 15, these cells migrate posteriorly, gradually increasing in number. During stage 15, they fuse with the precursors of the corpus allatum from the gnathal mesoderm to form the ring gland." [FlyBase:FBrf0179777]
synonym: "corpus cardiacum placode" RELATED []
synonym: "embryonic corpus allatum" BROAD []
synonym: "P1 CC" RELATED [FBC:DOS]
is_a: FBbt:00017009 ! ring gland primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004450 ! late extended germ band embryo (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001721
name: nervus corporis cardiaci I (Drosophila)
def: "Bilaterally paired nerve bundle that connects the larval ring gland to the brain. It comprises, among others, the axons of neurons from the neurosecretory cells of the pars intercerebralis. It joins the nervus corporis cardiaci II (NccII) at the medial edge of the protocerebrum, continuing towards the ring gland (de Velasco et al., 2007; Hartenstein, 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0134726, FlyBase:FBrf0193772, FlyBase:FBrf0194938]
synonym: "NCC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001911 ! insect embryonic/larval nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001724
name: prothoracic gland (Drosophila)
def: "A component of the embryonic/larval ring gland composed of a cluster of 10-20 cells on either side of the aorta. Ventrally, it is continuous with the corpus cardiaca, dorsally with the corpus allatum. It degenerates after metamorphosis." [FlyBase:FBrf0053727, FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "thoracic gland" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00007435 ! endocrine system component (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0002368 ! endocrine gland
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0010001 ! cell cluster organ
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005497 ! prothoracic gland primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001722 ! ring gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001725
name: embryonic/larval corpus allatum (Drosophila)
def: "A component of the embryonic/larval ring gland composed of a cluster of about 10 cells that sit medially on top of the aorta." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval corpus allatum" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0001057 ! corpus allatum
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001716 ! corpus allatum primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000011 ! gnathal segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001722 ! ring gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001726
name: embryonic/larval corpus cardiacum (Drosophila)
def: "A bilaterally paired neuro-endocrine structure of the embryonic/larval ring gland. In the late embryo it is composed of 6-8 small cells on each side, arranged in a U-shape around the floor of the aorta. The cells send short processes ventromedially, forming a bundle that is attached to the ventral wall of the aorta." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0179777]
synonym: "corpora cardiacum" EXACT []
synonym: "larval corpus cardiacum" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0001056 ! corpus cardiacum
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001717 ! corpus cardiacum primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000011 ! gnathal segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001722 ! ring gland

