[Term]
id: FBbt:00001834
name: imaginal ring (Drosophila)
def: "A ring shaped structure in the embryo/larva that gives rise to part of the adult." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, ISBN:978-0-521-58445-6]
is_a: UBERON:6001648 ! embryonic imaginal precursor
is_a: UBERON:6001760 ! embryonic/larval imaginal precursor

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001835
name: salivary gland imaginal ring (Drosophila)
def: "Ring of imaginal cells situated where the larval salivary glands join the salivary ducts, from which the adult salivary glands develop." [FlyBase:FBrf0064786, FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
is_a: FBbt:00001834 ! imaginal ring (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001044 ! saliva-secreting gland
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000165 ! embryonic labial segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001740 ! larval labial segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001836
name: foregut imaginal ring (Drosophila)
def: "Ring of imaginal tissue located in the embryonic/larval gut, at the junction of the foregut and midgut epithelia in the anterior part of the proventriculus. It is the precursor of the posterior region of the adult foregut." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733, FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
synonym: "proventriculus imaginal ring" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00001834 ! imaginal ring (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005611 ! adult foregut precursor (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001862 ! embryonic/larval foregut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001837
name: midgut imaginal island (Drosophila)
def: "A cluster of adult midgut precursor cells adjacent to the basement membrane of the larval midgut. These clusters are scattered throughout the larval midgut. They form by division of adult midgut precursor cells (FBbt:00000449) during larval stages. There are two such divisions during larval life, producing quartets of cells by the wandering third instar stage. Usually one, but sometimes two peripheral cells extend their processes around the adult midgut precursor that form an imaginal island." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
synonym: "midgut imaginal histoblasts" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:6001760 ! embryonic/larval imaginal precursor
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00000449 ! adult midgut precursor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001838
name: anterior midgut imaginal island (Drosophila)
def: "Imaginal island of the anterior midgut." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00001837 ! midgut imaginal island (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00000450 ! anterior adult midgut progenitor (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001839
name: posterior midgut imaginal island (Drosophila)
def: "Imaginal island of the posterior midgut." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00001837 ! midgut imaginal island (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00000451 ! posterior adult midgut progenitor (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001840
name: hindgut imaginal ring (Drosophila)
def: "Ring of imaginal tissue located at the anterior region of the embryonic/larval hindgut, posterior to where the Malpighian tubules join the hindgut, from which the adult hindgut forms. The hindgut imaginal ring cells are densely clustered, appear immature and have little cytoplasm (Murakami and Shiotsuki, 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0135849]
is_a: FBbt:00001834 ! imaginal ring (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001046 ! hindgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001841
name: anal imaginal ring (Drosophila)
def: "Imaginal tissue from which the adult anus develops." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
is_a: FBbt:00001834 ! imaginal ring (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001758 ! larval abdominal segment 11 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001843
name: embryonic/larval mouth (Drosophila)
def: "Most anterior region of the embryonic/larval gut which opens anteriorly." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
synonym: "larval mouth" NARROW []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00100323 ! embryonic/larval alimentary canal (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0008816 ! embryonic head
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001730 ! larval head

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001844
name: embryonic/larval cibarium (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior portion of the embryonic/larval pharynx, posterior to the atrium." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "embryonic/larval atrium" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0041814]
synonym: "larval cibarium" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00017019 ! cibarium primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001866 ! embryonic/larval pharynx (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000009 ! antennal segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001846
name: mouth hooks (Drosophila)
def: "A moveable pair of chitinous structures at the anterior tip of the cephalopharyngeal skeleton of the larva, on either side of the atrium. Each mouth hook has three processes: a hooked oral process extending anteriorly, a ventral process, and a dorsal process extending dorso-posteriorly to the median tooth. The mouth hooks develop from the maxillary segment." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001845 ! cephalopharyngeal skeleton

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001847
name: dental sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Sclerite that helps root the mouth hooks into their epidermal pockets (Jurgens et al., 1986)." [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "ectostomal sclerite" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001845 ! cephalopharyngeal skeleton

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001849
name: hypostomal sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Part of the pharyngeal sclerite consisting of two lateral bars connected by a bridge (H) across the floor of the atrium, just anterior to the opening of the salivary duct." [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "H-piece" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000014 ! labial segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001845 ! cephalopharyngeal skeleton

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001850
name: pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Pharyngeal component of the cephalopharyngeal skeleton." [FBC:DOS]
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001845 ! cephalopharyngeal skeleton

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001851
name: lateral process (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior portion of the cephalopharyngeal skeleton which connects posteriorly with the vertical plates. The lateral process is tightly linked to the H piece of the hypostomal sclerite (Jurgens et al., 1993)." [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "lateralgrate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "lateralgraten" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064788]
synonym: "LG" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001854
name: vertical bridge (Drosophila)
def: "Paired structure of the pharyngeal sclerite that connects the dorsal and ventral arms." [FlyBase:FBim0000950, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "vertical plate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001855
name: dorsal bridge (Drosophila)
def: "Unpaired part of the pharyngeal sclerite that connects the paired vertical bridges (vertical plates) ." [FlyBase:FBim0000950, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "latticed process" RELATED []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001856
name: embryonic/larval tentorium (Drosophila)
def: "Duct that arises from invagination from the maxillary and intercalary segments and runs between the dorsal pouch and the pharynx. It's ventral arm serves as a muscle attachment site for the ventral pharyngeal muscles (VPM 1-3)." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval tentorium" NARROW []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001857
name: embryonic/larval dorsal pouch (Drosophila)
def: "Pouch shaped epidermal structure in the embryonic and larval head formed by the movement of the dorsal fold. The embryonic dorsal pouch incorporates the acron and dorsal regions of the head segment. In the larva, it branches dorsally from the larval atrium, just behind the mouth. It contains the dorsal section of the cephalopharyngeal skeleton (dorsal bridge and dorsal arms)." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0045366, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval dorsal pouch" NARROW []
is_a: FBbt:00005807 ! dorsal pouch (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0015833 ! foregut epithelium
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001862 ! embryonic/larval foregut (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001731 ! larval ocular segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001858
name: inner layer of dorsal pouch (Drosophila)
def: "Ventral epidermal layer of the embryonic/larval dorsal pouch." [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001857 ! embryonic/larval dorsal pouch (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001859
name: outer layer of dorsal pouch (Drosophila)
def: "Dorsal epidermal layer of the embryonic/larval dorsal pouch." [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001857 ! embryonic/larval dorsal pouch (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001860
name: dorsal fold (Drosophila)
def: "Epidermal structure of the embryo head which is part of the dorsal pouch. It is formed during germ band elongation shortening, at the time when the dorsal ridge moves dorsally to reach the midline and fuse with its complement on the other side. The fold progressively moves over the clypeolabrum and procephalic lobe, advancing from caudal to rostral and from lateral to medial." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001857 ! embryonic/larval dorsal pouch (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001861
name: median tooth (Drosophila)
def: "A grey, shovel-like structure that marks the site where the posterior roof of the atrium merges with the inner layer of the dorsal pouch. It is on the midline of the atrium, at the level of the anterior processes of the H-piece (hypostomal sclerite). It is characteristic of the first larval stage." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0045366, FlyBase:FBrf0064788]
synonym: "larval labrum" RELATED []
synonym: "unpaired labrum" EXACT []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000008 ! labral segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001862
name: embryonic/larval foregut (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior-most part of the embryonic/larval alimentary canal. It opens anteriorly at the mouth and is composed of the atrium (to which the salivary glands are attached), the pharynx, and the esophagus and part of the proventriculus." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792]
synonym: "foreintestine" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
synonym: "larval foregut" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0001041 ! foregut
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005606 ! embryonic foregut (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007512 ! embryonic/larval gut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001863
name: hypopharyngeal lobe (Drosophila)
def: "Protuberance of the procephalon that marks the rudimentary third (intercalary) head segment (Hartenstein, 1993). It first becomes apparent at stage 11 of embryogenesis. This lobe bears the primordium of the hypopharyngeal organ (Jurgens and Hartenstein, 1993)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064788, FlyBase:FBrf0064803]
is_a: UBERON:0005423 ! developing anatomical structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00000010 ! intercalary segment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001862 ! embryonic/larval foregut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001864
name: keyhole structure (Drosophila)
def: "Proventriculus primordium during embryonic stage 15 when it has a keyhole shape due to buckling of the foregut tube." [FlyBase:FBrf0079140]
is_a: FBbt:00005550 ! proventriculus primordium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001865
name: alveolar cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell of the intermediate layer of the larval proventriculus. Alveolar cells are interspersed within this layer." [FlyBase:FBrf0010887]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005754 ! proventriculus intermediate layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001866
name: embryonic/larval pharynx (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the embryonic/larval foregut between the atrium and the esophagus. It consists of a bulbous epithelial tube associated with an elaborate chitinous skeleton and musculature. The anterior edge of the pharynx is delimited ventrally by the opening of the salivary gland common duct and dorsally by the median tooth of the mouth hooks. The posterior edge is delimited by the narrowing of the foregut that marks the beginning of the esophagus." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval pharynx" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0006562 ! pharynx
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001862 ! embryonic/larval foregut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001867
name: pharyngeal bar (Drosophila)
def: "Longitudinal chitinous ridge that extends ventrally along the entire length of the floor of the larval pharynx. There are 9 of these folds in third instar larvae and 7 in the second." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733, FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "pharyngeal rib" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0160641]
synonym: "pharyngeal ridge" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "T rib" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "T-bar" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6007245 ! cuticular specialization
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001866 ! embryonic/larval pharynx (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001868
name: embryonic/larval epipharynx (Drosophila)
def: "Floor of the embryonic-larval pharynx." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval epipharynx" NARROW []
is_a: FBbt:00005750 ! epipharynx (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004201 ! epipharynx primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001866 ! embryonic/larval pharynx (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000008 ! labral segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001869
name: embryonic/larval hypopharynx (Drosophila)
def: "Roof of the embryonic-larval pharynx." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval hypopharynx" NARROW []
is_a: FBbt:00005751 ! hypopharynx (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00016002 ! hypopharynx proper primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00000010 ! intercalary segment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001866 ! embryonic/larval pharynx (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00001870
name: embryonic/larval esophagus (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the embryonic/larval foregut posterior to the pharynx and anterior to the proventriculus. It has an approximately uniform diameter and is much narrower than the pharynx." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval esophagus" NARROW []
synonym: "larval oesophagus" NARROW []
