[Term]
id: FBbt:00001887
name: embryonic/larval copper cell (Drosophila)
def: "Specialised cell of the larval midgut. It secretes acid and accumulates copper. It shows a distinct apical invagination, with an opening to the lumen. The invagination is flask shaped in the posteriormost coper cells with a narrow opening, while anteriormost copper cells are beaker shaped and their opening to the lumen is larger." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0100557, FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "calycocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0002495]
synonym: "embryonic cuprophilic cell" NARROW []
synonym: "embryonic/larval cuprophilic cell" EXACT []
synonym: "larval cuprophilic cell" NARROW []
synonym: "secretory cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208023]
