[Term]
id: FBbt:00002239
name: A1-7 dorsal VUM motor neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Neuromodulatory motor neuron that innervates the internal dorsal acute and oblique muscles of larval abdominal segments A1 to A7. It exits the ventral nerve cord via the posterior root of the intersegmental nerve and fasciculates with the ISNb or ISNd intersegmental nerve branches. It innervates the DO's and DA's via type II boutons." [FlyBase:FBrf0132289]
