[Term]
id: FBbt:00002311
name: A1-7 DA2 motor neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Motor neuron developing from the second ganglion mother cell that differentiates from neuroblast NB7-1. It innervates the internal dorsal acute muscle 2 of larval abdominal segments A1 to A7. Its dendritic arborization occupies the lateral and intermediate domains of the ventral nerve cord neuropil. It exits the ventral nerve cord via the anterior root of the intersegmental nerve and innervates the DA2 muscle with type Ib boutons." [FlyBase:FBrf0099344, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0132289, FlyBase:FBrf0160715, FlyBase:FBrf0167986, FlyBase:FBrf0174847, FlyBase:FBrf0208790]
synonym: "abdominal A1-7 DA2 motor neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "abdominal U2 neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "MN-DA2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0099344]
synonym: "MN2-Ib" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0132289]
synonym: "U/CQ neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0167497]
synonym: "U2 motor neuron" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00001566 ! U2 neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007679 ! type Ib motor neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110218 ! ISN motor neuron of the intermediate neuropile of A1-7 (Drosophila)

