[Term]
id: FBbt:00002628
name: embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)
def: "A group of small, interconnected ganglia in the embryo or larva situated posterior to and between the two brain hemispheres and associated with the pharynx, esophagus, proventriculus and dorsal pouch." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval stomatogastric nervous system" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:6005096 ! stomatogastric nervous system
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001919 ! embryonic/larval central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002629
name: embryonic/larval frontal ganglion (Drosophila)
def: "A small paired ganglion of the embryonic and larval stomatogastric nervous system. At embryonic stage 17, it consists of approximately 25-30 neurons that form a U-shaped ganglion wedged between the anterior aspect of the brain hemispheres and the dorsal pharynx. The somata of the neurons surround a sparse neuropil domain and are enclosed in a glial sheath. Lateral projections from these neurons form the frontal connective. Medial projections that turn anteriorly on reaching the midline form the frontal nerve. Medial projections that turn posteriorly on reaching the midline form the recurrent nerve." [FlyBase:FBrf0064803, FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval frontal ganglion" NARROW []
synonym: "parapharyngeal ganglion" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: FBbt:00005803 ! frontal ganglion (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001079 ! delaminating stomatogastric nervous system precursor (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002628 ! embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002630
name: embryonic/larval frontal nerve (Drosophila)
def: "Embryonic or larval nerve that travels in the median cleft between the dorsal pharyngeal muscles (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It connects the tritocerebrum and the frontal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "FrN" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00100329 ! frontal nerve (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0011215 ! central nervous system cell part cluster
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002628 ! embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002631
name: embryonic/larval recurrent nerve (Drosophila)
def: "Embryonic or larval nerve connecting the frontal ganglion to the hypocerebral and paraesophageal ganglia. It contains approximately 50 neuronal projections and is surrounded by flattened cells - probably glia." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "RcN" RELATED []
synonym: "recurrens nerve" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0104745]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
is_a: UBERON:0011215 ! central nervous system cell part cluster
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002628 ! embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002632
name: embryonic/larval hypocerebral ganglion (Drosophila)
def: "Small ganglion of the embryonic or larval stomatogastric nervous system. At embryonic stage 17, it is located on the left hand side of the embryo, between the two brain hemispheres and behind the supraesophageal commissure. It is more compact than the paraesophageal ganglion and occupies a more dorsal position. It contains approximately 10-12 neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
synonym: "larval hypocerebral ganglion" NARROW []
is_a: FBbt:00005804 ! hypocerebral ganglion (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001077 ! intermediate vesicle of tSNSP (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002628 ! embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002633
name: esophageal ganglion 1 (Drosophila)
def: "Esophageal ganglion of the embryonic/larval brain. It is composed of a row of cells apposed to the esophagus and, from a dorsal perspective, it lies to the left of esophageal ganglion 2." [FlyBase:FBrf0075001]
is_a: FBbt:00005760 ! esophageal ganglion (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002632 ! embryonic/larval hypocerebral ganglion (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002634
name: esophageal ganglion 2 (Drosophila)
def: "Esophageal ganglion of the embryonic/larval brain. It is formed by a group of cells connected through the proventricular nerve to the proventricular ganglion. From a dorsal perspective, it lies to the right of esophageal ganglion 1." [FlyBase:FBrf0075001]
is_a: FBbt:00005760 ! esophageal ganglion (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002632 ! embryonic/larval hypocerebral ganglion (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002635
name: paraesophageal ganglion (Drosophila)
def: "Small ganglion of the embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system located on the right hand side of the larva, between the two brain hemispheres, behind the supraesophageal commissure. It is elongated, less compact than the hypoesophageal ganglion and occupies a more ventral position, closely attached to the esophageal wall." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: UBERON:0003339 ! ganglion of central nervous system
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00001076 ! rostral vesicle of tSNSP (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002628 ! embryonic/larval stomatogastric nervous system (Drosophila)

