[Term]
id: FBbt:00002715
name: knob in pit sensillum (Drosophila)
def: "Paired external sensillum situated dorso-laterally on the head and consisting of a knob shaped cuticular structure located in a pit and innervated by 3 dendrites - one terminating at its base and the other two extending into the knob. Putative combined mechanoreceptor (Singh and Singh, 1984) and taste sensillum (Singh, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0074007, FlyBase:FBrf0100249]
synonym: "KIP" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0074007]
