[Term]
id: FBbt:00002879
name: abdominal ventral sensillum campaniformium vc3 (Drosophila)
def: "A ventrally located campaniform sensillum of larval abdominal segments 1-7, innervated by the dendrite of a single neuron - vesC. The tormogen (socket) cell of this sensillum is unusual in having numerous short cytoplasmic extensions (Barolo et al., 2000). It fasciculates in branch c of the segmental nerve, SNc (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997)." [FlyBase:FBrf0045359, FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0132262, http://www.normalesup.org/~vorgogoz/FlyPNS/PNSdescription.html#vp3]
