[Term]
id: FBbt:00002981
name: pupal abdominal trachea (Drosophila)
def: "Specialised trachea of the pupa that branches from tracheal metameres 4 and 5 (A2 & A3 respectively) and projects posteriorly. It develops from tracheoblasts of the 4th and 5th spiracular branches, near the junctions with the transverse connectives, forming 3 - 5 major branches and many fine terminals branches. It becomes functional at pupation." [FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
is_a: FBbt:00002956 ! pupal trachea (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002982
name: pupal wing branch (Drosophila)
def: "Trachea that branches from the anterior region of the pupal lateral trunk to tracheate the developing wing." [FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
is_a: FBbt:00002956 ! pupal trachea (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002983
name: pupal haltere branch (Drosophila)
def: "Trachea that branches from the pupal lateral trunk between transverse connectives 2 and 3 to tracheate the developing haltere." [FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
is_a: FBbt:00002956 ! pupal trachea (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00002984
