def: "Ring neuron R that arborizes only in the outer ring of the ellipsoid body. Arborizing branches originate in the periphery of the ellipsoid body canal and extend inwards." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0111476]
synonym: "ebR4" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10261]
synonym: "R4 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0111476]
is_a: FBbt:00007507 ! ring neuron R (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003654
name: extrinsic ring neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Ring neuron with arborizations outside the central complex." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "ExR" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00003649 ! ring neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00003660 ! extrinsic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003655
name: extrinsic ring neuron ExR1 (Drosophila)
def: "Extrinsic ring neuron with a large soma located in the pars intercerebralis. It projects ventrally and ipsilaterally, arborizing in the superior medial protocerebrum (smpr), the upper fan-shaped body and lateral accessory lobes (ventral bodies). Its main projection then encircles the ellipsoid body and sends multiple evenly spaced projections that arborize in an anterior ring corresponding to the arborization domain of R3 neurons. Arborizations of this neuron are spiny (Hanesch et al., 1989). They are presynaptic in the fan-shaped body and ellipsoid body and postsynaptic in the lateral accessory lobes and smpr (Armstrong and Young, 2010)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0210154]
synonym: "ExR1" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10264]
is_a: FBbt:00003654 ! extrinsic ring neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003656
name: extrinsic ring neuron ExR2 (Drosophila)
def: "Extrinsic ring neuron that arborizes with blebs in the posterior of the ellipsoid body. It branches in the median protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "ExR2" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10265]
is_a: FBbt:00003654 ! extrinsic ring neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003657
name: fan-shaped neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron with a large arborization field that forms a quasi-horizontal strata within the fan-shaped body that fills it in both the transverse and longitudinal directions. They mostly extend caudally from the anterior margin of the fan-shaped body. This pattern makes some of them look like a fan, although the strata in most cases do not show a separation into 8 (or 16) segments. Some subtypes are specific to a single fan-shaped body layer." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "F neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0210154]
synonym: "fan shaped neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007515 ! large field neuron of the central complex (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003658
name: median fan-shaped neuron Fm (Drosophila)
def: "Fan-shaped neuron that projects through the ellipsoid body canal via the median bundle to arborize with bleb-like terminals in the second layer of the fan-shaped body." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "Fm neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
synonym: "Fm1" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10268]
is_a: FBbt:00007541 ! fan-shaped neuron F2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003659
name: lateral fan-shaped neuron Fl (Drosophila)
def: "Fan-shaped neuron with a fiber that reaches the fan-shaped body laterally and that extends along its anterior surface." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
is_a: FBbt:00003657 ! fan-shaped neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003660
name: extrinsic neuron (Drosophila)
def: "An interneuron that extends projections between different neuropil domains." [FBC:DOS, FBC:SPR]
is_a: CL:0000402 ! CNS interneuron

