synonym: "protocerebral bridge glomerulus 8" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003669 ! protocerebral bridge slice (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003678
name: ellipsoid body (Drosophila)
def: "A doughnut shaped synaptic neuropil domain of the central complex of the adult brain that lies just anterior to the fan-shaped body. Its hole (the ellipsoid body canal) points anteriorly and has an axon tract (the anterior bundle) running through it. It is divided into concentric layers and into 16 radial segments, 8 per hemisphere, numbered 1-8 from superior medial to inferior medial." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem1.html, VFB_vol:00003678]
synonym: "EB" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "eb" RELATED []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045020 ! central body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003679
name: fan-shaped body (Drosophila)
def: "The largest synaptic neuropil domain of the adult central complex, covered by an extensive glial sheath. It is located posterior to the ellipsoid body. The fan-shaped body is a regular structure of 6-8 horizontal layers and 16 vertical slices (sometimes called staves, columns or segments), 8 per hemisphere numbered from medial to lateral - arranged in 4 closely associated pairs. Its inferior part is much narrower than its superior part, forming a fan shape. Fibers emerging from the basal-most area of the fan project to the noduli. Rostro-caudally, it can be divided into 4 shells on the basis of the extent and position of small field arborizations." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0205148, FlyBase:FBrf0210154, FlyBase:FBrf0212649, FlyBase:FBrf0213955, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/terms/terms.html]
synonym: "fan shaped body" EXACT []
synonym: "FB" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "fb" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045020 ! central body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003680
name: nodulus (Drosophila)
def: "Paired synaptic neuropil domain of the adult brain located just caudal to the ellipsoid body and ventral to the fan-shaped body, on either side of the midline. Its a glomerular structure composed of 4 subunits: three subunits are stacked as discs and the fourth subunit is posterior to these. There is asymmetry between the noduli, with one nodulus always lying slightly more anterior than the other." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem1.html]
synonym: "NO" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "no" EXACT []
synonym: "noduli" RELATED []
synonym: "ventral tubercle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003632 ! adult central complex

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003681
name: lateral accessory lobe (Drosophila)
def: "A bilaterally paired synaptic neuropil domain with a roughly pyramidal shape that is located inferior-lateral to the ellipsoid body and anterior-inferior to the bulb (lateral triangle). It lies behind the antennal lobe and in front of the ventral complex." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, VFB_vol:00003681]
synonym: "LAL" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "vbo" EXACT []
synonym: "ventral body" EXACT []
synonym: "vmpr" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007067 ! baso-central synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00040001 ! lateral complex (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003682
name: bulb (Drosophila)
def: "A bilaterally paired synaptic neuropil domain located lateral to the ellipsoid body and anterior lateral to the fan-shaped body. It contains many bulbous domains. It is formed primarily by the collateral arborizations of neuronal fibers that project to the ellipsoid body and by the terminals of the fibers projecting from the anterior optic tubercle and other neuropils." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, VFB_vol:00003682]
synonym: "BU" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "IST" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "isthmus" EXACT []
synonym: "lateral triangle" EXACT []
synonym: "ltr" RELATED []
synonym: "mimpr" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00040001 ! lateral complex (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003683
name: median bundle (Drosophila)
def: "Tract located in the anterior midline of the adult brain. It emerges as a paired tract from a broad area around the esophagus, merging into a single tract at the tip of the flange and terminates in the superior lateral protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem2.html, ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "mb" RELATED []
synonym: "MBDL" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "VAC1" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003684
name: adult mushroom body (Drosophila)
def: "Bilaterally paired neuropil structure situated postero-dorsally in the protocerebrum that functions in olfactory associative learning and memory. The mushroom body is divided into: the calyx, which is closest to the cortex and receives sensory interneuron afferents; the pedunculus, which is a thick axon bundle extending from the calyx to the base of the lobes; and the mushroom body lobe system, which consists of a vertical branch composed of two intertwined lobes (alpha and alpha') and a medial branch consisting of three parallel lobes (beta, beta' and gamma)." [FlyBase:FBrf0105215]
synonym: "corpora pedunculata" RELATED []
synonym: "MB" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: UBERON:0001058 ! mushroom body
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00011929 ! embryonic/larval mushroom body (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003685
name: mushroom body calyx (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain containing the dendrites of mushroom body intrinsic cells and receiving sensory interneuron afferents, mainly from the antennal lobes." [http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem3.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/terms/terms.html]
