[Term]
id: FBbt:00003740
name: T neuron T5d (Drosophila)
def: "T neuron T5 with a largely bleb-type terminal arborization in lobula plate layer 4. It is a glutamatergic neuron (Raghu and Borst, 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0213690]
synonym: "T5d" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10124]
is_a: FBbt:00003736 ! T neuron T5 (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100291 ! glutamatergic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003741
name: lamina wide-field cell (Drosophila)
def: "An intrinsic columnar neuron of the visual system whose cell body is located in the medulla cortex and that has a main projection that ascends via the first optic chiasm into the lamina where it is restricted to a single column for most of its length before making wide-field arborizations in the distal lamina. These neurons also arborize on the distal surface of the medulla in a circular field of about 20 columns. Several linking fibers from this arborization descend into M4 where they form a wide arborization field covering about 30-40 columns (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Morante and Desplan, 2008). In the lamina, it forms presynaptic terminals with photoreceptors R1-R3 and R6, lamina monopolar cells L1-L3 and L5, lamina amacrine neurons Lai, centrifugal neurons C2-C3 and columnar neuron T1. It also establishes connections with epithelial glial cells. It receives input from photoreceptor R1. Synaptic connections also exist between the different collaterals of Lawf in the lamina (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "Lawf" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10094]
synonym: "Lawf1" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007578 ! intrinsic columnar neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110137 ! wide-field columnar neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003708 ! lamina (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003742
name: centrifugal neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Columnar neuron whose soma lies in the cortex between the medulla and the lobula plate that extends through a single column of the medulla and lamina." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
is_a: FBbt:00007578 ! intrinsic columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003743
name: centrifugal neuron C2 (Drosophila)
def: "A centrifugal neuron with wide field arborizations in the medulla layers M1, M5, M8 and M10 and more restricted arborizations in the lamina (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). In the lamina it is presynaptic to lamina monopolar neuron L2 and lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells, and postsynaptic to photoreceptor R5, lamina lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and lamina wide-field cells Lawf (Meinertzhagen and O'Neil, 1991; Rivera-Alba et al., 2011). In the medulla, it is presynaptic to monopolar lamina neuron L2 and makes reciprocal synaptic connections with L1 in M1 (Takemura et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0054529, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "C2" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10079]
is_a: FBbt:00003742 ! centrifugal neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003744
name: centrifugal neuron C3 (Drosophila)
def: "A centrifugal wide-field neuron with wide field arborizations in the medulla layers M1-2, M5, and M8-10 and more restricted arborizations in the lamina (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). In the lamina it is presynaptic to photoreceptor R3, lamina monopolar neurons L1-L2, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and columnar neuron T1 (Meinertzhagen and O'Neil, 1991; Rivera-Alba et al., 2011; Morante and Desplan, 2008). It also establishes connections with epithelial glial cells. It forms postsynaptic terminals in the lamina (Morante and Desplan, 2008) with photoreceptor R3, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and lamina wide-field cells Lawf. In the medulla it is presynaptic to monopolar lamina neuron L2 and to T1, and postsynaptic to L1 (Takemura et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0054529, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "C3" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10080]
is_a: FBbt:00003742 ! centrifugal neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110137 ! wide-field columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003745
name: lamina tangential neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Tangential neuron of the optic lobe that projects and arborizes along the plane of one or more layers of the lamina." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Lat" RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000397 ! ganglion interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00001366 ! supraesophageal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007579 ! tangential neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003708 ! lamina (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003746
name: lamina intrinsic neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Intrinsic neuron of the lamina with arborizations spanning the proximal and distal lamina, whose cell body lies proximal to the lamina (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Meinertzhagen and Sorra, 2001). It has extensive arborizations forming presynaptic terminals with photoreceptors R2, R4 and R5, lamina monopolar cells L1-L5 (L4 collaterals from the same column), columnar neuron T1, centrifugal neurons C2 and C3 and epithelial glia. It receives input from photoreceptors R1-R6, lamina monopolar cell L4 (L4 collaterals from the same and adjacent columns), centrifugal neurons C2 and C3 and lamina wide-field cells Lawf. Connections are also present between branches of the same cell (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0159582, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "Am" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0159582]
synonym: "amacrine cell" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Lai" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
is_a: FBbt:00003745 ! lamina tangential neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003747
name: optic cartridge (Drosophila)
def: "Segment (column) of the lamina defined by the distal-proximal (eye to central brain) projections of photoreceptor cells of a single ommatidium." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "cartridge" RELATED []
synonym: "lamina cartridge" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00040069 ! synaptic neuropil segment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003708 ! lamina (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003748
name: medulla (Drosophila)
def: "The second optic neuropil, sandwiched between the lamina and the lobula complex. It is divided into 10 layers: layers 1-6 make up the outer medulla, and the seventh (or serpentine) layer exhibits a distinct architecture. Proximal to this, layers 8-10 make up the inner medulla." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/terms/terms.html, VFB_vol:00003748]
synonym: "m" RELATED []
synonym: "ME" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "optic medulla" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0212889]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006795 ! arthropod optic lobe

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003749
name: outer medulla (Drosophila)
def: "Layers 1-6 of the medulla." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045001 ! plexiform medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003750
name: medulla layer M1 (Drosophila)
def: "Distal-most layer of the medulla. It is defined by the distal extent of the distal lamina monopolar neuron L1 arborization (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "stratum M1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003751
name: medulla layer M2 (Drosophila)
def: "Second most lateral layer of the medulla. It is defined by the distal extent of the distal lamina monopolar neuron L2 arborization (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "L2 layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "layer M2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "medulla layer 2" EXACT []
synonym: "stratum M2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003752
name: medulla layer M3 (Drosophila)
def: "Third most lateral layer of the medulla. It is defined by the proximal border of the lamina monopolar neuron L2 arborization to that of the lamina neuron L3 terminal (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "L3 layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "medulla layer 3" EXACT []
synonym: "stratum M3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003753
name: medulla layer M4 (Drosophila)
def: "Fourth most lateral layer of the medulla. It corresponds to the narrow layer between the proximal end of lamina neuron L3 and the distal border of lamina neuron L1's proximal arborization (Takemura et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "L4 layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "medulla layer 4" EXACT []
synonym: "stratum M4" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003754
name: medulla layer M5 (Drosophila)
def: "Fifth most lateral layer of the medulla. It is defined by the lamina neuron L1's proximal arborization and contains the proximal lamina neuron L5 terminal (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "medulla layer 5" EXACT []
synonym: "proximal L1 layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "stratum M5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003755
name: medulla layer M6 (Drosophila)
def: "Sixth most lateral layer of the medulla, immediately lateral to the serpentine layer. It lies between the lamina neuron L1's arborization and the serpentine layer (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "medulla layer 6" EXACT []
synonym: "R7 layer" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "R7 recipient layer" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0209317]
synonym: "stratum M6" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003749 ! outer medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003756
name: serpentine layer (Drosophila)
def: "A major layer of extensive tangential fibers in the medulla, many of which project via the posterior optic commissure to the opposite medulla. It is the 7th most lateral layer of the medulla." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0065419, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "medulla layer 7" EXACT []
synonym: "medulla layer M7" RELATED []
synonym: "SPL" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040008 ! synaptic neuropil layer (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003748 ! medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003757
name: inner medulla (Drosophila)
def: "Layers 8-10 of the medulla." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "MEI" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00040008 ! synaptic neuropil layer (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003748 ! medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003758
name: medulla layer M8 (Drosophila)
def: "Lateral-most layer of the inner medulla, immediately medial to the serpentine layer." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "medulla layer 8" EXACT []
