def: "Medullary intrinsic neuron with fine, extensive and bushy arborizations in medulla layers M2, M8 and M9." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Mi12" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10100]
is_a: FBbt:00003775 ! medullary intrinsic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003788
name: transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)
def: "An intrinsic columnar neuron of the optic lobe whose cell body lies in the distal cortex of the medulla and that projects through the medulla and optic chiasm into the lobula. All neurons arborize in the lobula and most, but not all, in the medulla (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652]
synonym: "Tm neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007578 ! intrinsic columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003789
name: transmedullary neuron Tm1 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary narrow field neuron that terminates in lobula layer 1 with a bleb-type terminal arborization and that has fine arborizations in medulla layer M2 and bleb-type arborizations in M3 and M9 (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Takemura et al., 2011). In M2, it receives synaptic input from lamina monopolar neuron L2 (Takemura et al., 2011). It is a cholinergic neuron (Varija Raghu et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0212356, FlyBase:FBrf0217052]
synonym: "Tm1" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10132]
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013789 ! narrow field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003790
name: transmedullary neuron Tm2 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary narrow field neuron that terminates with bleb-type terminal arborizations in lobula layers 1 and 2. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layer M1 and M2, and has bleb-like arborizations in layers M3, M4 and M9 (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Takemura et al., 2011). In M2 it receives synaptic input from lamina monopolar cell L2 and in M4-M5 from L4. Each Tm2 neuron forms 3 connections with L4: one from the L4 in the parent column and two from L4 cells in two posterior columns (Takemura et al., 2011). It is a cholinergic neuron (Varija Raghu et al., 2011; Gao et al., 2008; Takemura et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0206213, FlyBase:FBrf0212356, FlyBase:FBrf0217052]
synonym: "Tm2" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10144]
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013789 ! narrow field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003791
name: transmedullary neuron Tm3a (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary narrow field neuron that terminates in lobula layers 1 and 4 with bleb-like terminal arborizations. It has fine arborizations in medulla layers M1, M4, and M5, and has bleb-type arborization in medulla layers M1, M4, M9 and M10 (Morante and Desplan, 2008; Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). It is a GABAergic neuron." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0213020, FlyBase:FBrf0220286]
synonym: "Tm3" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBrain_NDB:10153]
synonym: "Tm3a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "transmedullary neuron Tm3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
is_a: CL:0011005 ! GABAergic interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00007228 ! GABAergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013789 ! narrow field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003792
name: transmedullary neuron Tm4 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary narrow field neuron that terminates in lobula layers 1, 2 and 4 with bleb-type arborizations, and with fine arborizations in layer 3. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M2, M3, M4 and M9, and has bleb-type arborizations in layers M2, M4, and M9 (Morante and Desplan, 2008; Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). It seems to be capable of both cholinergic and GABAergic neurotransmission." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0212356, FlyBase:FBrf0220286]
synonym: "Tm4" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10155]
is_a: CL:0011005 ! GABAergic interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007228 ! GABAergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013789 ! narrow field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003793
name: transmedullary neuron Tm5 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary neuron that terminates in lobula layers 4 and 5 with bleb-type arborizations. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M3, M4, M5, M6, M8 and the serpentine layer, and has bleb-type terminals in layers M6 and M8. It is postsynaptic to distal medullary amacrine neuron Dm8a in medulla layer M6 (Gao et al., 2008). It is a GABAergic neuron." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0206213, FlyBase:FBrf0220286]
synonym: "Tm5" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10157]
is_a: CL:0011005 ! GABAergic interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00003788 ! transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007228 ! GABAergic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003794
name: transmedullary neuron Tm6 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary neuron that terminates in lobula layer 4 with bleb-type arborizations. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M1, M2, M3, M8 and M9, and has bleb-type arborizations in layers M1, M2, M8 and M9." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Tm6" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10160]
is_a: FBbt:00003788 ! transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003795
name: transmedullary neuron Tm7 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary wide-field neuron that terminates in lobula layer 5 with both fine and bleb-type arborizations. It has fine arborizations in medulla layers M3, M4, M6 and M8, and bleb-type arborizations in layer M6 (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Morante and Desplan, 2008). It is a cholinergic neuron (Varija Raghu et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0212356]
synonym: "Tm7" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10161]
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013788 ! wide field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003796
name: transmedullary neuron Tm8 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary wide-field neuron that terminates in lobula layers 5 and 6 with bleb-type arborizations. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M4, M6, M8 and M9, and has bleb-type arborizations in layers M4 and M8 (Morante and Desplan, 2008; Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). It is a cholinergic neuron (Varija Raghu et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0212356]
synonym: "Tm8" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10162]
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00013788 ! wide field transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003797
name: transmedullary neuron Tm9 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary narrow field neuron that terminates in lobula layer 1 with bleb-type arborizations. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M2 and M3, and has bleb-type arborizations in layers M3 and M4. It receives synaptic contacts from photoreceptor cell R8, laminar cell L3 and Dm8a (in M4) (Gao et al., 2008). It is a GABAergic neuron." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0206213, FlyBase:FBrf0220286]
synonym: "Tm9" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10163]
