def: "Transmedullary neuron that terminates in lobula layer 6 with both fine and bleb-type arborizations, and bleb-type arborizations in layers 4 and 5. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M2, M3, M8 and M10, and has bleb-type arborizations in layer M3." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Tm19" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10142]
is_a: FBbt:00003788 ! transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00003808
name: transmedullary neuron Tm20 (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary wide-field neuron that terminates in lobula layer 5 with bleb-type arborizations. It displays fine arborizations in medulla layers M1, M2, M3 and M8, and has bleb-type arborizations in layers M3 and M8 (Morante and Desplan, 2008; Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652]
synonym: "Tm20" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10145]
