[Term]
id: FBbt:00004043
name: adult maxillary nerve (Drosophila)
def: "The adult maxillary nerve is a mixed sensory-motor nerve of the gnathal ganglion (GNG). It ~120 axons contains axons from the sensory cells of the maxillary appendages entering the maxillary neuromere of the GNG and GNG motor axons to maxillary musculature. The maxillary nerve is fused with the labial nerve and for much of its length, forming the maxillary-labial nerve." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0042883, FlyBase:FBrf0080339, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "maxillary labellar nerve" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "maxillary labial nerve" RELATED [FBC:FlyBase]
