[Term]
id: FBbt:00004048
name: stomodeal nerve (Drosophila)
def: "Nerve arising from the corpus cardiacum (Rajashekhar and Singh, 1994), located along the dorsal surface of the esophagus. After it exits from the esophageal canal it loops ventrally and anastomoses with the pharyngeal nerve to form the recurrent nerve (Rajashekhar and Singh, 1994)." [FlyBase:FBrf0080339]
synonym: "recurrent nerve" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
is_a: UBERON:0011215 ! central nervous system cell part cluster
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004047 ! stomodeal ganglion (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004049
name: cardia nerve (Drosophila)
def: "Nerve that connects the stomodeal ganglion to the cardial valve of the adult proventriculus (cardia)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
