[Term]
id: FBbt:00004059
name: mesothoracic neuromere (Drosophila)
def: "Any neuromere (FBbt:00005140) that is part of some mesothoracic segment (FBbt:00000018)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00111026 ! thoracic neuromere (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6000018 ! mesothoracic segment

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004060
name: anterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve (Drosophila)
def: "The largest and anterior-most of the two dorsal mesothoracic nerves. It extends dorso-anteriorly from the thoracico-abdominal ganglion and then dorso-laterally, bending around the anterior face of the anterior tergosternal muscles before splitting into branches that innervate the lateral muscles near the body wall, beneath the base of the wing. It also sends a branch between the tergosternal muscles. The fine sensory fibers of this nerve project along with a smaller number of coarse motor fibers, dorsally between various muscle groups. The sensory fibers extend into the wing where they innervate various sensory organs." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003021 ! adult mesothoracic segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003559 ! adult nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004061
name: posterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve (Drosophila)
def: "A nerve that arises from the thoracico-abdominal ganglion, just posterior to the root of the anterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve. It projects posteriolaterally before branching, with one branch innervating the tergal depressor of the trochanter (muscle 66), while the other branch forms further, terminal branches that innervate targets including the dorsal medial muscle (dorsal longitudinal muscle (FBbt:00003362))." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003021 ! adult mesothoracic segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003559 ! adult nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004062
name: accessory mesothoracic nerve (Drosophila)
def: "A nerve that arises from the lateroposterior side of the mesothoracic neuromere at a point in front of the origin of the haltere nerve. It extends posteriorly and slightly dorsally and laterally around the anterior wings of the mesofurca, before branching, with one branch innervating furcoentopleural muscles (= muscles 59 and 60 ?) and another innervating laterally placed vertical tubular muscles close to the anterior of the halteres (muscle 87?)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003021 ! adult mesothoracic segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003559 ! adult nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004063
name: mesothoracic leg nerve (Drosophila)
def: "A nerve that arises from a ventral protuberance on the adult mesothoracic neuromere. It splits at its base, with a small number of fibers innervating a ventral tubular muscle, posterior-lateral to the tergal depressor of the trochanter and the rest projecting into the mesothoracic leg." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
synonym: "ventral mesothoracic nerve" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003021 ! adult mesothoracic segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003559 ! adult nervous system

