is_a: UBERON:0002268 ! olfactory organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004176
name: small sensillum basiconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)
def: "Small olfactory basiconic sensillum on antennal segment 3. The surface of the sensillum is perforated by longitudinal rows of pores, connecting to a lymph space innervated by 2 branched olfactory receptor neuron dendrites." [FlyBase:FBrf0104820, FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: FBbt:00004174 ! sensillum basiconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00005186 ! small sensillum basiconicum (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0002268 ! olfactory organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004177
name: sensillum coeloconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)
def: "Olfactory sensillum coeloconicum that is part of antennal segment 3. A short conical peg arising from a broad basal platform, basally smooth but distally having deep longitudinal grooves. The peg has a double cuticular wall. The inner wall encloses a central lumen innervated by olfactory receptor neuron dendrites. Distally, the central lumen is connected to the outer, sensillum lymph-filled chamber by radial spoke channels." [FlyBase:FBrf0104820, FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: FBbt:00004172 ! antennal segment 3 sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00005190 ! sensillum coeloconicum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007241 ! adult head sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0002268 ! olfactory organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004178
name: Johnston organ (Drosophila)
def: "Compound chordotonal organ of antennal segment 2 involved in hearing (Gopfert and Robert, 2002), direction-sensitive wind detection (Yorozu et al., 2009) and gravitaxis (Kamikouchi et al., 2009). The actin-filament rich basal tips of the Johnston's organ scolopidia connect to the inner surface of antennal segment 2, and the apical tips connect to the hook of antennal segment 3 (Gopfert and Robert, 2002). Its sensory neurons (Johnston's organ neurons or JONs) are connected to the Johnston's organ nerve (Kamikouchi et al., 2006), and predominantly innervate the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). There are 477 +/- 24 cell bodies, arranged in a bowl shape lying vertically with the 'top' facing the lateral side, and forming a ring around the antennal nerve (Kamikouchi et al., 2006). JONs connecting to opposing sides of the hook are alternatively stimulated by stretching or compression according to the hook's oscillatory movement (Gopfert and Robert, 2002)." [FlyBase:FBrf0147122, FlyBase:FBrf0166419, FlyBase:FBrf0179481, FlyBase:FBrf0187921, FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "chordotonal organ of antennal segment 2" RELATED []
synonym: "JO" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0210248]
synonym: "Johnston's organ" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005377 ! antennal segment 2 sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007234 ! compound sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007686 ! auditory sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0001038 ! chordotonal organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004179
name: sacculus (Drosophila)
def: "A three-chambered pit organ on antennal segment 3 that contains many sensilla. It extends ventrodorsally, with an opening to the posterior side of the antennal segment (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
is_a: FBbt:00004172 ! antennal segment 3 sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007235 ! external compound sense organ (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110819 ! presumptive sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004180
name: grooved sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of chamber III of the sacculus of the antenna. The sensilla are double-walled and bear alternating longitudinal grooves and ridges for three-quarters of their length from the tip. They are innervated by two sensory neurons (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "GS" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "sensillum coeloconicum of sacculus" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005191 ! grooved sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110027 ! sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110026 ! chamber III of sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004181
name: grooved sensillum 1 (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of the ventral compartment of chamber III of the sacculus of the antenna. The sensilla are thick, blunt-tipped and bear 9-12 grooves with slit channels (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "blunt-tipped grooved sensilla" BROAD []
synonym: "GS1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
is_a: FBbt:00004180 ! grooved sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004182
name: grooved sensillum 2 (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of the dorsal compartment of chamber III of the sacculus of the antenna. The sensilla are slender than the grooved sensillum 1 and bear 6-8 grooves with slit channels (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "GS2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "slender grooved sensilla" BROAD []
is_a: FBbt:00004180 ! grooved sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004183
name: blunt-tipped sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of chamber II of the sacculus of the antenna. The sensilla are blunt-tipped with a smooth cuticular surface and have a pore-like structure at their distal end. They are innervated by three sensory cells (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "no-pore sensilla coeloconica" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "np-Sc" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005192 ! blunt-tipped sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110027 ! sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110025 ! chamber II of sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004184
name: basiconic sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of chamber I of the sacculus of the antenna. The sensilla are devoid of pores, have no socket at the base and gradually taper at the distal end. The sensilla have an irregularly sculpted external surface at their distal end. They are innervated by two or three sensory cells (Shanbhag et al., 1995)." [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "no-pore sensilla basiconica" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
synonym: "np-SB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084361]
is_a: FBbt:00004174 ! sensillum basiconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110027 ! sensillum of sacculus (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110024 ! chamber I of sacculus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004185
name: aristal sensillum (Drosophila)
def: "Sensillum of the arista. There are three of these per arista, each consisting of a pair of sensory neurons surrounded by 2 sheath cells. They project into the lymph space of the arista core, where they float freely - unattached to the epidermis. These projections consist of specialised dendrites surrounded throughout their length by sheath cells and distally by an electron dense dendritic sheath. The three projections terminate at different points along the shaft." [FlyBase:FBrf0049408, FlyBase:FBrf0088919]
synonym: "aristal sense organ" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007151 ! adult antennal sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007241 ! adult head sensillum (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6004519 ! arista

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004186
name: neuron of aristal sensillum (Drosophila)
def: "Sensory neuron of aristal sensillum. Each sensillum contains a pair of sensory dendrites. The outer segment of these dendrites is encased in an electron-dense dendritic sheath and each of the pair has a distinct morphology: one is short and cylindrical proximally, but flattened distally; the other is larger and has a plasma membrane that form 2 interdigitating spiral whorls of lamellae and has periodically arranged electron dense particles protruding from the plasma membrane into the extracellular space (Foelix et al., 1989). The inner-segments of these dendrites are delimited from the outer segments by a ciliary region and are rich in vesicles, mitochondria and ribosomes. The somata sit in a small ganglion near the base of the arista. The axons project via the aristal nerve, which merges with the antennal nerve, and innervate glomeruli VP2 and/or VP3 of the adult antennal lobe. (Stocker et al., 1983)." [FlyBase:FBrf0039019, FlyBase:FBrf0051437, FlyBase:FBrf0137012]
synonym: "neuron of aristal sense organ" RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000101 ! sensory neuron
is_a: FBbt:00005163 ! sensory organ cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004185 ! aristal sensillum (Drosophila)

