[Term]
id: FBbt:00004215
name: photoreceptor cell R2 (Drosophila)
def: "Outer photoreceptor cell of the adult eye whose rhabdomere is located in the middle of the longer of the two parallel sides of the trapezoid of rhabdomeres in each ommatidium. It has a single axon that projects along a single lamina optic cartridge (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Wolff and Ready, 1993) within which it makes extensive presynaptic connections with the lamina monopolar cells L1-L3, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and columnar neuron T1, before terminating in the proximal lamina. It also establishes connections with epithelial and surface glial cells The photoreceptor R2 receives input from L2, L4 (collaterals from adjacent columns), lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and lamina wide-field neurons Lawf (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0064798, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "lamina receptor cell R2" EXACT []
synonym: "receptor cell R2" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006007 ! outer photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004216
name: rhabdomere R2 (Drosophila)
def: "Any rhabdomere (FBbt:00004212) that is part of some photoreceptor cell R2 (FBbt:00004215)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00007455 ! rhabdomere of eye photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004215 ! photoreceptor cell R2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004217
name: photoreceptor cell R3 (Drosophila)
def: "Outer photoreceptor cell of the adult eye whose rhabdomere is located at the non-right angled vertex of the longer of two parallel sides of the trapezoid of rhabdomeres in each ommatidium. It has a single axon that projects along a single lamina optic cartridge (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Wolff and Ready, 1993) within which it makes extensive presynaptic connections with the lamina monopolar cells L1-L3, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells, columnar neuron T1 and centrifugal neuron C3, before terminating in the proximal lamina. It also establishes connections with epithelial glial cells. The photoreceptor R3 receives input from L4 (collaterals from adjacent columns), centrifugal neuron C3 and lamina wide-field neurons Lawf (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0064798, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "lamina receptor cell R3" EXACT []
synonym: "receptor cell R3" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006007 ! outer photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004218
name: rhabdomere R3 (Drosophila)
def: "Any rhabdomere (FBbt:00004212) that is part of some photoreceptor cell R3 (FBbt:00004217)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00007455 ! rhabdomere of eye photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004217 ! photoreceptor cell R3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004219
name: photoreceptor cell R4 (Drosophila)
def: "Outer photoreceptor cell of the adult eye whose rhabdomere is located in the middle of the longer of the two non-parallel sides of trapezoid of rhabdomeres in each ommatidium, in between the rhabdomeres of R3 and R5. It has a single axon that projects along a single lamina optic cartridge (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Wolff and Ready, 1993) within which it makes extensive presynaptic connections with the lamina monopolar cells L1-L3, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and columnar neuron T1, before terminating in the proximal lamina. It also establishes connections with epithelial glial cells. The photoreceptor R4 receives input from L4 (collaterals from adjacent columns) and lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0064798, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "lamina receptor cell R4" EXACT []
synonym: "receptor cell R4" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006007 ! outer photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004220
name: rhabdomere R4 (Drosophila)
def: "Any rhabdomere (FBbt:00004212) that is part of some photoreceptor cell R4 (FBbt:00004219)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00007455 ! rhabdomere of eye photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004219 ! photoreceptor cell R4 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004221
name: photoreceptor cell R5 (Drosophila)
def: "Outer photoreceptor cell of the adult eye whose rhabdomere is located at a non-right angle vertex of the shorter of the two parallel sides of the trapezoid of rhabdomeres in each ommatidium. It has a single axon that projects along a single lamina optic cartridge (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Wolff and Ready, 1993) within which it makes extensive presynaptic connections with the lamina monopolar cells L1-L3, lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells and centrifugal neuron C2, before terminating in the proximal lamina. It also establishes connections with epithelial and marginal glial cells. The photoreceptor R5 receives input from L4 (collaterals from the same and adjacent columns) and lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0064798, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "lamina receptor cell R5" EXACT []
synonym: "receptor cell R5" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006007 ! outer photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004222
name: rhabdomere R5 (Drosophila)
def: "Any rhabdomere (FBbt:00004212) that is part of some photoreceptor cell R5 (FBbt:00004221)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00007455 ! rhabdomere of eye photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004221 ! photoreceptor cell R5 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004223
name: photoreceptor cell R6 (Drosophila)
def: "Outer photoreceptor cell of the adult eye whose rhabdomere is located at the right angle vertex of the shorter of the two parallel sides of the trapezoid of rhabdomeres in each ommatidium. It has a single axon that projects along a single lamina optic cartridge (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989; Wolff and Ready, 1993) within which it makes extensive presynaptic connections with the lamina monopolar cells L1-L4 (L4 collaterals from adjacent columns) and lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells, before terminating in the proximal lamina. It also establishes connections with epithelial and marginal glial cells. The photoreceptor R6 receives input from L4 (L4 collaterals from adjacent columns) and lamina wide-field neurons Lawf (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0064798, FlyBase:FBrf0216925]
synonym: "lamina receptor cell R6" EXACT []
synonym: "receptor cell R6" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006007 ! outer photoreceptor cell (Drosophila)

