[Term]
id: FBbt:00004229
name: mystery cell (Drosophila)
def: "Epithelial cell that is part of early ommatidial preclusters but which, unlike the rest of the cells in the precluster, rejoins the surrounding undifferentiated tissue of the eye disc. Mystery cells are usually located between putative R3 and R4 cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
is_a: FBbt:00007108 ! imaginal disc epithelial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007144 ! early ommatidial precursor cluster (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004231
name: primary pigment cell (Drosophila)
def: "Retinal pigment cell that is part of an ommatidium. Each ommatidium has two primary pigment cells. These cells line the pseudocone and are in contact basally with the cone cells. They contain coarse granules of ommochrome screening pigment. Along with the cone cells, they secrete the lens." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
is_a: FBbt:00007371 ! retinal pigment cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007370 ! primary pigment cell precursor (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000971 ! ommatidium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004232
name: secondary pigment cell (Drosophila)
def: "Inter-ommatidial pigment cell that lies between the edges of adjacent ommatidia. It contains the red screening pigment pteridine, as well as ommochrome granules." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
is_a: FBbt:00007250 ! inter-ommatidial cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007371 ! retinal pigment cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004233
name: tertiary pigment cell (Drosophila)
def: "Inter-ommatidial pigment cell that lies between the vertices of adjacent ommatidia. Except at the margins of the eye, vertices alternate between those with tertiary pigment cells and those with bristles. Vertices at the margins all have tertiary pigment cells. These cells contain the red screening pigment pteridine, as well as ommochrome granules." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
is_a: FBbt:00007250 ! inter-ommatidial cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007371 ! retinal pigment cell (Drosophila)

