is_a: UBERON:6007288 ! insect integumentary specialisation
relationship: part_of UBERON:6005396 ! adult integumentary system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004483
name: ptilinum (Drosophila)
def: "Membranous sac that is part of the front of the head capsule. It is everted at eclosion and serves to break open the operculum at the end of the puparium. Following eclosion, it is withdrawn into the head where it collapses and becomes sclerotized, externally leaving the ptilinal suture." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007284 ! insect region of integument
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110832 ! presumptive ptilinum (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004484
name: ptilinal suture (Drosophila)
def: "Suture across the front of the head, in between the eyes and just dorsal to the base of the antennae. It is a remnant of the internalization of the ptilinum after eclosion." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00004479 ! suture (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004483 ! ptilinum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004485
name: fronto-orbital plate (Drosophila)
def: "Integument of the anterior adult head which is located in between the postfrons and the eye." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004486
name: fronto-orbital suture (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00004479 ! suture (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004487
name: antennal foramen (Drosophila)
def: "Foramen of the adult head in which the antenna is articulated. There are two of these." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00004478 ! foramen (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004488
name: frons (Drosophila)
def: "An anterior part of the head capsule between the vertex and the clypeus, bounded laterally by the frontal suture and bearing a median ocellus." [FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004489
name: prefrons (Drosophila)
def: "Integument that covers the anterior head capsule ventral to the ptilinum." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
synonym: "facial carina" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0045560]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004488 ! frons (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004490
name: postfrons (Drosophila)
def: "Integument that covers the anterior head capsule, in between the ptilinum and the ocelli." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004488 ! frons (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004491
name: gena (Drosophila)
def: "The bilateral part of the head capsule below the eyes, delimited by the occipital suture behind and the mouthparts below." [FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
synonym: "cheek" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004493
name: paraocciput (Drosophila)
def: "Ventral area of the occiput sclerite of the adult head." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003155 ! arthropod occiput

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004494
name: postocciput (Drosophila)
def: "Narrow sclerotized area immediately surrounding the dorsal and lateral margins of the occipital foramen." [ISBN:978-0-521-57890-5]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003155 ! arthropod occiput

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004495
name: ocellar triangle (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the integument of the dorsal postfrons in the adult head where the ocelli are located. The cuticle is smooth, in contrast to the rest of the postfrons." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004490 ! postfrons (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004496
name: postgena (Drosophila)
def: "A posterior region of the head capsule behind the gena." [FBC:gg]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004497
name: premandibular suture (Drosophila)
def: "Suture of the posterior adult head that is on the border between the postgena and the occiput." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
synonym: "premandibular sulcus" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00004479 ! suture (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110846 ! presumptive premandibular suture (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6004481 ! adult external head

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004498
name: rostral membrane (Drosophila)
def: "Integument which covers the basiproboscis, extending dorsally to the occipital foramen. It is covered with grouped hairs, with the distal rostral sensilla located near its ventral edge, at the insertion of the maxillary palpus." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004499
name: occipital foramen (Drosophila)
def: "Foramen of the adult head with which the neck articulates." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: FBbt:00004478 ! foramen (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004500
name: adult tentorium (Drosophila)
def: "Internal sclerite of the adult head, ventral to the occipital foramen. On each side, it is fused with the head wall for some distance, and then becomes free, extending down to the anterior tentorial pit. It is formed by inward growths of the epidermis. The tentorium provides many of the apodemes for cervical muscles, called tentorial pits." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0093677]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003153 ! head capsule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004501
name: tentorial pit (Drosophila)
def: "Paired depression of the head capsule corresponding to an articulation of the tentorial bar (arm). There is an anterior and posterior tentorial pit." [FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: UBERON:0004905 ! articulation
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004500 ! adult tentorium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004502
name: anterior tentorial pit (Drosophila)
def: "Lateral paired tentorial pit ventral to the eye, at the boundary between the head capsule and the mouthparts." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: FBbt:00004501 ! tentorial pit (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004503
name: posterior tentorial pit (Drosophila)
def: "Paired tentorial pit at the back of the head capsule, at the boundary between the post-gena and the tentorial bridge." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
is_a: FBbt:00004501 ! tentorial pit (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004504
name: posterior tentorial bar (Drosophila)
def: "Bar across the ventral base of the occipital foramen." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:6007288 ! insect integumentary specialisation
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004500 ! adult tentorium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004509
name: eye equator (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000018 ! compound eye

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004513
name: first segment of antenna (Drosophila)
def: "Proximal-most segment of the antenna. It is a narrow ring which bears on its dorsal side a medial group of four and a single lateral bristle. Its pigmentation and hair pattern are similar to those of the prefrons." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
synonym: "antennal segment 1" EXACT []
synonym: "scape" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007149 ! segment of antenna
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110812 ! presumptive first segment of antenna (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004514
name: second segment of antenna (Drosophila)
def: "Second segment of the antenna located ventrolaterally to the first segment. It is larger than the first segment and somewhat swollen. It has on average 25 bristles of various sizes. The Johnston's organ is contained in this segment." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
synonym: "antennal segment 2" EXACT []
synonym: "pedicel" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007149 ! segment of antenna
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110813 ! presumptive second segment of antenna (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004515
name: third segment of antenna (Drosophila)
def: "Largest segment of the antenna. It is bulbous, light grey in colour and it bears numerous hairs and sensilla, including sensilla trichoidea, basiconica, intermedia and coeloconica. It has an articulated joint with the second segment of the antenna. It contains the sacculus." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
synonym: "antennal segment 3" EXACT []
synonym: "flugellum" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "funiculus" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007149 ! segment of antenna
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110814 ! presumptive third segment of antenna (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004516
name: fourth segment of antenna (Drosophila)
def: "A small ring at the base of the 5th segment, where it attaches to the 3rd segment." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "antennal segment 4" RELATED []
synonym: "flugellum" BROAD []
is_a: UBERON:6007149 ! segment of antenna

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004517
name: fifth segment of antenna (Drosophila)
def: "Segment of the antenna at the base of the arista." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "antennal segment 5" RELATED []
synonym: "flugellum" BROAD []
is_a: UBERON:6007149 ! segment of antenna

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004518
name: basal cylinder (Drosophila)
synonym: "antennal segment 4+5 of Ferris" RELATED []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004517 ! fifth segment of antenna (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004523
name: anterior labial plate (Drosophila)
def: "Elongated plate of variable sclerotization in the dorsal or anterior surface of the mediproboscis, distal to the labrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110712 ! presumptive anterior labial plate (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005905 ! insect labrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004524
name: discal sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Horse-shoe shaped sclerite on the distal end of the labrum, bordering the oral opening." [FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
synonym: "horse-shoe sclerite" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
synonym: "horseshoe sclerite" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110711 ! presumptive discal sclerite (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005905 ! insect labrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004525
name: prestomal cavity (Drosophila)
def: "Oral opening at the distal end of the labrum, which is surrounded by the discal sclerite." [FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
synonym: "prestomal aperture" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
is_a: UBERON:0000464 ! anatomical space
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005905 ! insect labrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004526
name: adult cibarium (Drosophila)
def: "The proximal portion of the adult pharynx, which functions as a sucking pump. It consists of two arched sclerotized plates. The posterior plate is fixed in position by its connections with the clypeus. The anterior plate fits against the concave side of the posterior plate and bears a ridge shaped apodeme (apodemal carina) that is attached to large dilator muscles that attach to clypeus. Their contraction pulls the anterior plate forward, enlarging the cibarial lumen and thus producing suction." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
synonym: "adult atrium" EXACT []
relationship: develops_from UBERON:6001765 ! clypeo-labral disc
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003128 ! adult pharynx (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004527
name: cibarial plate (Drosophila)
def: "One of the two sclerotized plates of the cibarium." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004526 ! adult cibarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004528
name: anterior plate of cibarium (Drosophila)
def: "Mobile, arched, sclerotized plate on the anterior side of the cibarium. It bears a ridge shaped apodeme (apodemal carina) that is attached to large dilator muscles that attach to clypeus." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
is_a: FBbt:00004527 ! cibarial plate (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004529
name: posterior plate of cibarium (Drosophila)
def: "Fixed, arched, sclerotized plate on the posterior side of the cibarium. It is attached to the clypeus." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
is_a: FBbt:00004527 ! cibarial plate (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004531
name: labellum (Drosophila)
def: "The broadened, cushion-like, apical part of the rostral mouth parts. It consists of two regions; its lateral surface has a hemispherical, on which there are approximately 33-34 gustatory (chemosensory) and two mechanosensory bristles. The gustatory bristles are arranged into three ill-defined rows of 10-11 bristles: two medial and one located peripherally. The mechanosensory bristles are located in the most dorsolateral area of the labella surface and are shorter than the gustatory sensilla. The inner (medial) surface bears a series of open collecting channels, the pseudotrachea, that converge medially and conduct food to the tip of the labrum. Taste pegs are present in between the pseudotrachea, with 30-40 on each side." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0074012, FlyBase:FBrf0137194, FlyBase:FBrf0166419, FlyBase:FBrf0211916]
synonym: "labial palpus" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007288 ! insect integumentary specialisation
relationship: develops_from UBERON:6001764 ! labial disc
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004542 ! distiproboscis (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004533
name: labellar cap (Drosophila)
def: "Chitinous dorsal half of the labellum which is covered in bristles." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110709 ! presumptive labellar cap (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004531 ! labellum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004534
name: prementum (Drosophila)
def: "Rectangular sclerotized plate which is present in the posterior region of the mediproboscis. It contains about 11 large bristles placed in a characteristic pattern." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
synonym: "theca" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0033866]
is_a: UBERON:6004475 ! sclerite
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110710 ! presumptive prementum (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004531 ! labellum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004536
name: lacinia (Drosophila)
def: "Paired inner lobate structures sitting on the apical margin near the base of the maxillary palps. A component of the proboscis." [FBC:gg, FlyBase:FBim0000788, FlyBase:FBim0000834, FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
relationship: part_of UBERON:6004520 ! mouthpart

