[Term]
id: FBbt:00004807
name: Wheeler's organ (Drosophila)
def: "A chordotonal organ associated with the anterior of abdominal sternite 2. It is visible externally as a raised patch of smooth cuticle without trichomes or bristles. It consists of two clusters of scolopidia (FBbt:00005217), one on either side of the ventral midline (Smith and Shepherd, 1996). The sensory neurons of Wheeler's organ project through the second segmental nerve of the abdomen and then through the abdominal neuromeres via dorso-lateral tract of the ventral fasciculus (DLV), to terminate in the prothoracic neuromere (Smith and Shepherd, 1996)." [FlyBase:FBrf0032262, FlyBase:FBrf0042053, FlyBase:FBrf0085956]
is_a: FBbt:00004113 ! adult sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0001038 ! chordotonal organ
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004800 ! abdominal sternite 2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004814
name: adult abdominal spiracle (Drosophila)
def: "A spiracle of the adult abdomen. There are 7 pairs of these, in segments A1-7. Each has a rigid circular rim and the opening leads to a tubular atrium lined by inward projecting circular lamellae. Where the atrium joins the trachea, the passage is constricted by a deep fold in the anterior wall which can be closed by the action of an associated spiracular occlusor muscle (FBbt:00013334)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734, FlyBase:FBrf0034081]
is_a: FBbt:00003120 ! adult spiracle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003024 ! adult abdominal segment

