[Term]
id: FBbt:00004860
name: germline cell (Drosophila)
synonym: "germ cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00007002 ! cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004862
name: fusome (Drosophila)
def: "Cytoplasmic membrane-rich zones found in developing germline stem cells and their progeny. A small spherical fusome (spectrosome) grows during germline stem cell formation into a large branched structure (polyfusome) that extends through the ring canals into every cystocyte in germarium region 2a. Once the germline cyst has stopped dividing, the fusome begins to break down, usually disappearing soon after the progeny of the germline stem cell leaves the germarium." [FlyBase:FBrf0103408]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000991 ! gonad

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004863
name: polyfusome (Drosophila)
def: "A gelatinous mass assembled by the fusion of the adjacent fusomes formed at consecutive cystocyte divisions in Drosophila, resulting in a large branched structure." [FlyBase:FBrf0049530, ISBN:978-0-19-514324-9]
is_a: FBbt:00004862 ! fusome (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005411 ! spectrosome (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004866
name: germarium (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior region of the ovariole, that is connected to posterior egg chambers." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004893 ! ovariole (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004867
name: germarium region 1 (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior region of the germarium where cysts start developing." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004868
name: germarium cap cell (Drosophila)
def: "Somatic cell found posterior to the terminal filament. There is a group of 2-6 cells which are usually positioned asymmetrically on one side of the germarium tip, capping the underlying germ line stem cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0087119]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004867 ! germarium region 1 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004869
name: germarium region 2 (Drosophila)
def: "Large middle portion of the germarium that contains 16-cell cysts." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004870
name: germarium region 2a (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior region of germarium region 2. Cysts in this region have not been fully enclosed by follicle cells, and directly contact neighboring cysts." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004867 ! germarium region 1 (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004869 ! germarium region 2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004871
name: germarium region 2b (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior region of germarium region 2. Individual cysts in this region have been fully separated by inwardly migrating follicle cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004870 ! germarium region 2a (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004869 ! germarium region 2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004872
name: germarium region 3 (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior region of the germarium. It is where stage 1 egg chambers are found, before they separate from the germarium." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004871 ! germarium region 2b (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004874
name: oogonial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Female germline stem cell. Each division of an oogonial cell gives rise to one cystoblast and one female germline stem cell." [FlyBase:FBrf0017959]
is_a: CL:0000025 ! egg cell
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004875
name: germline cyst (Drosophila)
def: "A developing unit of gametogenesis consisting of germline cells encapsulated by a layer of somatic cells." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004876
name: cystoblast (Drosophila)
def: "Female germline cell which is the daughter of a female germline stem cell. It is found in region 1 of the germarium. It divides four times to give rise to 16 daughter cystocytes, which together form a germline cyst. Division is through a cleavage-like process, with the daughter cells being smaller than the parent cystoblast." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: FBbt:00004874 ! oogonial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from CL:0000088 ! female germ line stem cell (sensu Nematoda and Protostomia)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004877
name: cystocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Female germline cell born during one of four rounds of cell division following the birth of a cystoblast from a female germline stem cell until the point where one of the resulting 16 cells (the presumptive oocyte) enters meiosis. Cystocytes are interconnected by ring canals. The oocyte develops from one of two cystocytes that contain 4 ring canals, the other 15 cystocytes differentiate as nurse cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0021038, FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
synonym: "cyst cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: FBbt:00004874 ! oogonial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004876 ! cystoblast (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004879
name: nurse cell ring canal (Drosophila)
def: "Cytoplasmic bridge that connects a nurse cell to other nurse cells or oocyte." [FlyBase:FBrf0016305]
is_a: FBbt:00005409 ! ring canal (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007137 ! female germline cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004880
name: nurse cell ring canal rim (Drosophila)
def: "The outer edge of a nurse cell ring canal." [FlyBase:FBrf0016305]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004879 ! nurse cell ring canal (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004881
name: inner nurse cell ring canal rim (Drosophila)
def: "Electron dense inner rim of a nurse cell ring canal." [FlyBase:FBrf0016305]
is_a: FBbt:00004880 ! nurse cell ring canal rim (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004882
name: outer nurse cell ring canal rim (Drosophila)
def: "Electron opaque outer rim of a nurse cell ring canal." [FlyBase:FBrf0016305]
is_a: FBbt:00004880 ! nurse cell ring canal rim (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004883
name: nurse cell spectrosome (Drosophila)
def: "Spherical fusome found in the cystocytes that will develop as nurse cells." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00005411 ! spectrosome (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of CL:0000026 ! invertebrate nurse cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004884
name: nurse cell fusome (Drosophila)
def: "A tube-shaped gelatinous mass that extends through each ring canal formed during the cycle of cystocyte divisions." [FlyBase:FBrf0073745, ISBN:978-0-19-514324-9]
is_a: FBbt:00007140 ! female fusome (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of CL:0000026 ! invertebrate nurse cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004887
name: endobody (Drosophila)
def: "Spherical structure associated with the karyosome of the oocyte." [FlyBase:FBrf0034074, FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004888 ! oocyte nucleus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004888
name: oocyte nucleus (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004889
name: karyosome (Drosophila)
def: "The condensed chromosomes of an oocyte." [FlyBase:FBrf0034074, FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004888 ! oocyte nucleus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004891
name: pole plasm (Drosophila)
def: "Specialized region of the female egg cytoplasm characterized by the presence of dense organelles (polar granules)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064781]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of CL:0000023 ! oocyte
relationship: part_of CL:0000025 ! egg cell
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005290 ! pre-blastoderm embryo (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004892
name: pole granule (Drosophila)
def: "Dense organelles found in the pole plasm of female eggs. They are 0.2 to 0.5 micrometers in diameter, changing size during development. They lack a membrane and contain RNA granules, among other components." [FlyBase:FBrf0014742, FlyBase:FBrf0064781]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004891 ! pole plasm (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004893
name: ovariole (Drosophila)
def: "An egg assembly line. Consists of a germarium at the anterior tip connected to a chain of egg chambers, each one more mature than the preceding, more anterior egg chamber in the chain. Each ovariole is encased in an ovarian sheath. A typical ovary contains about 16 ovarioles." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000992 ! ovary

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004895
name: basal stalk (Drosophila)
def: "Stalk that connects the female ovarioles in the posterior tip of the ovary to the oviduct." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004893 ! ovariole (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004897
name: peritoneal sheath (Drosophila)
def: "A network of anastomosing muscle fibers that covers the ovary. The muscle is striated with an irregular interdigitation of thick and thin filaments and perforated Z-discs." [FlyBase:FBrf0018806, FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
is_a: FBbt:00003527 ! adult circular muscle (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004898
name: epithelial sheath (Drosophila)
def: "Inner epithelial layer of the ovarian sheath." [FlyBase:FBrf0018806]
is_a: UBERON:0004911 ! epithelium of female gonad

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004899
name: ovarian basement membrane (Drosophila)
def: "An acellular membrane some 50 micrometers thick that is attached to the surface of the terminal filament, the germarium, and all developing egg chambers. The ovarian sheath sits on top (outside) of this." [FlyBase:FBrf0018806, FlyBase:FBrf0019876, FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
synonym: "tunica propria" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004893 ! ovariole (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004900
name: vitellarium (Drosophila)
def: "Ovariole excluding the germarium." [FBC:DOS]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004893 ! ovariole (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004901
name: terminal filament (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior most region of the germarium, forming the tip. It contains a group of terminal filament somatic cells. Only the most posterior cells contact the germline stem cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777, FlyBase:FBrf0084162]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004902
name: terminal filament basal cell (Drosophila)
def: "Somatic cell in the anterior germarium region 1, near the germline stem cells. There is a group of 3 cells asymmetrically positioned." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777, FlyBase:FBrf0084162]
synonym: "terminal filament base cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0084162]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004901 ! terminal filament (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004907
name: polar follicle cell (Drosophila)
def: "Follicle cell at the anterior or posterior pole of the egg chamber. The anterior polar follicle cells become border follicle cells. The posterior polar follicle cells are precursors of the posterior aeropyle." [FlyBase:FBrf0021038]
is_a: CL:0000477 ! ovarian follicle cell

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004908
name: nurse follicle cell (Drosophila)
def: "Follicle cell of the germarium that migrates posteriorly and covers the nurse cells during stage 9. There are approximately 50 follicle cells that flatten to form a squamous domain over the nurse cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0135734]
synonym: "NCFC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0135734]
synonym: "nurse cell follicle cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0135734]
synonym: "squamous follicle cell" EXACT []
synonym: "stretch follicle cell" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000477 ! ovarian follicle cell
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007031 ! nurse cell associated follicular epithelium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004911
name: oviduct (Drosophila)
def: "Duct of the female genitalia that connects the ovaries to the uterus. It is divided into 2 lateral and one common regions." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0005156 ! reproductive structure
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110692 ! presumptive oviduct (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000474 ! female reproductive system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004912
name: lateral oviduct (Drosophila)
def: "Epithelial tube that connects an ovary to the common oviduct. It is lined with a chitinous intima." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004911 ! oviduct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004913
name: common oviduct (Drosophila)
def: "Epithelial tube that connects the lateral oviducts to the uterus. It is lined with a chitinous intima." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "main oviduct" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004911 ! oviduct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004914
name: female accessory gland (Drosophila)
def: "Small, bilaterally paired gland that lies behind the spermathecae and is connected to the uterus by a duct. The gland wall consists of a single layer of polygonal cells, each with a large vacuole and a minute acidophillic granule towards the gland lumen." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0141451]
synonym: "AcGl" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "colleterial gland" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "parovarium" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
is_a: UBERON:0005398 ! female reproductive gland

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004915
name: female accessory gland duct (Drosophila)
def: "A duct connecting a female accessory gland to the uterus, opening just behind the spermathecal ducts. It consists of a tube of thin epithelium lined with a thin chitinous intima, irregularly ringed with sharp ridges that project into the lumen." [FlyBase:FBrf0186027]
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004914 ! female accessory gland (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004918
name: calyx of oviduct (Drosophila)
def: "The anterior-most, cup-shaped region of the lateral oviduct." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004912 ! lateral oviduct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004920
name: pedicel of ovarian sheath (Drosophila)
def: "The posterior end of the ovarian sheath, between the most posterior egg or egg chamber and the lateral oviduct." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:6001787 ! female genital disc
relationship: part_of UBERON:0004911 ! epithelium of female gonad

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004922
name: seminal receptacle (Drosophila)
def: "A compactly coiled tube epithelial tube connected to the anterior end of the uterus. The tube is long (1.7-2.7 mm) and slender, consisting of a proximal duct around 22 micrometres wide with a narrow lumen (2.5 - 4.5 micrometres) and a wider distal half (around 28 micrometres) with a much larger lumen (12-19 micrometres). It is lined with a thin chitinous intima and surrounded by a nucleated sheath. The coil as a whole is surrounded by a sparsely nucleated peritoneal envelope. After copulation, the lumen of this tube is filled with spermatozoa, arranged longitudinally with their heads towards the closed tip of the tube." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "tubular receptacle" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0005156 ! reproductive structure
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110701 ! presumptive seminal receptacle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000474 ! female reproductive system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004923
name: spermathecal duct (Drosophila)
def: "Duct connecting the capsule of the spermathecum to the uterus. It opens into the uterus on its dorsal wall, just posterior to the mouth of the oviduct and close to the openings of the accessory gland ducts." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0004909 ! epithelium of gonad
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000994 ! spermathecum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004925
name: vagina (Drosophila)
def: "An elongate muscular pouch, the anterior part of which is the uterus, where eggs are fertilized, and the posterior part of which, the vulva is the copulatory orifice and site of exit for eggs." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "genital chamber" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005156 ! reproductive structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110694 ! presumptive vagina (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000474 ! female reproductive system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004926
name: vulva (Drosophila)
def: "Broad area with chitinous papillae and long and narrow ridges which surrounds the vaginal opening." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110695 ! presumptive vulva (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004925 ! vagina (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004930
name: hub cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell which is part of the hub of the germinal proliferation center. It is attached to male germline stem cells and somatic stem cells via adherens junctions." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778, FlyBase:FBrf0190226]
synonym: "apical cell" RELATED []
synonym: "interstitial cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006031 ! somatic cell of testis (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007141 ! germinal proliferation center hub (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004931
name: cyst cell (Drosophila)
def: "One of a pair of somatic cells that envelope each cyst of developing male germline cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00006031 ! somatic cell of testis (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004933 ! cyst progenitor cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007136 ! male germline cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004933
name: cyst progenitor cell (Drosophila)
def: "A somatic stem cell; Mother of cyst cells; Associated with the hub of the germinal center and with male germline stem cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
synonym: "cyst stem cell" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006010 ! gonadal somatic stem cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00006031 ! somatic cell of testis (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005259 ! germinal proliferation center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004934
name: primary gonial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Daughter of a male germline stem cell. Unlike its sister, which will remain a stem cell, the primary gonial cell is displaced laterally from the hub cells, where it becomes enclosed by two 'cyst cells'. Morphology is much like its stem cell sister." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
synonym: "gonialblast" EXACT []
synonym: "primary spermatogonial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: CL:0000020 ! spermatogonium
relationship: develops_from CL:0000087 ! male germ line stem cell (sensu Nematoda and Protostomia)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004937
name: spermatocyte fusome (Drosophila)
def: "Fusome found in the cytoplasm of the spermatocyte." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00007139 ! male fusome (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of CL:0000017 ! spermatocyte

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004938
name: primary spermatocyte cyst (Drosophila)
def: "Male germline cyst containing primary 16 spermatocytes." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005258 ! spermatocyte cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004939
name: spermatocyte ring canal (Drosophila)
def: "Cytoplasmic bridge that connects the 16 primary spermatocytes in a cyst." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005409 ! ring canal (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004938 ! primary spermatocyte cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004940
name: Y chromosome loop (Drosophila)
def: "Loop in the Y chromosome in the nucleus of primary spermatocytes. Y loops are caused by the transcription of male fertility factors present on the Y chromosome." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of CL:0000017 ! spermatocyte

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004943
name: Nebenkern (Drosophila)
def: "Mitochondrial mass which is the result of fusion of mitochondria into one structure, found in developing spermatids. At the onion stage, the Nebenkern consists of a densely packed sphere of tightly packed multiple layers of wrapped mitochondrial membranes, that resembles an onion at cross section. At leaf stage, the Nebenkern unfurls to resemble a spear point or leaf blade, and later at comet stage it elongates and splits into two mitochondrial derivatives." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004945 ! onion stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004944
name: protein body (Drosophila)
def: "Protein aggregate that forms a dark and dense structure found in the nucleus of a developing spermatid. It is first visible at the agglomeration stage, gradually increasing in size during the pre-elongation stage." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of CL:0000018 ! spermatid

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004945
name: onion stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "A round spermatid containing a spherical Nebenkern with an onion-like arrangement of mitochondrial material. The axoneme begins to grow out from the basal body inserted at the base of the nucleus and the Golgi complexes have fused to form the acroblast and acrosomal granule located at the apical side of the nucleus, opposite the basal body. There is a prominent protein body in the nucleus." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: CL:0000018 ! spermatid
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057171 ! clew stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004946
name: waste bag (Drosophila)
def: "After individualisation of spermatids, the excess cytoplasm and organelles are dumped in a waste bag at the tail end of the spermatid cyst. This bag pinches off and eventually degrades." [FlyBase:FBrf0158862]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000473 ! testis

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004947
name: acroblast (Drosophila)
def: "Organelle formed by the fusion of the Golgi complexes, in an onion stage spermatid. It is located at the apical side of the nucleus, opposite the basal body, in the same area as the acrosomal granule. Together with the acrosomal granule it serves as the site of formation of the acrosome." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778, FlyBase:FBrf0219730]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of CL:0000018 ! spermatid

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004948
name: acrosomal granule (Drosophila)
def: "Granule found in the acroblast in an onion stage spermatid. It is located at the apical side of the nucleus, opposite the basal body. Together with the acroblast, it serves as the site of formation of the acrosome." [FlyBase:FBrf0219730]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004947 ! acroblast (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004949
name: axial complex (Drosophila)
def: "The complex formed by the axoneme and Nebenkern derivatives that extends the length of the sperm tail at the end of the elongation stage. The position between the axoneme and the Nebenkern derivatives is characteristic, although they become somewhat independent regarding rotation after the sperm bundle coils during individualization stage." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00007012 ! cell component (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005310 ! elongation stage spermatid (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005320 ! individualization stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004950
name: spermatid axoneme (Drosophila)
def: "Flagellar organelle that grows out from the basal body embedded at the base of the nucleus, on an onion stage spermatid. It elongates throughout the elongation stage to extend the length of the sperm tail. It is surrounded by a double membrane (axonemal sheath) and has the characteristic 9+2 disposition, with 9 outer doublet microtubules surrounding a central pair of singlet microtubules. During development, a projection from each doublet microtubule extends to form an accessory microtubule which becomes densely stained. Radial spokes develop that connect the outer doublets with the central region of the axoneme." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
synonym: "axial filament" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004949 ! axial complex (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004951
name: Nebenkern derivative (Drosophila)
def: "Structure that develops from the Nebenkern during spermatid elongation. During late onion stage, the Nebenkern begins to unfurl and elongate. At comet stage it splits into two mitochondrial derivatives, which elongate and become unequal in size during mid elongation stage. The mitochondrial derivatives assume a characteristic position to a plane that splits the central pair of axoneme microtubules which changes slightly through elongation." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004943 ! Nebenkern (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004949 ! axial complex (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004952
name: major mitochondrial derivative (Drosophila)
def: "Bigger mitochondrial derivative that develops from mid elongation spermatid stage onwards. It initially lies at a 90 degrees angle to a plane that splits the central pair of axoneme microtubules. This decreases gradually to 60 degrees during elongation, returning to 90 degrees during the later stages of spermatid differentiation. Late in the elongation stage, there is a deposition of a paracrystalline array of densely staining granules closely juxtaposed to the axonemal sheath." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004951 ! Nebenkern derivative (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004953
name: minor mitochondrial derivative (Drosophila)
def: "Smaller mitochondrial derivative that develops from mid elongation spermatid stage onwards. It lies at a 30 degrees angle to a plane that splits the central pair of axoneme microtubules." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004951 ! Nebenkern derivative (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004956
name: testis pigment cell (Drosophila)
def: "Flat, polygonal, pigmented epithelial cell which is part of the outer layer of the testis sheath." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: CL:0000066 ! epithelial cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0004910 ! epithelium of male gonad

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004957
name: testicular duct (Drosophila)
def: "Duct connecting the testis and the seminal vesicles in the adult male genitalia. It is 80 micrometers long and 23 micrometers in diameter, making a single spiral turn. It has a narrow lumen, surrounded by a thick epithelium containing small, closely spaced nuclei. It is covered in an inner sheath and an outer pigment sheath, as in the seminal vesicles." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: UBERON:0005904 ! duct of male reproductive system
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004959
name: male accessory gland (Drosophila)
def: "Paired distended tubular accessory gland of the male genitalia which opens into the ejaculatory duct just behind the vas deferens. It is composed of binucleate cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0029539]
synonym: "AcGl" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "paragonium" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005399 ! male reproductive gland
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110680 ! presumptive male accessory gland (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004960
name: male accessory gland main cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell type found in both lobes of the male accessory gland. These cells are flat, hexagonal and binucleate, which secrete their products into the lumen of each lobe. There are approximately 1000 main cells per lobe, interspersed with around 43 secondary cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0057142]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004959 ! male accessory gland (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004961
name: male accessory gland secondary cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell type found in at the distal tip of both lobes of the male accessory gland. These cells are large, spherical and binucleate with large vacuoles. There are approximately 43 secondary cells interspersed with around 1000 main cells per lobe." [FlyBase:FBrf0057142]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004959 ! male accessory gland (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004962
name: ejaculatory bulb (Drosophila)
def: "Bilaterally symmetric structure with two anterior and two posterior lateral lobes, a sclerotized rod-like apodeme arising from its upper side and muscles fibres radiating from the end of the rod to the side walls. The anterior ejaculatory duct enters the bulb on the upper side and the posterior ejaculatory duct arises between the paired projections on the opposite side. The walls of the bulb consists of a thick columnar epithelium lined with a well developed intima, enclosing a chamber filled with clear viscous fluid." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0029539, FlyBase:FBrf0075527]
synonym: "sperm pump" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005156 ! reproductive structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110685 ! presumptive ejaculatory bulb (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000079 ! male reproductive system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004963
name: ejaculatory bulb apodeme (Drosophila)
def: "Sclerotized rod-like apodeme on the upper side of the ejaculatory bulb of the adult male genitalia." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "skeletal rod" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005091 ! apodeme (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004962 ! ejaculatory bulb (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004964
name: ejaculatory bulb plate (Drosophila)
def: "Basal plate of the ejaculatory bulb apodeme of the adult male genitalia." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "basal plate of apodeme" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
synonym: "baseplate" EXACT []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004963 ! ejaculatory bulb apodeme (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004965
name: ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)
def: "Unpaired duct that connects the male accessory glands and vasa deferentia to the ejaculatory bulb in the adult male genitalia." [FlyBase:FBrf0075527]
is_a: UBERON:0003914 ! epithelial tube
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: UBERON:0005904 ! duct of male reproductive system
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110684 ! presumptive ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004966
name: posterior ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)
def: "Duct that connects the ejaculatory bulb to the aedeagus in the male adult genitalia. It is 300 micrometers long with a diameter of 11-18 micrometers, continuous with the intima lining the ejaculatory bulb. Its wall is chitinous and 0.5 micrometers thick, with small scattered nuclei on its surface. The duct passes below the rectum and opens below the ninth and tenth abdominal segments." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0034969 ! epithelial layer of duct
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004965 ! ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004967
name: anterior ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)
def: "Duct that connects the vasa deferentia and accessory glands to the ejaculatory bulb in the male adult genitalia. It is 1.2mm long with an anterior dilated portion with a diameter of 120 micrometers, tapering to a narrow tube of 20 micrometers in diameter which enter the ejaculatory bulb. In the abdomen, it extends dorsally, then curves downward and to the left and loops over the rectum to the right side of segment 5 or 6. The duct wall consists of a single thick layer of epithelial cells lined with a thin chitinous intima surrounded by an inconspicuous outer sheath." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0034969 ! epithelial layer of duct
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004965 ! ejaculatory duct (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004968
name: vas deferens (Drosophila)
def: "Paired tube of the male genitalia which opens into the anterior ejaculatory duct. Its distal portion is enlarged, forming the seminal vesicle. The twisted narrow portions of the vasa deferentia merge just before the junction with the anterior ejaculatory duct. In recently emerged flies, three distinct wall layers of the vas deferens are visible: a thick inner epithelium, with columnar cells containing small nuclei, a thin inner sheath with inconspicuous, widely spaced and flattened nuclei and an outer sheath of finely reticular cytoplasm containing an occasional large nucleus." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735, FlyBase:FBrf0029539]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00110681 ! presumptive vas deferens (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000079 ! male reproductive system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004971
name: cuticulin layer (Drosophila)
def: "Outer layer of the cuticle consisting of proteins and waxes which functions as an impermeability barrier." [FlyBase:FBrf0064790]
is_a: FBbt:00007246 ! cuticle layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004972
name: epicuticle (Drosophila)
def: "Amorphous layer between cuticulin layer and procuticle which consists largely of protein and is generally free of chitin." [FlyBase:FBrf0064790]
is_a: FBbt:00007246 ! cuticle layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004975
name: procuticle (Drosophila)
def: "Lamellate innermost layer of cuticle which consists largely of protein and chitin. Within each lamella layer, chitin-protein fibers are arranged parallel to each other and to the surface of the underlying epidermis. The lemallae themselves are arranged in a helicoid fashion." [FlyBase:FBrf0064790]
is_a: FBbt:00007246 ! cuticle layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004976
name: assembly zone (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007246 ! cuticle layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004977
name: cuticular pore (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0000464 ! anatomical space
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001001 ! chitin-based cuticle

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004978
name: exuvial fluid (Drosophila)
synonym: "moulting fluid" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0000463 ! non-tissue substance
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001001 ! chitin-based cuticle

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004980
name: dorsal hair (Drosophila)
def: "Hair on the dorsal surface of the larva on all segments except the prothorax, which is devoid of them. Members of this group are distributed in a well defined pattern." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: UBERON:6004979 ! trichome
relationship: part_of UBERON:6004983 ! embryonic/larval cuticle

[Term]
id: FBbt:00004981
