name: asynchronous muscle (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0014895 ! somatic muscle

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005089
name: muscle attachment site (Drosophila)
def: "The place where the muscle system attaches to the body wall." [FBC:gg]
is_a: FBbt:00100290 ! endocuticular specialization (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000383 ! musculature of body

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005090
name: tendon cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005089 ! muscle attachment site (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005091
name: apodeme (Drosophila)
def: "A cuticular ingrowth of the endoskeleton, sometimes only a peg, frequently ridge-like, and often serving as a muscle attachment site. Does not generally correspond to superficial invaginations." [FlyBase:FBrf0111704, FlyBase:FBrf0166419]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005089 ! muscle attachment site (Drosophila)

