[Term]
id: FBbt:00005520
name: fat body/gonad primordium (Drosophila)
def: "Primordium which develops into the fat body and gonadal sheath. The first morphological sign of its development comes during stage 11, when the outer of the two layers of the trunk mesoderm thickens medially to become 2-3 cells thick. Segmentally arranged groups of cells split off from inner most layer of this thickening, becoming sandwiched between the somatic muscle primordium and the circular visceral muscle primordium. By stage 13, these segmental clusters have fused into continuous columns on either side of the embryo. These bands split into dorsal and ventral subdivisions. A sub-population of cells in the dorsal subdivision in parasegments 10-12 split off to form the gonadal sheath primordium during stage 14-15." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570, FlyBase:FBrf0092473]
synonym: "FaB/GP2" RELATED []
synonym: "gonadal mesoderm" NARROW []
synonym: "P2 FaB/GP" RELATED [FBC:DOS]
