[Term]
id: FBbt:00005721
name: epithelial glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cuboidal glial cell found in the visual system of larvae and adults, located more distal than the row of marginal glial cells. These glial cells contact marginal glia at their base (proximal) and satellite glia at their apex (distal), and constitute the only class of cells with nuclei in the neuropil proper, in the distal lamina. A triad of epithelial glial cells surrounds groups of lamina neurons to form a cartridge (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). Epithelial glial cells elaborate numerous fine processes into the lamina plexus, especially from the surface juxtaposing the R1-R6 growth cones or axon termini (Poeck et al., 2001). In the lamina, they receives synaptic input from photoreceptors R1-R6, lamina monopolar cell L4 (collaterals from adjacent columns), lamina intrinsic (amacrine) cells, centrifugal cell C3 and lamina wide-field neuron Lawf (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055906, FlyBase:FBrf0134808, FlyBase:FBrf0205531, FlyBase:FBrf0209968, FlyBase:FBrf0210316]
is_a: FBbt:00100517 ! adult optic lobe glial cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005722
name: marginal glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cuboidal glial cell of the optic lobe elaborating numerous fine processes. It is located in a layer at the proximal surface of the lamina, with one marginal glial cell per cartridge (Edwards and Meinertzhagen, 2010). Processes extend from the apical side into the lamina to envelop axons and trachea. It is between the marginal glial cells and epithelial glial cells that the R1-R6 growth cones terminate (Poeck et al., 2001; Winberg et al., 1992). In the lamina, it receives synaptic input from photoreceptors R1, R5-R6 and lamina monopolar cell L4 (collaterals from adjacent columns) (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055906, FlyBase:FBrf0134808, FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
synonym: "adult marginal glial cell" EXACT []
synonym: "proximal glial cell" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0134808]
is_a: FBbt:00100502 ! adult neuropil associated glial cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100517 ! adult optic lobe glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003747 ! optic cartridge (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005723
name: satellite glial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Glial cell with long ensheathing processes of the optic lobe that are interspersed among the lamina neurons (Poeck et al., 2001). In the lamina it receives synaptic input from photoreceptors R1 and R2 (Rivera-Alba et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0055906, FlyBase:FBrf0096428, FlyBase:FBrf0134808, FlyBase:FBrf0205531]
synonym: "adult satellite glial cell" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100501 ! adult cell body glial cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100517 ! adult optic lobe glial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00100509 ! developing satellite glial cell (Drosophila)

