id: FBbt:00005763
name: scolopidial cilium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005223 ! scolopidial dendrite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005780
name: mushroom body dorsal paired medial cell (Drosophila)
def: "A serotonergic mushroom body intrinsic neuron (Lee et al., 2011) whose large cell body (~12um) is part of a bilateral pair of neurons located on the posterior ventral superior medial protocerebrum and antler region of the brain. A single neurite extends towards the ipsilateral mushroom body and bifurcates in the superior neuropils. One branch arborizes extensively within the mushroom body alpha and alpha' lobes, whilst the other branch arborizes extensively within the mushroom body beta, beta' and gamma lobe complexes. The cell processes also form a network of fibers and terminations in the mushroom body spur and anterior region of the pedunculus. There are no detectable projections to any other brain neuropil region (Waddell et al., 2000). Pre-synaptic terminals are found throughout the mushroom body lobes, being more pronounced in the alpha and beta lobes (Pitman et al., 2011). This neuron is electrically connected to the mushroom body anterior paired lateral cell (Wu et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0132261, FlyBase:FBrf0205263, FlyBase:FBrf0213725, FlyBase:FBrf0213804, FlyBase:FBrf0214737]
synonym: "dorsal paired medial cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205263]
synonym: "DPM" RELATED []
synonym: "MB-DPM" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205263, FlyBrain_NDB:10445]
is_a: CL:0000402 ! CNS interneuron
is_a: CL:0000850 ! serotonergic neuron
is_a: FBbt:00007484 ! mushroom body intrinsic neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005781
name: gastric caecum (Drosophila)
def: "Blind sac that branches from the anterior-most region of the embryonic/larva midgut (ventriculus). There are four of these per animal. Their cells have a similar morphology to those of the midgut epithelium." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733]
synonym: "embryonic/larval gastric caecum" EXACT []
synonym: "larval gastric caecum" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0009854 ! digestive tract diverticulum
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001882 ! embryonic/larval midgut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005782
name: copper cell (Drosophila)
def: "Large cell in the middle region of the midgut that is cup-shaped with long microvilli. These cells accumulate copper and secrete acid." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0100557, FlyBase:FBrf0139611, FlyBase:FBrf0174753]
synonym: "cuprophilic cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0139611]
is_a: CL:0002251 ! epithelial cell of alimentary canal
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001045 ! midgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005783
name: midgut interstitial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Interstitial cell of the midgut. There are 30-40 cells that initially delaminate from the tip of the posterior midgut rudiment during embryonic stages 10 and 11. Later on, they intercalate into the midgut epithelium." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814]
is_a: CL:0002251 ! epithelial cell of alimentary canal
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001045 ! midgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005784
name: principal midgut epithelial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell that forms an epithelium during germ band retraction. It corresponds to the majority of midgut rudiment cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0041814, FlyBase:FBrf0074599]
synonym: "PMEC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0074599]
is_a: CL:0002251 ! epithelial cell of alimentary canal
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001045 ! midgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005785
name: anal pad (Drosophila)
def: "Plate or plates that surrounds the anus." [FBC:MMC]
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001046 ! hindgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005787
name: posterior Malpighian tubule (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior Malpighian tubule that extends from the midgut hindgut border. It is formed from the ventral part of the hindgut. There is a pair of these that are connected to a common ureter that is on the midgut/hindgut border. The posterior tubules extend towards the tail of the embryo, with each tubule positioned on opposite sides within the body cavity. At the end of embryogenesis, the distal ends switch sides by crossing over the posterior region of the hindgut. In the mature tubules, the tip cell of the posterior tubules makes contact with the a9 abdominal visceral nerve. The posterior tubule pair is shorter than the posterior one." [FlyBase:FBrf0075100, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: UBERON:0001054 ! Malpighian tubule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005788
name: anterior Malpighian tubule (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior Malpighian tubule that extends from the midgut hindgut border. It is formed from the dorsal part of the hindgut. There is a pair of these that are connected to a common ureter that is on the midgut/hindgut border. The anterior tubules extend forward towards the head, with each tubule on opposite sides within the body cavity. The tubules bend back on themselves so the apex of the bend -the elbow or kink region- extends forward, leading the anterior tubules towards the head. Towards the end of embryogenesis, the kink region dips ventrally while the distal tips extend to retain their dorsal position. In the mature tubules, the tip cell of the anterior tubules makes contact with alary muscles of the heart. The anterior tubule pair is longer than the posterior one." [FlyBase:FBrf0211514, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: UBERON:0001054 ! Malpighian tubule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005789
name: Malpighian tubule segment (Drosophila)
def: "Segment of the Malpighian tubule. Each tubule can be divided into 4 distinct segments based on differences in appearance, cell structure and function: initial, transitional, main and ureter, from distal to proximal, respectively. The initial segment is involved in calcium homeostasis and excretion, the transitional and upper part of the main segment are secretory, whereas the lower part of the main segment is reabsorptive. Type I cells are found throughout the 4 segments, but Type II cells are absent from the lower part of the main segment and the ureter." [FlyBase:FBrf0030988, FlyBase:FBrf0083335, FlyBase:FBrf0128452, FlyBase:FBrf0184042, FlyBase:FBrf0218070, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001054 ! Malpighian tubule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005790
name: initial segment of Malpighian tubule (Drosophila)
def: "Distal segment of the Malpighian tubule. It is involved in calcium homeostasis and excretion. The initial segment of the adult is smaller than in the larva." [FlyBase:FBrf0030988, FlyBase:FBrf0083335, FlyBase:FBrf0128452, FlyBase:FBrf0184042, FlyBase:FBrf0218070, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: FBbt:00005789 ! Malpighian tubule segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005791
name: transitional segment of Malpighian tubule (Drosophila)
def: "Second most distal segment of the Malpighian tubule. It is involved in secretion." [FlyBase:FBrf0030988, FlyBase:FBrf0083335, FlyBase:FBrf0128452, FlyBase:FBrf0184042, FlyBase:FBrf0218070, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: FBbt:00005789 ! Malpighian tubule segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005792
name: main segment of Malpighian tubule (Drosophila)
def: "Third most distal segment of the Malpighian tubule. Its upper region is involved in secretion and the lower region in reabsorption." [FlyBase:FBrf0030988, FlyBase:FBrf0083335, FlyBase:FBrf0128452, FlyBase:FBrf0184042, FlyBase:FBrf0218070, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: FBbt:00005789 ! Malpighian tubule segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005793
name: ureter (Drosophila)
def: "Proximal segment connecting a pair of Malpighian tubules to the alimentary canal. The ureter is surrounded by longitudinal and circular muscles." [FlyBase:FBrf0030988]
is_a: FBbt:00005789 ! Malpighian tubule segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005794
name: specialised Malpighian tubule cell (Drosophila)
def: "Specialised cell of the Malpighian tubules. There are four different types: type I, type II, tip and tiny cell." [FlyBase:FBrf0184042]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001054 ! Malpighian tubule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005795
name: Malpighian tubule tip cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell at the distal tip of each Malpighian tubule. It is involved in tube elongation in embryogenesis by stimulating cell proliferation in neighboring cells and in positioning the tubules." [FlyBase:FBrf0050653, FlyBase:FBrf0075100, FlyBase:FBrf0222532]
is_a: FBbt:00005794 ! specialised Malpighian tubule cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005796
name: Malpighian tubule Type I cell (Drosophila)
def: "Morphologically distinct cell type found throughout the Malpighian tubules. It is a large epithelial cell joined by septate junctions to other Type I cells, with apical microvilli and infolding of the basal membrane. There are small differences between Type I cells in different tubule segments: in the initial segment, the cells have few microvilli and are relatively narrow compared with the larger, flatter cells of the main segment. Type I cells originate from division of the ectodermal Malpighian tubules primordial cells that are found in the junction between the hindgut and midgut. Type I cell proliferation is complete by late stage 13 of embryogenesis. In the mature tubules there are on average 484 Type I cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0091042, FlyBase:FBrf0108479, FlyBase:FBrf0160477]
synonym: "Malpighian tubule principal cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0030988]
synonym: "PC" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005794 ! specialised Malpighian tubule cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005798
name: excretory structure (Drosophila)
def: "Anatomical structure of the excretory system." [FBC:MMC]
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001054 ! Malpighian tubule

[Term]
id: FBbt:00005803
