[Term]
id: FBbt:00006016
name: peritracheal cell (Drosophila)
def: "Neuropeptide-expressing cell located at the base of the trachea (one per hemisegment)." [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005155 ! open tracheal system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00006017
name: embryonic/larval peritracheal cell (Drosophila)
def: "Cell located at the base of the larval trachea (one per hemisegment). It is part of a cluster of 3 cells, of which one is a non-neuronal peptidergic cell (PM cell). This peptidergic cell shows a complex morphology and extends several cytoplasmic processes. The two non-peptidergic cells (PMa cells) have less processes and are located adjacent to the branch point from which the transverse tracheal connective leaves the main longitudinal trachea (O'Brien and Taghert, 1998; Laneve et al., 2013)." [FlyBase:FBrf0100681, FlyBase:FBrf0158877, FlyBase:FBrf0220777]
synonym: "larval peritracheal cell" EXACT []
synonym: "peritracheal myomodulin cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
synonym: "PM" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
synonym: "PMa" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
synonym: "PT" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0220777]
is_a: FBbt:00006016 ! peritracheal cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00000185 ! embryonic/larval tracheal system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00006018
name: adult peritracheal cell (Drosophila)
def: "Neuropeptide-expressing cell located at the base of the adult trachea (two per segment)." [FlyBase:FBrf0100681]
is_a: FBbt:00006016 ! peritracheal cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003037 ! adult tracheal system (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00006019
name: Tv neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Larval neurosecretory neuron whose cell body is located close to the lateral border of the neuromere, ventrolaterally to the ventrolateral tract of the midline. It projects its axon below the ventrolateral tract, central lateral and central intermediate tracts and approaches the dorsal median tract from below, where it arborizes extensively. It fasciculates with the contralateral Tv neuron and innervates the thoracic neurohemal organ. The Tv neuron is one of the neurons of the cluster of apterous-expressing neurons of the lateral cluster of the thorax. The arborization at the dorsal median tract of the 3 pairs of Tv neurons overlaps and extends until the region between the first and second abdominal neuromeres (Benveniste et al., 1998; Marques et al., 2003; Santos et al., 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0106026, FlyBase:FBrf0167500, FlyBase:FBrf0201188, FlyBase:FBrf0209429]
synonym: "Ap4 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0209429]
is_a: CL:0000397 ! ganglion interneuron
is_a: CL:0000402 ! CNS interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00001983 ! thoracic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007436 ! endocrine neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110872 ! apterous-expressing neuron of the lateral cluster of the thorax Ap4 (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000934 ! ventral nerve cord
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001742 ! larval thoracic segment

