name: dorsal multidendritic neuron ddaF (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron whose cell body is located most dorsally in the dorsal group of dendritic arborization neurons. It has long primary and secondary branches marked by spiked protrusions (1-20um) along most of its length (Grueber et al., 2002)." [FlyBase:FBrf0148943, FlyBase:FBrf0148966, FlyBase:FBrf0183734, http://www.normalesup.org/~vorgogoz/FlyPNS/PNSdescription.html#ddaF, http://www.normalesup.org/~vorgogoz/FlyPNS/PNSnomenclature.html]
