name: head visceral muscle primordium (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00005519 ! visceral muscle primordium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007050
name: adult cerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "The cerebral ganglion, minus the optic lobes. It includes the first three neuromeres: protocerebrum, deutocerebrum and tritocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "adult midbrain" RELATED []
synonym: "central brain" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007051
name: procephalic glioblast (Drosophila)
def: "Any glioblast (FBbt:00005145) that is part of some central brain primordium (FBbt:00005542)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: CL:0000030 ! glioblast
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005542 ! central brain primordium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007052
name: ventral midline glioblast (Drosophila)
is_a: CL:0000030 ! glioblast
relationship: part_of FBbt:00016014 ! ventral midline glia primordium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007053
name: lateral horn (Drosophila)
def: "Dorso-lateral most synaptic neuropil domain of the adult midbrain. This horn-like projection houses the terminals of various antennal lobe projection neurons. It is not separated from other neuropils by a glial sheath, but by the extent of arborization and synapsing of these antennal lobe projection neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem3.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem1.html]
synonym: "lateral protocerebrum" RELATED []
synonym: "LH" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007064 ! dorsal centro-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007054
name: superior lateral protocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "Lateral synaptic neuropil domain of the superior neuropils. It lies behind the anterior optic tubercle, in front of the mushroom body calyx and above the superior clamp and lateral horn. Its boundary with the anterior optic tubercle (AOTU), mushroom body calyx and lateral horn is demarcated by the extent of arborization of visual projection neurons and antennal lobe projection neurons. Boundaries with the superior clamp, anterior and posterior ventro-lateral protocerebrum are defined using clearly distinguishable fiber bundles." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem2.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem2.html, VFB_vol:00045031]
synonym: "adult superior lateral protocerebrum" RELATED []
synonym: "SLP" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "slpr" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007064 ! dorsal centro-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007065 ! dorso-anterior synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007066 ! dorso-posterior synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045030 ! superior neuropils (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007055
name: superior medial protocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "Medial synaptic neuropil domain of the superior neuropils that lies above the area flanked by the mushroom lobes, pedunculus, and calyx. It is separated from the pedunculus by the superior clamp and insulated from the medial lobe by the crepine. The fan-shaped body protrudes deeply into this neuropil, separating it into anterior (ASMP) and posterior (PSMP) regions." [FBC:AJ, FBC:VH, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem1.html, VFB_vol:00007055]
synonym: "impr" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0212889]
synonym: "SMP" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "smpr" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045030 ! superior neuropils (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007058
name: ventrolateral protocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "A large mass of synaptic neuropil domains in the anterior brain of the adult, between the antennal lobe and the optic lobe. It can be divided into an anterior and posterior regions (AVLP and PVLP)." [FBC:AJ, FBC:VH, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem1.html]
synonym: "anterior optic foci" EXACT []
synonym: "ventro-lateral adult protocerebrum" EXACT []
synonym: "ventro-lateral protocerebrum" EXACT []
synonym: "VLP" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "vlpr" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007068 ! baso-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045021 ! ventrolateral neuropils (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007059
name: anterior optic tubercle (Drosophila)
def: "Synaptic neuropil domain of the adult protocerebrum that receives extensive arborizations from visual projection neurons from the lobula and the medulla, projecting via the anterior optic tract. It protrudes from the anterior-most area of the ventro-lateral neuropils and is slightly detached from the ventro-lateral protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/module/1997/descdn/index.html, VFB_vol:00007059]
synonym: "AOTU" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "optic tubercle" EXACT []
synonym: "OTU" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00045021 ! ventrolateral neuropils (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007063
name: baso-posterior medial compartment (Drosophila)
def: "One of a group of synaptic neuropil domains of the larval brain which are located ventral to the mushroom body and are grouped around the long axon tracts connecting the larval protocerebrum to the ventral nerve cord. This medially located compartment contacts the baso-anterior compartment (BA) posteriorly. The lateral cervical tract ascends through the center of this compartment." [FBC:VH, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "BPM" RELATED []
synonym: "larval baso-posterior midbrain" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001957 ! embryonic/larval deutocerebrum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007064
name: dorsal centro-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain of the larval brain that forms during the third instar from a dorsal region of the centro-posterior lateral compartment by growth of a neuropil glial sheath across it." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "CPLd" RELATED []
synonym: "dorsal centro-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain" EXACT []
synonym: "larval lateral horn" EXACT [FBC:VH]
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007065
name: dorso-anterior synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain of the larval brain that is located dorsal to the medial lobe of the mushroom body, and which is separated from the dorso-posterior compartment by a neuropil glial sheath slightly posterior to the vertical lobe of the mushroom body." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "DA" EXACT []
synonym: "dorso-anterior synaptic neuropil compartment" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007066
name: dorso-posterior synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain of the larval brain that is located dorsal to the medial lobe of the mushroom body and which is separated from the dorso-anterior compartment by a neuropil glial sheath slightly posterior to the vertical lobe of the mushroom body. Axons from this compartment converge with those from the centro-posterior lateral compartment (CPL) to form the posterior transverse tract (PTT)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "DP" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007067
name: baso-central synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "One of a group of synaptic neuropil domains of the larval brain which are located ventral to the mushroom body and are grouped around the long axon tracts connecting the larval protocerebrum to the ventral nerve cord. This medially located compartment contacts the baso-anterior compartment (BA) posteriorly." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "BC" EXACT []
synonym: "centro-posterior medial neuropil compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "larval ventral body" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007068
name: baso-posterior lateral synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "One of a group of synaptic neuropil domains of the larval brain which are located ventral to the mushroom body and are grouped around the long axon tracts connecting the larval protocerebrum to the ventral nerve cord. This compartment contacts the baso-anterior compartment (BA) posteriorly, and is lateral to the baso-central (BC) and baso-posterior medial (BPM) compartments. It grows anteriorly during larval development." [FBC:VH, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "baso-posterior lateral" EXACT []
