[Term]
id: FBbt:00007080
name: great commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Commissure of the adult brain located ventral to the fan-shaped body and posterior to the noduli. It connects the left and right ventro-lateral protocerebrum, and its main component connects the lobula of both optic lobes. The commissure also contains many other fibers that connect different neuropils. It demarcates the boundaries of the posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (posterior region), posterior lateral protocerebrum (anterior region), noduli (posterior region), inferior bridge (anterior region), superior posterior slope (anterior region), vest (posterior-superior region), epaulette (posterior region) and gorget (inferior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "c op fo" EXACT []
synonym: "commissure of optic foci" EXACT []
synonym: "GC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "VPC2" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007081
name: lateral medial fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "A transverse axon tract in the protocerebrum which is connected to the inferior lateral protocerebrum, the ventro-lateral protocerebrum and inferior medial protocerebrum." [FBC:VH, ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "l m fasc" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007082
name: medial fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "A vertical axon tract within the protocerebrum connected to the superior/inferior medial protocerebrum and to the ventral body." [ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "m fasc" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0005838 ! fasciculus of brain
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007083
name: posterior lateral fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "An arch-like bundle of neuronal fibers connecting the posterior lateral protocerebrum (PLP) and the superior intermediate protocerebrum (SIP). It demarcates the boundary between the superior clamp and lateral horn/superior lateral protocerebrum (SLP). The posterior lateral fascicle makes a steep curve near the anterior medial edge of the lateral horn (LH), where it narrowly intersects the trajectories of the mALT, mlALT and lALT. It can be divided into two sections: the lateral section between the PLP and the LH tip, and the superior section between the LH tip and the SIP (Tanaka et al., 2012)." [FlyBase:FBrf0219809, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem3.html, ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "p l fasc" RELATED []
synonym: "PLF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6007145 ! adult protocerebrum

