[Term]
id: FBbt:00007108
name: imaginal disc epithelial cell (Drosophila)
def: "A columnar epithelial cell with distinct apical-basal polarity. The apical surface has microvilli with dense plaques at their tips. A cortical network (ring) of actin filaments underlies the apical surface, extends into the microvilli and is associated with a zonula adherens which encircles each cell. Below this is a broad region of pleated sheet type septate junctions connecting all lateral surfaces to adjacent cells. Plaque-like gap junctions occur mainly interspersed among septate junctions and, at a lower frequency, below them. Small, sparsely distributed hemidesmosomes attach these cells to the underlying basal lamina." [FlyBase:FBrf0064790]
is_a: CL:0000066 ! epithelial cell
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007029 ! disc epithelium proper (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007109
name: imaginal disc anterior compartment (Drosophila)
def: "Anterior compartment of an imaginal disc. During growth of the disc, cells of the anterior compartment do not cross into the posterior compartment. With the exception of the eye-antennal disc, the boundary between these two compartments is defined at the time of disc specification by a parasegment boundary running through the disc anlage." [FlyBase:FBrf0064789]
is_a: FBbt:00007110 ! developmental compartment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000939 ! imaginal disc

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007110
name: developmental compartment (Drosophila)
def: "A region of developing tissue that is partially delimited by a compartment boundary. A compartment boundary is a sharp, stable boundary through a developing tissue that cells do not cross during development and that typically has no morphological correlate. The cells comprising the compartment form a population defined by their inability to cross the compartment boundary." [FlyBase:FBrf0151460]
xref: FBbt:00111537
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
is_a: UBERON:0005423 ! developing anatomical structure

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007111
name: imaginal disc posterior compartment (Drosophila)
def: "Posterior compartment of an imaginal disc. During growth of the disc, cells of the posterior compartment do not cross into the anterior compartment. With the exception of the eye-antennal disc, the boundary between these two compartments is defined at the time of disc specification by a parasegment boundary running through the disc anlage." [FlyBase:FBrf0064789]
is_a: FBbt:00007110 ! developmental compartment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000939 ! imaginal disc

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007112
name: cell body rind of mushroom body (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the cell body rind overlying the mushroom body calyx. It is distinct from the surrounding cortex because it contains the cell bodies of Kenyon cells (globuli cell bodies) which are smaller than other neuronal cell bodies (soma) in the midbrain cortex." [http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/silver/horiz/hrsil22.html]
synonym: "mushroom body cortex" EXACT []
synonym: "rCAp" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00100200 ! cell body rind region (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003625 ! adult brain cell body rind (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007113
name: mushroom body neuroblast (Drosophila)
def: "A neuroblast that is the precursor of the Kenyon cells. The Kenyon cells of each mushroom body descend from 4 mushroom body neuroblasts. These neuroblasts remain mitotically active throughout larval stages and into the late pupal stage." [FlyBase:FBrf0047815, FlyBase:FBrf0092568]
synonym: "MB-Nb" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00001334 ! protocerebral neuroblast (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007114
name: cell body rind of the central nervous system (Drosophila)
def: "Superficial neuronal layer of the central nervous system, composed of glia and the cell bodies of neurons (soma). The cell body rind lies under the perineurium." [ISBN:978-0-7204-7136-6]
synonym: "cortex of the central nervous system" EXACT []
synonym: "perikaryal rind" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207181]
is_a: UBERON:0000073 ! regional part of nervous system
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001017 ! central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007115
name: embryonic/larval neuroblast (Drosophila)
def: "Any neuroblast (FBbt:00005146) that is part of some larva (FBbt:00001727)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition, FlyBase:FBrf0047815]
synonym: "larval neuroblast" RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000031 ! neuroblast
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002548 ! larva

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007117
name: neuropil glial sheath (Drosophila)
def: "Layer of glial cells which largely surrounds a region of neuropil in the central nervous system." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "glial septum" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001017 ! central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007118
name: centro-anterior synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "Small synaptic neuropil domain of the larval protocerebrum that is located anterior to the medial mushroom body lobe. It contains numerous fine axons which project medially and contribute to the anterior transverse tract (ATT) and the medial cervical tract (MCT)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "CA" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007119
name: anterior transverse tract (Drosophila)
def: "Tract of the larval brain connected to the central anterior synaptic neuropil domain." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007120
name: posterior transverse tract (Drosophila)
def: "Tract of the larval brain formed by axons converging from the dorso-posterior and centro-posterior lateral compartments. This tract runs medial along the neuropil glial sheath between the dorso-posterior compartment and the mushroom body calyx before it joins the dorsal posterior commissure." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "PTT" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007121
name: dorsal posterior commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Commissure of the larval brain which is connected to (among others) the posterior transverse tract." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "DPC" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007122
name: dorsal posterior protocerebral tract (Drosophila)
def: "A vertical axon tract of the larval brain connecting the dorso-posterior compartment (DP) to the subesophageal ganglion. The tract dives ventrally through the centro-posterior intermediate compartment (CPI) towards the posterior boundary of the basoposterior medial compartment where it joins the posterior cervical tract (PCT)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155899, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "DPPT" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007125
name: centro-posterior intermediate synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain of the larval brain located posterior to the medial lobe of the mushroom body. It is separated from the centro-posterior medial compartment by the antenno-cerebral tract to which it is connected by a branch. Its axons project mainly into the posterior transverse tract and it receives a branch of the antenno-cerebral tract." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "centro-posterior intermediate synaptic neuropil compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "CPI" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007126
name: embryonic/larval posterior cervical tract (Drosophila)
def: "." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900, FlyBase:FBrf0192734]
synonym: "larval posterior cervical tract" EXACT []
synonym: "PCT" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007127
name: embryonic/larval antennal lobe (Drosophila)
def: "Paired synaptic neuropil domain of the larval deutocerebrum, located ventral to the mushroom body, that is the major target of innervation for axons carried by the antennal nerve. It is also connected to the antero-basal tract (ABT). Its posterior boundary contacts the basocentral (BC), basoposterior medial (BPM), basoposterior lateral and the basocervical (Bcv) synaptic neuropil domains." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "antennal compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "BA" EXACT []
synonym: "baso-anterior synaptic neuropil domain" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "LAL" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0147119]
synonym: "larval antennal lobe" EXACT []
synonym: "larval olfactory lobe" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00003924 ! antennal lobe (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001957 ! embryonic/larval deutocerebrum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007128
name: antero-basal tract (Drosophila)
def: "Tract of the larval brain which is connected to the baso-anterior synaptic neuropil domain (BA; antennal compartment). This tract travels along the neuropil glial sheath which forms the boundary between baso-anterior (BA) and baso-central (BC) synaptic neuropil domains. The tract then turns dorsally to make the antennal root of the antenno-cerebral tract (ACT)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155899, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "ABT" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007129
name: baso-cervical synaptic neuropil domain (Drosophila)
def: "One of a group of synaptic neuropil domains of the larval brain which are located ventral to the mushroom body and are grouped around the long axon tracts connecting the larval protocerebrum to the ventral nerve cord. This compartment contacts the baso-anterior compartment (BA) posteriorly and guides the medial cervical tract (MCT)." [FBC:VH, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "baso-cervical neuropil compartment" EXACT []
synonym: "Bcv" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007130
name: baso-medial protocerebral tract (Drosophila)
def: "An axon tract of the larval brain which is a branch of the lateral cervical tract. The branch point, at the center of the basal synaptic neuropil domain (the neuropil glial sheath between baso-posterio medial (BPM), baso-central (BC) and baso-posterior lateral (BPL)) compartments is known as the anterior hub. It crosses the baso-posterior lateral compartment (BPL) where it splays out into several terminal branches." [FlyBase:FBrf0155899, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "BMPT" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007131
name: larval optic focus (Drosophila)
def: "A synaptic neuropil domain of the larval brain formed during larval stages by axons originating from the lobula primordium in the optic lobe and dorso-lateral protocerebrum. These axons form terminal branches beyond the borders of the centro-posterior lateral and baso-lateral compartments which then become enclosed by a glial sheath, forming this compartment." [FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "LOF" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:6040007 ! synaptic neuropil domain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007132
name: dorsal air sac (Drosophila)
def: "Large, multi-lobed air sac of the dorsal adult thorax. It arises from an outgrowth of the lateral trunk between the branches to the second and third legs. It comprises the postnotal, lateroscutal, medioscutal, scutellar, pleural and notopleural air sacs." [FlyBase:FBrf0011558, FlyBase:FBrf0034081, FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
is_a: FBbt:00003101 ! tracheal air sac (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00007135 ! dorsal air sac primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003018 ! adult thorax

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007133
name: air sac subdivision (Drosophila)
def: "Subdivision of an adult tracheal air sac." [FBC:MMC]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003101 ! tracheal air sac (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007134
name: head air sac (Drosophila)
def: "Any tracheal air sac (FBbt:00003101) that is part of some adult head (FBbt:00003007)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition, FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
is_a: FBbt:00003101 ! tracheal air sac (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003007 ! insect adult head

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007135
name: dorsal air sac primordium (Drosophila)
def: "Primordium formed by tracheoblasts that bud from the tracheal branch which adheres to the wing disc during the late larval stage. During pupal stages this primordium forms an epithelial sac. Cells at the tip of this primordium show extensive protrusive activity - producing filopodia and lamellopodia - while maintaining epithelial integrity (including adherens junctions with their neighbors) ." [FlyBase:FBrf0151893, FlyBase:FBrf0190195]
is_a: FBbt:00007477 ! air sac primordium (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0000485 ! columnar epithelium

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007136
name: male germline cyst (Drosophila)
def: "Unit of spermatogenic differentiation consisting of a pair of cyst cells enclosing the developing germline cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00004875 ! germline cyst (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000473 ! testis

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007137
name: female germline cyst (Drosophila)
def: "A cyst of female germ cells interconnected by ring canals. Each cyst originates as a single cystoblast which divides to form 16 cystocytes. These become enveloped in a follicle cell epithelium as they pass through region 2 of the germarium. Cysts that have left the germarium are termed egg chambers." [FlyBase:FBrf0064777]
is_a: FBbt:00004875 ! germline cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007138
name: spermatogonial cyst (Drosophila)
def: "A male germline cyst consisting of 2 cyst cells and one primary spermatogonial cell. The latter is the mitotic founder of a cyst of secondary spermatogonia. Following 4 mitotic divisions, the spermatogonial cyst becomes a primary spermatocyte cyst." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00007136 ! male germline cyst (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007139
name: male fusome (Drosophila)
def: "Fusome of the male germline stem cell or its progeny." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00004862 ! fusome (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000473 ! testis

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007140
name: female fusome (Drosophila)
def: "Fusome of the female germline stem cell or its progeny." [FBC:MMC]
is_a: FBbt:00004862 ! fusome (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004866 ! germarium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007141
name: germinal proliferation center hub (Drosophila)
def: "A cone shaped cluster of densely packed cells at the center of the germinal proliferation center. It is anchored to the tip of the testis via apical connections to the thick, convoluted basal lamina found there." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: part_of FBbt:00005259 ! germinal proliferation center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007142
name: eye disc anterior to the morphogenetic furrow (Drosophila)
def: "Portion of imaginal disc epithelium which is anterior to the morphogenetic furrow of the eye disc." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001768 ! eye disc (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007143
name: eye disc posterior to the morphogenetic furrow (Drosophila)
def: "Portion of the eye disc which is posterior to the morphogenetic furrow. It contains developing ommatidial clusters whose maturity increases with distance posterior to the furrow." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001768 ! eye disc (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007144
name: early ommatidial precursor cluster (Drosophila)
def: "An ommatidial precursor cluster containing 5 prospective photoreceptors and 1-2 mystery cells. The definitive 5 cell ommatidial precluster is formed when these mystery cells are expelled from this structure and join the surrounding undifferentiated epithelium." [FlyBase:FBrf0064798]
is_a: FBbt:00001770 ! ommatidial precursor cluster (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007146
name: adult deutocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "Deutocerebrum of the adult brain." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "adult deuterocerebrum" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003923 ! deutocerebrum (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003012 ! adult antennal segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007147
name: adult tritocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "Tritocerebrum of the adult brain." [FBC:SPR]
is_a: FBbt:00003999 ! tritocerebrum (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003013 ! adult intercalary segment (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007148
name: embryonic/larval antenno-cerebral tract (Drosophila)
def: "Antenno-cerebral tract of the larva." [FlyBase:FBrf0155899, FlyBase:FBrf0155900]
synonym: "larval antenno-cerebral tract" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00001635 ! antennal lobe tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007151
name: adult antennal sense organ (Drosophila)
def: "Any sense organ (FBbt:00005155) that is part of some antenna (FBbt:00004511)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00004113 ! adult sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00005806 ! antennal sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000972 ! antenna

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007153
name: embryonic/larval antennal lobe glomerulus (Drosophila)
def: "Any glomerulus (FBbt:00005386) that is part of some embryonic/larval antennal lobe (FBbt:00007127)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
synonym: "larval antennal lobe glomerulus" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003925 ! antennal lobe glomerulus (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007127 ! embryonic/larval antennal lobe (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007157
name: anterior bundle (Drosophila)
def: "Tract of the adult brain which runs through the hole in the middle of the ellipsoid body (the ellipsoid body canal)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007158
name: adult maxillary neuromere (Drosophila)
def: "Second caudal neuromere of the gnathal ganglion, posterior to the mandibular neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem2.html]
synonym: "maxillary segment of adult subesophageal ganglion" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00111044 ! adult gnathal neuromere (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003016 ! adult maxillary segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007159
name: adult mandibular neuromere (Drosophila)
def: "First caudal neuromere of the gnathal ganglion, anterior to the maxillary neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem2.html]
synonym: "mandibular segment of adult subesophageal ganglion" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00111044 ! adult gnathal neuromere (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003015 ! adult mandibular segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007160
name: adult labial neuromere (Drosophila)
def: "Third caudal neuromere of the gnathal ganglion, posterior to the maxillary neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/sagschem2.html]
synonym: "labial segment of adult subesophageal ganglion" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00111044 ! adult gnathal neuromere (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003017 ! adult labial segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007161
name: maxillary subesophageal commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Second caudal segment of the gnathal ganglion, posterior to the mandibulary segment." [http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem2.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001020 ! nervous system commissure
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007158 ! adult maxillary neuromere (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007162
name: labial commissure (Drosophila)
def: "." [http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/horizschem2.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001020 ! nervous system commissure
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007160 ! adult labial neuromere (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007163
name: ventral arm of pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Ventral process (arm) of the pharyngeal sclerite that directly contacts the pharynx." [FlyBase:FBim0000950, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "ventral cornua" EXACT []
synonym: "ventral plate" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049928]
synonym: "ventral wing" EXACT []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007164
name: dorsal arm of pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)
def: "Paired dorsal process of the pharyngeal sclerite. This structure, into which the cibarial muscle inserts, is situated in the narrow lumen of the dorsal pouch. It is connected anteriorly to the dorsal bridge (also known as latticed process) and ventrally to the vertical bridge (also known as vertical plate)." [FlyBase:FBim0000950, FlyBase:FBrf0045366]
synonym: "dorsal cornua" EXACT []
synonym: "dorsal posterior process" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0220416]
synonym: "dorsal wing" EXACT []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001850 ! pharyngeal sclerite (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007165
name: dorsal wing blade (Drosophila)
def: "Parts of the wing blade and margin which develop from the dorsal compartment of the wing pouch." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007288 ! insect integumentary specialisation
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000984 ! imaginal disc-derived wing

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007166
name: ventral wing blade (Drosophila)
def: "Parts of the wing blade and margin which develop from the ventral compartment of the wing pouch." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:6007288 ! insect integumentary specialisation
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000984 ! imaginal disc-derived wing

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007173
name: cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Any neuron (FBbt:00005106) that capable of some acetylcholine secretion, neurotransmission (GO:0014055)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: CL:0000108 ! cholinergic neuron

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007189
name: central dome sensillum (Drosophila)
def: "Dome shaped cuticular process of the larval dorsal organ, innervated by seven circularly arranged triplets of olfactory receptor neuron (ORN) dendrites. The wall of the dome has numerous pore channels, consistent with a role as an olfactory sense organ." [FlyBase:FBrf0089570]
is_a: UBERON:6007231 ! external sensillum
is_a: UBERON:6007242 ! embryonic/larval head sensillum
relationship: part_of FBbt:00002655 ! dorsal organ (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007190
name: olfactory receptor neuron of dorsal organ (Drosophila)
def: "Odorant receptor expressing bipolar neuron whose dendrite innervates the central dome sensillum of the larval dorsal organ, whose cell body is part of the dorsal organ ganglion and whose axon is carried by the antennal nerve to innervate a larval antennal lobe glomerulus." [FlyBase:FBrf0147119, FlyBase:FBrf0187327]
synonym: "DO ORN" EXACT []
synonym: "DO OSN" EXACT []
synonym: "odorant receptor neuron of dorsal organ" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00005163 ! sensory organ cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007388 ! embryonic/larval olfactory receptor neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007189 ! central dome sensillum (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007191
name: calyx of larval mushroom body (Drosophila)
synonym: "MB-C" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0211533]
is_a: FBbt:00003685 ! mushroom body calyx (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00011929 ! embryonic/larval mushroom body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007192
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus A1 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from larval uniglomerular projection neuron 82a. It is usually located anterolaterally within the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007193
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus A2 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that is usually located ventrolaterally within the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007194
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus V3 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus that is innervated by extrinsic neurons that project from the larval subesophageal ganglion and that is usually located on the ventral surface of the larval mushroom body calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007195
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus D1 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from larval uniglomerular projection neuron 33b/47a. This is a large,landmark glomerulus that lies in a central position, posterior to glomerulus L3." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007196
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus L1 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from larval uniglomerular projection neuron 13a. It is usually the most dorsoposterior glomerulus of the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007197
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus M3 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from larval uniglomerular projection neuron 83. It is usually located at the ventromedial corner of the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007198
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus A3 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from a larval uniglomerular projection neuron 45a. It is usually located anteromedially within the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007199
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus V4 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus of the larval mushroom body calyx that is located in a ventral position, posterior to glomerulus A3." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007200
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus L2 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from a larval uniglomerular projection neuron 24a. It is usually located on the lateral edge of the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007201
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus D3 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from a larval uniglomerular projection neuron 49a. It is usually located dorsomedially within the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007203
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus I1 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that is located lateral and internal in the larval mushroom body calyx. It is located internal to larval mushroom body calyx L6 and L1." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007204
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus D5 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that is usually located dorsomedially, anteromedial to the larval mushroom body calyx D3. It is not always distinct from glomerulus D4 (FBbt:00007212)." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007205
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus I7 (Drosophila)
def: "A glomerulus located in the interior of the larval mushroom body calyx, interior to the larval mushroom body calyx M1." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007206
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus A4 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from a larval uniglomerular projection neuron 1a. It is usually located anteromedially within the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007207
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus L7 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus that is located at the lateral edge of the larval mushroom body calyx. It lies anterior or ventral to calyx glomerulus L3." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007208
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus M1 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus that is located medially in the larval mushroom body calyx. It lies ventral to calyx glomerulus D4." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007209
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus I2 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that is located anterior and internal in the larval mushroom body calyx. It lies internal to the larval mushroom body calyx A1." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007210
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus V7 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus that is located ventrally in the larval mushroom body calyx, anterior to glomerulus M4." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007211
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus V6 (Drosophila)
def: "Glomerulus that is located ventrally in the larval mushroom body calyx, anterolateral to glomerulus V1." [FlyBase:FBrf0191451]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007212
name: larval MB calyx glomerulus D4 (Drosophila)
def: "A larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus that receives synaptic input from a larval uniglomerular projection neuron 45b. It is usually located at the posteromedial edge of the calyx." [FlyBase:FBrf0208205, FlyBase:FBrf0211879]
is_a: FBbt:00007224 ! larval mushroom body calyx glomerulus (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007213
