[Term]
id: FBbt:00007336
name: abdominal nerve to the ovary (Drosophila)
def: "Paired nerve that branches from the abdominal nerve trunk and projects to the junction of the ovaries and the lateral oviduct where it branches repeatedly. Some branches radiate anteriorly across the peritoneal sheath, on which they terminate, mainly in the anterior two thirds of the ovary. Varicosities occur along these branches as well as at their ends. These branches do not penetrate the peritoneal sheath. Other branches innervate the lateral oviduct and the upper portion of the common oviduct. Two types of branches innervate the common oviduct - wandering fibers similar to those on the peritoneal sheath, and branches running circularly, parallel to the underlying myofibers." [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
synonym: "AbNvOv" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
is_a: FBbt:00002179 ! abdominal nerve (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003023 ! adult abdomen

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007337
name: abdominal nerve to the uterus (Drosophila)
def: "Paired nerve that branches from the abdominal nerve trunk and projects to the uterus where it innervated both the extrinsic muscles and the circular muscle fibers. One branch projects to the inner layers of the uterus." [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
synonym: "AbNvUt" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
is_a: FBbt:00002179 ! abdominal nerve (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003023 ! adult abdomen

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007338
name: lateral oviduct circular muscle (Drosophila)
def: "A striated array of circular muscle fibers forming an almost continuous sheet around the lateral oviduct." [FlyBase:FBrf0193596]
is_a: FBbt:00003527 ! adult circular muscle (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007339
name: serotonergic SP1 neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell body is located in the anterodorsal brain. There is a cluster of neurons in each hemisphere. In adults, there are three neurons per cluster, with two of these being generated during metamorphosis." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551, FlyBase:FBrf0158877]
synonym: "SP1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048551]
synonym: "supraesophageal ganglion neuron 1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0048551]
is_a: FBbt:00100359 ! serotonergic SP neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007340
name: haltere trichome (Drosophila)
def: "Trichome/hair of the haltere. Compared to wing hairs, they are smaller and present at a higher density." [FlyBase:FBrf0051925]
synonym: "haltere hair" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:6004979 ! trichome
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000987 ! haltere

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007341
name: serotonergic LP2 neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell bodies are located in 2 pairs of clusters (a and b) in the adult brain in the cortex of optic peduncle, adjacent to the medulla layer. These cells are born during metamorphosis. There are 8-10 neurons in this cluster." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551]
