[Term]
id: FBbt:00007369
name: inter-ommatidial precursor cell (Drosophila)
def: "Precursor of the inter-ommatidial cells (secondary and tertiary pigment cells). From 10 hours after puparium formation (APF), these cells are part of an unstructured pool of undifferentiated cells surrounding each developing ommatidial core. Around 20-23 hours APF, the primary precursors leave this pool and become part of the ommatidia. Following this, the inter-ommatidial precursors and inter-ommatidial bristle precursors develop into an organized lattice surrounding the ommatidia." [FlyBase:FBrf0103328]
synonym: "interommatidial precursor cell" EXACT []
synonym: "IPC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0103328]
is_a: FBbt:00007008 ! somatic precursor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007370
name: primary pigment cell precursor (Drosophila)
def: "Precursor of the primary pigment cells of the retina. From 10 hours after puparium formation, these cells are part of an unstructured pool of undifferentiated cells surrounding each developing ommatidial core. Around 20-23 hours APF, the primary pigment cell precursors leave this pool and become part of the ommatidia." [FlyBase:FBrf0103328]
is_a: FBbt:00007008 ! somatic precursor cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007371
