[Term]
id: FBbt:00007401
name: adult antennal lobe (Drosophila)
def: "The adult antennal lobe is a bilaterally paired synaptic neuropil domain of the deutocerebrum lying in front of the protocerebral synaptic neuropil domains. It is divided into approximately 50 glomeruli and is clearly separated from adjacent neuropil domains by an extensive glial sheath. The two antennal lobes are connected by the antennal commissure and receive olfactory receptor neuron axons from the antennal nerve and subesophageal tract. It is also connected to the antennal lobe tracts and the broad root." [FlyBase:FBrf0051437, FlyBase:FBrf0107836, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/atlas/schematic/frontschem1.html, http://flybrain.neurobio.arizona.edu/Flybrain/html/terms/terms.html, VFB_vol:00007401]
synonym: "adult olfactory lobe" EXACT []
synonym: "AL" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00003924 ! antennal lobe (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007146 ! adult deutocerebrum (Drosophila)

