[Term]
id: FBbt:00007405
name: CSD interneuron (Drosophila)
def: "A large serotonergic interneuron of the adult brain whose cell body is located close to the antennal lobe, whose dendrites innervate the antennal lobe in the same hemisphere as the cell body and whose axons innervate the contralateral antennal lobe and higher brain centers including the mushroom body cortex, the dorsal horn and the posterior superior protocerebrum. There are only two CSD interneurons per brain (one cell body per hemisphere)." [FlyBase:FBrf0195231, FlyBase:FBrf0205432]
synonym: "adult serotonergic IP1-1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0219731]
synonym: "contralaterally innervating serotonin immunoreactive deutocerebral interneuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205432]
synonym: "CSD neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "CSDn" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0205432]
synonym: "MB-CSD" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
