id: FBbt:00007406
name: tergotrochanteral muscle motor neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Motor neuron that innervates the tergotrochanteral muscle and is electrically synapsed to the giant fiber neuron. It functions in jump response escape behavior. It projects through the posterior dorsal mesothoracic nerve to the mesothoracic neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0085744]
synonym: "TTMn" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0085744]
is_a: FBbt:00005123 ! motor neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007407
name: great commissural interneuron (Drosophila)
def: "Any interneuron (FBbt:00005125) that fasciculates with some great commissure (FBbt:00007080)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: CL:0000099 ! interneuron

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007408
name: peripherally synapsing interneuron (Drosophila)
def: "." [FlyBase:FBrf0085744]
is_a: CL:0000099 ! interneuron

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007409
name: leg taste bristle (Drosophila)
def: "Any chaeta (FBbt:00005177) that is part of some leg (FBbt:00004640) and  that capable of some detection of chemical stimulus involved in sensory perception of taste (GO:0050912)." [FBC:auto_generated_definition]
is_a: FBbt:00004246 ! leg sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00005178 ! taste bristle (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007411
name: large labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
def: "Largest taste bristle subtype of the outside labellum: each bristle is around 35 micrometres long. These bristles are located in the region between the intermediate bristles on the lobe periphery and the medial-ventrally located short taste bristles. These taste bristles contain 4 gustatory receptor neurons (Shanbhag et al., 2001) sensitive to: sugars, low concentrations of salt, bitter or high salt concentrations and water or low osmolarity (Meunier et al., 2003; Fujishiro et al., 1984) and one mechanosensory neuron (Shanbhag et al., 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0041338, FlyBase:FBrf0137194, FlyBase:FBrf0160792]
synonym: "L-type sensilla" EXACT []
synonym: "long labellar taste bristle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0137194]
synonym: "lTB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0137194]
is_a: FBbt:00004162 ! labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004533 ! labellar cap (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007412
name: intermediate labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
def: "Intermediate sized taste bristle of the outside of the labellum: each bristle is around 25 micrometers long. These bristles are located dorsally, on the labellar lobe periphery. These taste bristles house the sensory dendrites of 2 gustatory receptor neurons (Shanbhag et al., 2001): one sensitive to sugars and low concentrations of salt and the other to bitter and high salt concentrations (Hiroi et al., 2004). These taste bristles also contains the sensory dendrite of one mechanosensory neuron (Shanbhag et al., 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0137194, FlyBase:FBrf0180410]
synonym: "I-type sensilla" EXACT []
synonym: "iTB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0137194]
is_a: FBbt:00004162 ! labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004533 ! labellar cap (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007413
name: short labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
def: "Shortest subclass of taste bristle of the labellum: each bristle is around 15 micrometres long and is curved in the medial direction. These bristles are located in the most medial and ventral regions of the outside labellum. These taste bristles contain the sensory dendrites of 4 gustatory receptor neurons (Shanbhag et al., 2001) sensitive to: sugars; low concentrations of salt; bitter or high salt concentrations; water or low osmolarity (Meunier et al., 2003; Fujishiro et al., 1984).These taste bristles also contains the sensory dendrite of one mechanosensory neuron (Shanbhag et al., 2001)." [FlyBase:FBrf0041338, FlyBase:FBrf0137194, FlyBase:FBrf0160792]
synonym: "S-type sensilla" EXACT []
synonym: "sTB" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0137194]
is_a: FBbt:00004162 ! labellar taste bristle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004533 ! labellar cap (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007414
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron vPN (Drosophila)
def: "Adult antennal lobe projection neuron that is derived from the ventral AL neuroblast lineage and that innervates multiple antennal lobe glomeruli. The dendritic arbors of these neurons do not form glomerular shapes (Lai et al., 2008). All of these neurons have an axon that innervates the lateral horn." [FlyBase:FBrf0146917, FlyBase:FBrf0203179, FlyBase:FBrf0205814]
synonym: "multi vPN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0203179]
synonym: "multiglomerular projection neuron vPN" EXACT []
synonym: "multiglomerular vPN" EXACT []
synonym: "vmulti" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0203179]
is_a: FBbt:00007437 ! adult antennal lobe projection neuron vPN (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007441 ! adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007415
name: adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron lPN (Drosophila)
def: "Adult antennal lobe projection neuron that is derived from the lateral AL neuroblast lineage and that innervates multiple antennal lobe glomeruli. The dendritic arbors of these neurons do not outline individual glomeruli and their axons project through the medial antennal lobe tract to various higher brain centers such as the posterior-lateral protocerebrum and the superior protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0205814]
synonym: "atypical multiglomerular PN" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0205814]
synonym: "multiglomerular lPN" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007439 ! adult antennal lobe projection neuron lPN (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007441 ! adult multiglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00067350 ! antennal lobe projection neuron iPN (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007416
name: GABAergic adult local interneuron type A of the lateral AL neuroblast (Drosophila)
def: "GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe that is derived from the lateral AL neuroblast and that arborizes throughout the antennal lobe without outlining individual glomeruli." [FlyBase:FBrf0205814]
synonym: "GABAergic type A lateral local neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "GABAergic type A lLN" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007395 ! adult local interneuron type A of the lateral AL neuroblast (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007402 ! GABAergic local interneuron of the adult antennal lobe (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007417
name: GABAergic local interneuron of larval antennal lobe (Drosophila)
def: "GABAergic local interneuron that connects glomeruli within the larval antennal lobe. Most (perhaps all) of local interneurons of the larval antennal lobe are GABAergic (Python and Stocker, 2002)." [FlyBase:FBrf0152159]
synonym: "GABAergic larval LN" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0011005 ! GABAergic interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00007226 ! local interneuron of larval antennal lobe (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007228 ! GABAergic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007418
name: outer optic anlage neuroblast (Drosophila)
def: "A neuroblast that is located in the larval outer optic anlage during larval stages." [FBC:MMC]
synonym: "outer anlage neuroblast" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00110571 ! optic lobe forming neuroblast (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007419
name: antennal basiconic sensillum TB (Drosophila)
def: "Olfactory basiconic sensillum of antennal segment 3 with about the same length as the large ab sensilla, but thinner and with longitudinal rows of pores like those found in the small ab sensilla." [FlyBase:FBrf0128642, PMID:18535862]
synonym: "TB" RELATED []
synonym: "thin antennal basiconic sensillum" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: FBbt:00004174 ! sensillum basiconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0002268 ! olfactory organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007420
name: antennal basiconic sensillum TB-2 (Drosophila)
def: "Thin ab basiconic sensillum innervated by 2 olfactory receptor neurons (ORNs). In some subtypes the innervating dendrites are highly branched, while in others are innervated by unbranched, hollow dendrites." [FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: FBbt:00007419 ! antennal basiconic sensillum TB (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007421
name: antennal basiconic sensillum TB-4 (Drosophila)
def: "Thin ab basiconic sensillum innervated by the branched dendrites of 4 olfactory receptor neurons (ORNs)." [FlyBase:FBrf0128642]
is_a: FBbt:00007419 ! antennal basiconic sensillum TB (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007422
name: antennal lobe projection neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Interneuron whose dendrite innervates the antennal lobe (larval or adult) and whose axon innervates some higher brain centre (generally the mushroom body calyx and/or lateral horn)." [FBC:DOS]
synonym: "olfactory projection neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0183938]
is_a: FBbt:00007392 ! projection neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007423
name: lamina furrow (Drosophila)
def: "A region of the lamina anlage marked by a fold. Like the morphogenetic furrow in the developing eye, this fold progresses from posterior to anterior, reflecting posterior to anterior progression of differentiation." [FlyBase:FBrf0054817, ISBN:978-3-540-42590-8]
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
is_a: UBERON:6007424 ! epithelial furrow
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001939 ! lamina anlage (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007426
name: ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
def: "A tract of the central nervous system that does not cross the midline." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:0001018 ! axon tract

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007427
name: posterior optic commissure (Drosophila)
def: "A large midline-crossing commissure that emerges from the serpentine layer of the medulla and connects the medulla of each brain hemisphere, passing dorsal to the esophageal foramen (Helfrich-Forster and Homberg, 1993). It demarcates the boundaries of the posterior lateral protocerebrum (posterior-inferior region), superior posterior slope (posterior-inferior region) and inferior posterior slope (posterior-superior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0065419, FlyBase:FBrf0224194, ISBN:978-3-540-07343-7]
synonym: "POC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "posterior optic tract" EXACT []
synonym: "POT" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0001020 ! nervous system commissure

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007428
name: s-LNv neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron of the period-expressing LNv cluster of the adult brain, with a small cell body and generally located more dorsally than the l-LNv neurons (Helfrich-Forster, 1998). There are 5 cells present in each cluster, all except one of which express Pdf (FBgn0023178)." [FlyBase:FBrf0193849]
synonym: "s-LNv" EXACT []
synonym: "s-vLN neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0209505]
synonym: "sLNv" EXACT []
synonym: "small LNv" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004044 ! LN period neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007429
name: DN1a neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Anteriorly located member of the Period-expressing DN1 cluster of the adult brain. There are two DN1a neurons per cluster located between 15 and 30 micrometers anterior to the DN1p cluster." [FlyBase:FBrf0152101, FlyBase:FBrf0195358]
synonym: "anterior DN1 neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "DN1a" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00003629 ! DN1 neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007430
name: DN1p neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Posteriorly located member of the Period-expressing DN1 cluster of the adult brain that expresses glass (FBgn0004618). There are 14-17 DN1p cells per cluster. Many, perhaps all cells in this cluster project through the dorsal fusion commissure (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0152101, FlyBase:FBrf0195358]
synonym: "DN1p" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior DN1 neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003629 ! DN1 neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007431
name: DN3a neuron (Drosophila)
def: "DN (dorsal Period-expressing neuron of adult brain) with a medium-sized cell body, located in the lateral-most cluster of per expressing DN neurons. There are two cells per hemisphere, each of which project anteriorly to the aMe (Helfrich-Forster et al., 2007)." [FlyBase:FBrf0193849]
synonym: "adult dorsal neuron-3a." RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00003628 ! adult DN period neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007432
name: LP neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Period-expressing neuron located in a cluster of 3-4 cells in the lateral central brain, medial to the LNd cluster and near the posterior of the brain (Shafer et al., 2006; Helfrich-Forster, 2005)." [FlyBase:FBrf0183981, FlyBase:FBrf0187530, FlyBase:FBrf0195358]
synonym: "lateral posterior neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "LPN" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00006048 ! pacemaker neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007433
name: Pdf negative s-LNV neuron (Drosophila)
def: "s-LNv neuron of the adult brain that does not express Pdf (FBgn0023178). There is one of these in each ventral cluster of LN period neurons. It is located more dorsally than the s-LNv Pdf neurons (Helfrich-Forster, 2007; Rieger et al., 2006). It extends a single neurite through the medulla that invades the lamina, forming thin arborizations in the lamina cortex near the retina that terminate at the border of the fenestrated glia (Damulewicz and Pyza, 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0101921, FlyBase:FBrf0214354]
synonym: "PDF-negative s-LNv" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193849]
synonym: "PDH negative s-LNV neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "PDH-negative s-LNV neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "sLNv PDF-negative" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003702 ! optic lobe neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007428 ! s-LNv neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007434
