[Term]
id: FBbt:00007513
name: adult gut (Drosophila)
def: "Structure consisting of the adult foregut, midgut and hindgut." [FBC:DOS]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00100322 ! adult alimentary canal (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007514
name: small field neuron of the central complex (Drosophila)
def: "A small field neuron that innervates the central complex. The majority of small field neurons of the central complex are intrinsic to it, and they typically connect one central complex domain to another. Some also connect subdomains within a single central complex domain." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
is_a: CL:0000402 ! CNS interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00003633 ! small field neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007515
name: large field neuron of the central complex (Drosophila)
def: "Large field neuron that innervates the central complex. Typically these neurons innervate a single neuropil domain with the central complex, arborizing in either the entire domain or some entire subdomain, as well as innervating additional regions external to the central complex." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409]
is_a: FBbt:00003648 ! large field neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007516
name: vertical system neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Giant neuron of the lobula plate with a dendritic arbor that extends along the dorsal-ventral axis of the lobula plate and an axon terminal projecting to the protocerebral region (Scott et al., 2002). It receives synaptic input both in the lobula plate and in the protocerebrum and has its synaptic output in the latter (Raghu et al., 2007). Cells of this class are involved in the optomotor response (Joesch et al., 2008) and exhibit directionally selective responses during the presentation of vertically moving periodic gratings. Each VS cell possesses its distinct receptive field (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0032046, FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0200428, FlyBase:FBrf0204334, FlyBase:FBrf0207482]
synonym: "VS" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10041]
synonym: "VS neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00003906 ! lobula plate giant neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007517
name: vertical system neuron 1 (Drosophila)
def: "The outermost vertical system neuron. This neuron has a main dendritic shaft that produces one or a few dorsally projecting branches before sweeping ventrally. As the main shaft extends ventrally, it continues to produce smaller branches that combine to form a narrow band covering the most lateral part of the lobula plate. This cell is relatively flat but extends anteriorly in the dorsal aspect of its dendritic tree (Scott et al., 2002). Its receptive field of vision is the most frontal of all VS cells. It is electrically coupled to VS2 (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0204334]
synonym: "VS1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007518
name: vertical system neuron 2 (Drosophila)
def: "Vertical system neuron whose dendritic tree within the lobula plate partially overlaps with that of vertical system neuron 1 (VS1) but extends more medially. Its major dendritic shaft sweeps from dorsal to ventral. Its dendritic tree is less highly branched than that of VS1 and is very flattened in the anterior-posterior axis, with all of its dendritic structures among the posterior dendrites of the vertical system (Scott et al., 2002). Its receptive field of vision is in between the receptive fields of VS1 and VS3. It is electrically coupled to VS1 and VS3 (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0204334]
synonym: "VS2 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007519
name: vertical system neuron 3 (Drosophila)
def: "Vertical system neuron with both dorsally and ventrally sweeping major branches and whose dorsal dendritic tree extends anteriorly and posteriorly. Unlike ventral system neuron 2, its dorsal dendrites continue to slant laterally as they extend dorsally and have a major component that extends anteriorly (Scott et al., 2002). Its receptive field of vision is in between the receptive fields of VS2 (more frontal) and VS4 (more lateral). It is electrically coupled to VS2 and VS4 (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0204334]
synonym: "VS3 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007520
name: vertical system neuron 4 (Drosophila)
def: "Vertical system neuron with both dorsally and ventrally sweeping major branches and whose dorsal dendritic tree extends anteriorly and posteriorly. Unlike VS3, its dorsal dendrites curve so that they extend directly dorsally or even medially and have only a few simple anterior projections (Scott et al., 2002). Its receptive field of vision is in between the receptive fields of VS3 (more frontal) and VS5 (more lateral). It is electrically coupled to VS3 and VS5 (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0204334]
synonym: "VS4 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007521
name: vertical system neuron 5 (Drosophila)
def: "Vertical system neuron whose dendritic branching pattern is simple and predominantly limited to the dorsal lobula plate. This neuron projects at least two major dendritic branches dorsally, one from the initial dorsal extension, and one from a major branch that initially grows into the central lobula before contributing a dorsally extending branch. Its dendritic tree extends much more anteriorly than that of other ventral system neurons (Scott et al., 2002). Its receptive field of vision is in between the receptive fields of VS4 (more frontal) and VS6 (more lateral). It is electrically coupled to VS4 and VS6 (Joesch et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898, FlyBase:FBrf0204334]
synonym: "VS5 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007522
name: vertical system neuron 6 (Drosophila)
def: "Vertical system neuron whose dendritic branching pattern is simple and predominantly limited to the dorsal lobula plate. This neuron has a single major dorsal branch that is an extension of the original dorsal arborization. Its dendritic tree extends anteriorly, but not as far as that of vertical system neuron 5." [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
synonym: "VS6 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0155898]
is_a: FBbt:00007516 ! vertical system neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007523
name: pontine neuron P1 (Drosophila)
def: "Pontine neuron of the fan-shaped body that connects segments on either side of the midline." [FlyBase:FBrf0049409, FlyBase:FBrf0210154]
is_a: FBbt:00003636 ! pontine neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003679 ! fan-shaped body (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007524
