[Term]
id: FBbt:00007654
name: prosternal nerve (Drosophila)
def: "A slender nerve that projects anteriorly from the thoracico-abdominal ganglion, near the base of the dorsal prothoracic nerve (FBbt:00004055) to innervate the prosternal sense organ." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: FBbt:00002063 ! prothoracic nerve (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0011215 ! central nervous system cell part cluster
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110174 ! adult prothoracic neuromere (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007655
name: prosternal sense organ (Drosophila)
def: "A sense organ located in a pit in the anterior wall of the thorax - immediately under the neck. It consists of a plate of sensory hairs whose innervating neurons have their cell bodies in a small ganglion behind the organ and project through the prosternal nerve to the prothoracic neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
synonym: "PSO" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: FBbt:00004113 ! adult sense organ (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007234 ! compound sense organ (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004558 ! adult external prothorax (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007656
name: anterior prothoracic chordotonal organ (Drosophila)
def: "A chordotonal organ of the adult prothorax with a V-shape in which the two arms are opened widely. One arm is attached to the anterior wall of the thorax at the articulation with the head, immediately below the prosternal sense organ (FBbt:00007655). The other arm is attached to the hypotremal apodeme and the angle between the two arms is pressed against the anterolateral corner of the prothoracic neuromere, immediately below the dorsal prothoracic and prosternal nerves. A thick, short group of fibers, the anterior prothoracic chordotonal nerve, connect this organ to the thoracico-abdominal ganglion (prothoracic neuromere)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
synonym: "aCO" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0090742]
synonym: "anterior chordotonal organ" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0090742]
synonym: "PCO" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
synonym: "prosternal chordotonal organ" EXACT [PMID:17362981]
synonym: "prothoracic chordotonal organ" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: UBERON:0001038 ! chordotonal organ

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007657
name: prothoracic leg nerve (Drosophila)
def: "A nerve that connects carries a mix of motor and sensory fibres from the prothoracic leg to the adult prothoracic neuromere. Each nerve extends laterally and slightly anteriorly from a slight swelling at the lower anterior corner of the ventral-anterior region of the prothoracic neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0007196]
is_a: FBbt:00002063 ! prothoracic nerve (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003020 ! adult prothoracic segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003559 ! adult nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007658
name: trichome field (Drosophila)
def: "A group of trichomes covering a region of integument." [FBC:DOS]
is_a: UBERON:0000477 ! anatomical cluster

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007659
name: optic column (Drosophila)
def: "A subdivision of the optic lobe neuropil that maps to a single ommatidium. In the lamina and distal medulla these correspond to the projections and arborization of photoreceptor cells. Narrow field columnar neurons define continuation of these columns medial to this." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "neuro-ommatidium" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "visual column" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
is_a: FBbt:00040069 ! synaptic neuropil segment (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007660
name: proximal joint of prothoracic coxa (Drosophila)
def: "The joint between the proximal end of the prothoracic coxa and the body of the prothoracic segment. The fossa (socket) of this joint is part of the coxa. The condyle (ball) is part of the body." [FlyBase:FBrf0031004, FlyBase:FBrf0158845, FlyBase:FBrf0219028]
