[Term]
id: FBbt:00007669
name: prothoracic ventral eclosion muscle (Drosophila)
def: "A muscle of the prothorax that forms a broad attachment onto the lateral region of the sternal apodeme and extends towards the neck. It dies within 24 hours of eclosion and (probably) function in the thoracic contractions that are part of eclosion behavior." [FlyBase:FBrf0167817]
is_a: FBbt:00003334 ! skeletal muscle of prothorax (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00016665 ! temporary eclosion muscle (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00007670
name: antennal nerve branch (Drosophila)
def: "One of the terminal branches of the antennal nerve in the antenna. One branch goes to the Johnston's organ in the second antennal segment. In the third antennal segment, the nerve splits into 3 major branches, which further ramify to innervate the external sensory organs of this segment." [FlyBase:FBrf0129873]
synonym: "fascicle of antennal nerve" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0129873]
