relationship: part_of FBbt:00001675 ! embryonic/larval heart (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00011929
name: embryonic/larval mushroom body (Drosophila)
def: "Mushroom body of the larva. It is composed of two lobes only, medial and vertical, in contrast to the adult. Mushroom body neuroblasts continue to supply increasing numbers of Kenyon cells through the larval stages. The axons of these neurons follow the tracts laid down during embryonic development. Which tracts they contribute to varies depending on the stage of development: from first instar to third instar stage 1, they contribute to the gamma lobe; during third instar stage 2 and puparium formation each axon bifurcates and contributes to the alpha' and beta' lobes (during the pupal stage they contribute to the alpha and beta lobes). At third instar stage, four layers at the level of the pedunculus and lobes: surface, outer, inner layers and core. Three types of intrinsic neurons can be identified at this stage that occupy specific layers: embryonic-born gamma type (surface layer), larval-born gamma type (outer and inner layers) and larval-born alpha'/beta' type (core layer) neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0111409, FlyBase:FBrf0144836]
synonym: "larval mushroom body" NARROW []
is_a: UBERON:0001058 ! mushroom body
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005508 ! mushroom body primordium (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001925 ! embryonic/larval protocerebrum

