[Term]
id: FBbt:00013333
name: spiracular occlusor muscle (Drosophila)
def: "A muscle that functions in closing a spiracle." [FBC:DOS, FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0014895 ! somatic muscle

[Term]
id: FBbt:00013334
name: occlusor of adult abdominal spiracle (Drosophila)
def: "A muscle that functions in closing an adult abdominal spiracle. These muscles are attached to sclerotised lever which is in turn attached to a deep fold in the wall of spiracle at the base of the atrium. The other end is attached to a rigid part of the wall of the atrium so that its contraction closes the passage. There is no dilator muscle so the passage is probably kept open by its natural elasticity (Miller, 1950 pg 459)." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: FBbt:00013333 ! spiracular occlusor muscle (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00013335
name: occlusor of adult thoracic spiracle (Drosophila)
def: "A muscle that functions in closing an adult thoracic spiracle. These muscles attach the rim (peritreme) of spiracle and to the adjacent body wall. Their contraction serves to bring the two lips of the spiracle together." [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: FBbt:00013333 ! spiracular occlusor muscle (Drosophila)

