name: visceral branch primordium (Drosophila)
def: "Tracheal primordium that develops into the embryonic/larval the embryonic/larval visceral branch. It branches anteriorly from the dorsal portion of the transverse connective primordium during stage 12, coursing anteriorly and inwardly towards the gut." [FlyBase:FBrf0064787]
