id: FBbt:00057155
name: meiotic secondary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Secondary spermatocyte during meiosis II (GO:0007135)." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: CL:0000657 ! secondary spermatocyte

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057167
name: polar primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Early primary spermatocyte with a spherical, asymmetrically placed nucleus and with mitochondria aggregated at the pole of the cell opposite the nucleus. The second nuclear membrane has started to form, the nucleolus is compact with few cavities and the centrioles are in the central region of the cell." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
synonym: "polar spermatocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005286 ! primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00005260 ! secondary spermatogonium (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057168
name: apolar primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Mid primary spermatocyte, with a large central nucleus which has an undulating surface. The nucleus of this cell is in the process of becoming surrounded by a second nuclear membrane, and has a large nucleolus filled with irregularly shaped cavities." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005286 ! primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057167 ! polar primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057169
name: mature primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
def: "Late, fully grown primary spermatocyte with a large central nucleus, blocky in appearance, often with indentations or grooves, containing Y-loops and a prominent nucleolus. The second nuclear membrane is fully formed. It has a highly developed endoplasmic reticulum, with mitochondria between the cisternae." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
synonym: "apolar spermatocyte" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005286 ! primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057168 ! apolar primary spermatocyte (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057170
name: agglomeration stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "A round spermatid in which the mitochondria have coalesced into one or more agglomerations that together form a crescent shaped mass, and in which a small spherical protein body has formed in the spherical nucleus." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005289 ! pre-elongation spermatid (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057172 ! coalescence stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057171
name: clew stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "A round spermatid in which fusion of mitochondria into a single, spherical mass with a clew-like (spherical Nebenkern) arrangement is complete. During this stage the centriole inserts into the base of the nucleus to become the basal body. The spermatid has increased in diameter to 6 micrometers. The second nuclear membrane no longer covers the part of the nucleus opposite the basal body and is often continuous with the endoplasmic reticulum." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005289 ! pre-elongation spermatid (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057170 ! agglomeration stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057172
name: coalescence stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "A round spermatid with a crescent-shaped group of mitochondria at the same pole of the cell as the centriole and with a small spherical nucleus that lacks a protein body." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: CL:0000018 ! spermatid
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057151 ! secondary spermatocyte in meiotic telophase II (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057174
name: comet stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "An early elongation-stage spermatid of length 35-120 micrometers resembling a comet, with a bipartite parallel mitochondrial derivative that developed from the Nebenkern, with its diameter decreasing from 5 to 1 micrometers. The cytoplasmic inclusions in the mitochondrial derivative gradually disappear. The nucleus is round and clear." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00057175 ! early elongation stage spermatid (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00057176 ! leaf blade stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057175
name: early elongation stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "A spermatid which has initiated axoneme elongation, but which is relatively short (up to 200 micrometers in length) and retains a round nucleus. The two parts of the mitochondrial derivative are roughly equal in size." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00005310 ! elongation stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00057176
name: leaf blade stage spermatid (Drosophila)
def: "An early elongation-stage spermatid of length 15-35 micrometers, with a Nebenkern resembling a spear point of leaf blade and with cytoplasmic inclusions. A protein body is visible in the nucleus, the centriole adjunct forms and the axoneme elongates." [FlyBase:FBrf0064778]
is_a: FBbt:00057175 ! early elongation stage spermatid (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from FBbt:00004945 ! onion stage spermatid (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00067000
name: antennal trichoid sensillum at3 (Drosophila)
def: "Olfactory trichoid sensillum of antennal segment 3 that is innervated by 3 ORNs. It is distinguishable from at4 by its odor response profile (de Bruyne and Baker, 2008) and the identity of the ORNs that innervate it (2a, 19a/b and 43a; Couto et al., 2005; de Bruyne and Baker, 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0187305, PMID:18535862]
is_a: FBbt:00007350 ! antennal sensillum trichodeum T3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00067001
name: adult olfactory receptor neuron Or2a (Drosophila)
def: "Bilateral olfactory receptor neuron (ORN) that expresses Or2a (FBgn0023523). Its axon branches, with one branch innervating the ipsilateral antennal lobe glomerulus DA4 medial compartment and the other fasciculating with the antennal commissure and innervating the contralateral antennal lobe glomerulus DA4 medial compartment. Its dendrite transduces signals from trichoid sensillum at3." [FlyBase:FBrf0187305]
synonym: "adult ORN Or2a" EXACT []
synonym: "odorant receptor neuron DA4m" RELATED []
synonym: "odorant receptor neuron Or2a" EXACT []
synonym: "ORN (Or2a)" EXACT [FlyBrain_NDB:10397]
synonym: "ORN at3A" EXACT [PMID:18535862]
synonym: "ORN at3X" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0226805]
is_a: FBbt:00007292 ! sensory neuron of trichoid sensillum (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007352 ! antennal olfactory receptor neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00067000 ! antennal trichoid sensillum at3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00067002
name: antennal basiconic sensillum ab2 (Drosophila)
def: "A large olfactory basiconic sensillum of the antenna, innervated by 2 ORNs. It is distinguishable from ab3 by its odor response profile (De Bruyne et al., 2001) and the identity of the ORNs that innervate it (59b and 85a/33b; Couto et al., 2005)." [FlyBase:FBrf0108493, FlyBase:FBrf0187305]
synonym: "antennal large basiconic sensillum ab2" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004175 ! large sensillum basiconicum of antennal segment 3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
