[Term]
id: FBbt:00100000
name: Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Scolopidial (mechanosensory) neuron of Johnston's organ. Its axon innervates the ipsilateral antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). A small number of fibers also innervate the contralateral AMMC via the commissure of JON. Subset of JO neurons extend into the ventral region of the ventrolateral protocerebrum and posterior part of the subesophageal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0083230, FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00005222 ! scolopidial neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004178 ! Johnston organ (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100001
name: Johnston organ bundle of antennal nerve (Drosophila)
def: "Bundle formed from the fasciculated axons of the Johnston's organ neurons (JONs) within the antennal nerve (AN). The JONs form two bundles (dorsolateral and medioventral) within the antennal nerve by the point it reaches the base of antennal segment 1 (a1/scape). Shortly before entering the brain, these two bundles combine and spread over a large area of the AN cross-section. Upon entering the brain, the JONs predominantly occupy the ventral part of the AN. At the ventrolateral side of the antennal lobe, the bundle bifurcates. One side of the bifurcation gives rise to the main trunk of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). The other side defasciculates and innervates zone A of the AMMC." [FlyBase:FBrf0187921, FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "Johnston organ nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "Johnston organ neuron nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "Johnston's organ nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron nerve" RELATED []
synonym: "JON nerve" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0187921, FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003980 ! adult antennal nerve (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100002
name: sound activated Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "A Johnston organ neuron (JON) that is activated by near-field sound ranging from 19 Hz to 952 Hz, maximally at 90dB (Kamikouchi et al., 2009; Yorozu et al., 2009). These neurons are transiently (phasically) activated by the onset and offset of arista displacement. Cells preferentially activated by low-frequency vibration are loosely distributed as a ring in the middle layer of JON cell bodies. Higher frequencies preferentially activate JON neurons with cell bodies located mainly in the inner layer, directly surrounding the antennal nerve (Kamikouchi et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston organ neuron phasically activated by arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron phasically activated by arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "sound activated Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "vibration sensitive JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
is_a: FBbt:00007684 ! auditory sensory neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100000 ! Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100003
name: gravity sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron (JON) that is tonically activated by aristal deflection and is necessary for normal gravitaxis behaviour. These neurons form a broad 'ring' in the medial and outer layers of the JON array (Kamikouchi et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "deflection sensitive neurons" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "gravity sensing neurons" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "gravity sensitive Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100012 ! Johnston organ neuron tonically activated by arista deflection (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100004
name: wind sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron (JON) tonically activated by arista deflection and required for 'wind-induced suppression of locomotion' behaviour (WISL; Yorozu et al., 2009). The cell bodies of these neurons form a broad ring in the medial and outer layers of the JON array (Kamikouchi et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "deflection sensitive neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "wind sensitive Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100012 ! Johnston organ neuron tonically activated by arista deflection (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100005
name: main trunk of antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)
def: "The main trunk (MT) of antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) is one of two bundles formed by the initial bifurcation of the Johnston's organ nerve projection, ventro-laterally to the antennal lobe. The second, more lateral bundle forms the anterior portion of AMMC zone A. The MT progresses posteriorly and exhibits a second bifurcation that gives rise to the bundle forming AMMC zone B. A final posterior MT bifurcation gives rise to the AMMC lateral core and EA bundle. The MT is devoid of presynaptic sites." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "main trunk" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "main trunk of AMMC" EXACT []
synonym: "main trunk of JON bundle" RELATED []
synonym: "MT" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: UBERON:0000122 ! neuron projection bundle
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100006
name: EA bundle of antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)
def: "Bundle, devoid of presynaptic sites, formed from one branch of the final, most posterior bifurcation of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) main trunk (MT). The other side of the bifurcation gives rise to the lateral core of the AMMC (LC). It is directly connected to zone E of the AMMC and consists of the projections of zone E Johnston's organ neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "anterior region of bundle e" EXACT []
synonym: "anterior region of zone E" EXACT []
synonym: "EA" EXACT []
synonym: "EA bundle of AMMC" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100007
name: lateral core of antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron projection bundle containing the axons of Johnston's organ neurons (JONs) that arises from the final, most posterior bifurcation of the main trunk of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). (The other bundle arising from this bifurcation is the EA region of the AMMC). The lateral core is devoid of presynaptic sites. It terminates in a bifurcation that gives rise to the synapse rich AMMC zones C and D." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "lateral core of AMMC" EXACT []
synonym: "LC" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100008
name: zone A Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron that innervates zone A of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). The cell bodies of these neurons are located mainly in the inner layer of Johnston's organ, directly surrounding the antennal nerve. These neurons plays a role in hearing and are activated when stimulated with courtship song pulses (between 19-952Hz, 90dB). They are phasically activated, with the strongest activation by higher-frequency vibrations (Kamikouchi et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "zone A Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone A JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00100002 ! sound activated Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100009
name: zone B Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron that innervates zone B of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). The cell bodies of zone B Johnston organ neurons are distributed as a ring in the middle layer of cells within the Johnston's organ (Kamikouchi et al., 2006). These neurons plays a role in hearing and are activated when stimulated with courtship song pulses (between 19-952Hz, 90dB). They are is phasically activated, with stronger activation by low-frequency vibrations. They are required for the detection of the courtship song (Kamikouchi et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "zone B Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone B JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00100002 ! sound activated Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100010
name: zone C Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron that innervates zone C of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). The cell bodies of these neurons are co-mingled with those of zone E Johnston organ neurons, forming a broad ring mainly in the medial and outer layers of the Johnston's organ. These neurons show a tonic response to static deflections of the arista (Kamikouchi et al., 2009) and are involved in sensing air-flow (Yorozu et al., 2009) and gravitational forces (Kamikouchi et al., 2009). Their response is strongest when the arista is displaced anteriorly, corresponding to air flow applied to the back of the head. They are required for wind-induced suppression of locomotion behaviour (WISL) (Yorozu et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston organ neuron activated by tonic anterior arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron activated by tonic anterior arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "zone C Johnston's organ neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone C JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00100003 ! gravity sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100004 ! wind sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100012
name: Johnston organ neuron tonically activated by arista deflection (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron whose response is maintained so long as unidirectional aristal deflection is sustained." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron tonically activated by arista deflection" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100000 ! Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100015
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone A (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone A is a synapse rich sub-region of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) formed from bifurcation of the Johnston's organ bundle. (The other structure arising from this bifurcation is the main trunk of the AMMC (MT)). Zone A is rich in presynaptic sites of Johnston's organ neurons. The cell bodies of zone A Johnston organ neurons are located mainly in the inner layer of Johnston's organ, directly surrounding the antennal nerve (Kamikouchi et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "AMMC zone A" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone A" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100016
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone B (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone B is a synapse rich sub-region of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) formed from the first bifurcation of the AMMC main trunk. It is rich in presynaptic sites of Johnston's organ neurons (JONs)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518]
synonym: "AMMC zone B" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone B" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100017
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone C (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone C is a synapse rich sub-region of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) that arises from the most lateral half of the bifurcation that terminates the lateral core (lc) bundle. (The other half of the bifurcation forms zone D). It is rich in the presynapses of Johnston's organ neurons (JONs) (Kamikouchi et al., 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "AMMC zone C" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone C" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100018
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone D (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone D is a synapse rich sub-region of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) that arises from the bifurcation that terminates the lateral core bundle. (The other half of the bifurcation forms zone C). It is rich in the presynapses of zone D Johnston's organ neurons (zone D JONs)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0225118]
synonym: "AMMC zone D" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone D" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100019
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone E (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal mechanosensory and motor center zone E is a synapse-rich sub-region of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) that is continuous with the EA bundle. It is rich in presynaptic sites of Johnston's organ neurons (JONs)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "AMMC zone E" EXACT []
synonym: "ammc zone E" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
synonym: "zone E" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00040006 ! synaptic neuropil subdomain (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003982 ! antennal mechanosensory and motor center (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100020
name: zone D Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron that innervates zone D of the most posterior region of the ipsilateral antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC) with little arborization. The cell bodies of these neurons are distributed as a pair of clusters in JO. These neurons plays a role in hearing and are activated when stimulated with courtship song pulses. They are phasically activated, with the strongest activation by medium range-frequency vibrations. These neurons are also activated by an anterior deflection of the arista, corresponding to air flow applied to the back of the head, similarly to zone C Johnston organ neuron." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0225118]
synonym: "zone D JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00100002 ! sound activated Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100004 ! wind sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100021
name: zone E Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Johnston's organ neuron that innervates zone E of the antennal mechanosensory and motor center (AMMC). The cell bodies of these neurons are co-mingled with those of zone C Johnston organ neurons, forming a broad ring mainly in the medial and outer layers of the Johnston's organ. These neurons show a tonic response to static deflections of the arista (Kamikouchi et al., 2009) and are involved in sensing air-flow (Yorozu et al., 2009) and gravitational forces (Kamikouchi et al., 2009). Their response is strongest when the arista is displaced posteriorly, corresponding to air flow applied to the front of the head and are required for wind-induced suppression of locomotion behaviour (WISL) (Yorozu et al., 2009)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194812, FlyBase:FBrf0207518, FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston organ neuron activated by tonic posterior arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "Johnston's organ neuron activated by tonic posterior arista deflection" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0207559]
synonym: "zone E JON" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0194812]
is_a: FBbt:00100003 ! gravity sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100004 ! wind sensitive Johnston organ neuron (Drosophila)

