[Term]
id: FBbt:00100100
name: Rh5 photoreceptor of Bolwig organ (Drosophila)
def: "Cholinergic photoreceptor cell of the larval Bolwig's organ that expresses the blue-absorbing rhodopsin Rh5 (lambda[max] = 437nm; FBgn0014019). Fibers pass along the larval optic nerve and terminate medioventrally in the larval optic neuropil where they are surrounded by the projections of Rh6 photoreceptors of Bolwig organ. Same neurites bypass the larval optic neuropil and project to the adjacent ipsilateral central brain (Keene et al., 2011). Their projections in the larval optic neuropil have been shown to overlap with serotonergic arborizations (Rodriguez Moncalvo and Campos, 2005) and with the dendrites of pacemaker lateral neurons (LN's) (Keene et al., 2011; Mazzoni et al., 2005). There are about 4 Rh5 photoreceptors per Bolwig organ." [FlyBase:FBrf0144829, FlyBase:FBrf0184213, FlyBase:FBrf0190156, FlyBase:FBrf0213587]
synonym: "Rh5 photoreceptor of Bolwig's organ" RELATED []
synonym: "Rh5-expressing photoreceptor of Bolwig's organ" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007253 ! photoreceptor cell of Bolwig organ (Drosophila)

