[Term]
id: FBbt:00100138
name: embryonic/larval subesophageal ganglion (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the embryonic/larval brain consisting of the fused ganglia of the three gnathal segments. The anterior-most part of this ganglion lies between the two brain hemispheres. Its posterior boundary with the thoracic ganglia lies within the ventral nerve cord. During metamorphosis this posterior boundary constricts to form the cervical connective." [FlyBase:FBrf0007733, FlyBase:FBrf0134489, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "embryonic/larval SOG" EXACT []
synonym: "hindbrain" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0134489]
