[Term]
id: FBbt:00100177
name: larval s-LNv neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Larval neuron of the period-expressing LNv cluster, with a small cell body and generally located more dorsally than the l-LNv neurons and that innervates the larval optic neuropil. There are 5 cells present in each cluster, all except one of which express Pdf (FBgn0023178). The four Pdf positive s-LNv neurons project into a distinct domain of the dorsal protocerebrum (Keene et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0098279, FlyBase:FBrf0101921, FlyBase:FBrf0213587]
synonym: "s-LNv" RELATED []
is_a: FBbt:00001913 ! larval LN period neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100178
name: larval Pdf negative s-LNv neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Larval s-LNv neuron that does not express Pdf (FBgn0023178). It innervates the larval optic neuropil significantly and projects to a broader domain than the four Pdf positive s-LNv neurons (Keene et al., 2011). There is only one of these per ventral cluster of LN period neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0098279, FlyBase:FBrf0213587]
is_a: FBbt:00100177 ! larval s-LNv neuron (Drosophila)

