[Term]
id: FBbt:00100214
name: dopaminergic PAM neuron (Drosophila)
def: "A dopaminergic neuron whose cell body is located in a cluster of approximately 100 cell bodies in the cortex of the anterior inferior medial protocerebrum. At least some members of this group project to areas posterior to the mushroom body medial lobe (Mao and Davis, 2009). Neurons in this cluster project bilaterally to the medial portion of the mushroom body beta-lobe (Claridge-Chang et al., 2009). Contacts with Kenyon cells are visible in the horizontal lobes, namely in the medial regions of the gamma, beta and beta' lobes." [FlyBase:FBrf0208427, FlyBase:FBrf0208958, FlyBase:FBrf0222995]
synonym: "PAM" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208427]
synonym: "PAM cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral anteriomedial dopaminergic cluster neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "protocerebral anterior medial dopaminergic cluster neuron" RELATED []
synonym: "TH-positive anteriomedial cluster neuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00005131 ! dopaminergic neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

