name: alpha'/beta' anterior-posterior Kenyon cell (Drosophila)
def: "A subgroup of the mushroom body alpha'/beta' neurons that has dendrites in the main calyx and project axons to the anterior and posterior layers of the alpha'/beta' lobes. There are around 210 neurons in each hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0205263, FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
