[Term]
id: FBbt:00100334
name: maxillary nerve (Drosophila)
synonym: "MxN" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100335
name: mandibular nerve (Drosophila)
def: "The mandibular nerve is a mixed sensory-motor nerve of the gnathal ganglion (GNG). It contains axons from the sensory cells of the mandibles entering the mandibular neuromere of the GNG and GNG motor axons to mandibular musculature." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "MnN" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: UBERON:0011779 ! nerve of head region
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003007 ! insect adult head

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100337
name: anterior optic tract (Drosophila)
def: "Tract that emerges from the medial part of the lobula. One branch ends in the anterior optic tubercle (AOTU) whilst the other makes a medial turn to terminate in the superior medial posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum (PVLP) of the adult brain. It demarcates the boundaries of the PVLP (lateral region), anterior VLP (superior and lateral region), AOTU (inferior-lateral region) and lateral horn (inferior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0039022, FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "AOT" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100338
name: pyriform fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "Tract emerging from the superior-most lateral area of the superior medial protocerebrum and ending in the region between the superior lateral protocerebrum and lateral horn of the adult brain. It demarcates the boundary between these two regions." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "PYF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100339
name: anterior superior lateral protocerebrum fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "Emerging from cells located in the lateral cell body region, the anterior superior lateral protocerebrum fascicle exhibits a J-shape and terminates in the boundary between the superior intermediate protocerebrum and the superior lateral protocerebrum (SLP) just posterior to the anterior optic tubercle of the adult brain. It demarcates the inferior boundary of the SLP with the superior intermediate protocerebrum, anterior and posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum and superior clamp." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "anterior SLP fascicle" EXACT []
synonym: "aSLPF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6110636 ! adult cerebral ganglion

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100340
name: horizontal ventrolateral protocerebral fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "Emerging from cells located in the lateral cell body region, the horizontal ventrolateral protocerebral fascicle terminates in an area between the lateral accessory lobe, inferior clamp and epaulette. It contains fibers projecting towards the inferior and ventromedial neuropils. It demarcates the boundaries of the lateral accessory lobe (posterior region), inferior clamp (inferior region) and epaulette (superior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "horizontal VLP fascicle" RELATED []
synonym: "hVLPF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100341
name: vertical ventrolateral protocerebral fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The vertical ventrolateral protocerebral fascicle emerges from cells in the lateral cell body region and terminates in the superior lateral protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "vertical VLP fascicle" RELATED []
synonym: "vVLPF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100342
name: medial equatorial fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The medial equatorial fascicle is a thick fascicle that emerges from cells in the medial posterior rind region below the mushroom body calyx and branches out in the region inferior-lateral to the fan-shaped body. It demarcates the boundaries of the inferior bridge (lateral region), inferior clamp (superior-medial), superior posterior slope (superior region), gorget (superior region) and fan-shaped body (inferior-lateral region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "median equatorial fascicle" EXACT []
synonym: "MEF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "protocerebral bridge - lateral protuberance tract" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100343
name: lateral equatorial fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The lateral equatorial fascicle emerges from the lateral posterior rind region and ends in the inferiormost part of the inferior clamp. It runs lateral to the medial equatorial fascicle. It demarcates the boundaries of the inferior clamp (inferior-lateral region), posterior lateral protocerebrum (medial region), superior posterior slope (superior-lateral), and gorget (lateral region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "LEF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100344
name: posterior cerebro-cervical fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The posterior cerebro-cervical fascicle derives from the superior lateral part of the cervical connective and terminates in the inferior fiber system. It demarcates the boundaries of the superior slope (inferior region), inferior slope (superior region) and wedge (superior-medial). It contains the axon of the giant fiber neuron." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "pCCF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "posterior CCF" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior cerebrocervical fascicle" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100345
name: medial cerebro-cervical fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The medial cerebro-cervical fascicle derives from the superior medial part of the cervical connective and ends in the medial part of the posterior gnathal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "mCCF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "medial CCF" EXACT []
synonym: "medial cerebrocervical fascicle" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100346
name: anterior cerebro-cervical fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The anterior cerebro-cervical fascicle derives from the inferior medial part of the cervical connective. It runs by the posterior maxillary sensory center (PMS) and converges to the inferior fiber system. It demarcates the boundary between the flange and saddle." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "aCCF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "anterior CCF" EXACT []
synonym: "anterior cerebrocervical fascicle" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100347
name: lateral cerebro-cervical fascicle (Drosophila)
def: "The lateral cerebro-cervical fascicle derives from the inferior lateral part of the cervical connective and projects towards the lateral surface of the saddle and wedge, demarcating their lateral boundaries." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "lateral CCF" EXACT []
synonym: "lateral cerebrocervical fascicle" EXACT []
synonym: "lCCF" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: FBbt:00007426 ! ipsilateral tract (Drosophila)
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100348
name: fiber system (Drosophila)
def: "Area of the brain where fascicles from various directions meet and merge. They are largely or completely devoid of synapses." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "fibre system" EXACT []
relationship: part_of FBbt:00040004 ! tract neuropil (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100349
name: superior fiber system (Drosophila)
def: "The superior fiber system is a prominent fiber system in the superior brain. It lies superior-lateral to the fan-shaped body and anterior to the superior part of the medial antennal lobe tract. It demarcates the boundaries between the superior lateral protocerebrum (posterior-medial region), superior intermediate protocerebrum (posterior region), superior medial protocerebrum (posterior-lateral region) and superior clamp (superior-medial region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "SFS" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "superior fibre system" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100348 ! fiber system (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100350
name: inferior fiber system (Drosophila)
def: "The inferior fiber system is a large fiber system in the inferior brain, lying inferior-posterior to the antennal lobe." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "IFS" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "inferior fibre system" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100348 ! fiber system (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100351
name: superior antennal lobe commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Dorsal-most of two commissures connecting the antennal lobes and running in front of the ellipsoid body." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "inter-antennal lobe tract" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "interantennal lobe tract" EXACT []
synonym: "sALC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "superior AL commissure" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003979 ! antennal commissure (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100352
name: inferior antennal lobe commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Ventral-most of two commissures connecting the antennal lobes and running in front of the ellipsoid body." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "iALC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "inferior AL commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "inter-antennal lobe tract" EXACT []
synonym: "interantennal lobe tract" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003979 ! antennal commissure (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100354
name: superior ellipsoid commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Commissure lying above the ellipsoid body connecting the superior medial protocerebrum (SMP), superior intermediate protocerebrum (SIP), superior clamp (SCL) and inferior clamp (ICL). It demarcates the boundaries of the ellipsoid body (superior region), SMP (inferior region), SIP (inferior region), SCL (inferior region) and ICL (superior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "SEC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "supra ellipsoid tract" RELATED []
synonym: "supra-ellipsoid tract" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100355
name: posterior posteriolateral protocerebral commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Commissure running above the esophagus and below the inferior bridge, connecting the middle levels of the posterior lateral protocerebrum. It demarcates the boundary between the inferior bridge and superior posterior slope." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "posterior PLP commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "pPLPC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100356
name: wedge commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Commissure lying posterior and inferior to the great commissure and anterior to the posterior optic commissure. It connects of both hemispheres. IT demarcates the superior posterior slope (inferior region) and inferior slope (superior region)." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "inferior ventrolateral protocerebrum commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "inferior VLP commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "IVLP commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "WEDC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100357
name: superior AMMC commissure (Drosophila)
def: "Component of the great commissure. It branches off anteriorly from the great commissure, posterior to the epaulette, and ends in the AMMC. It runs above the esophagus, dorsal to the inferior AMMC commissure." [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "sAMMC commissure" EXACT []
synonym: "sAMMCC" EXACT BRAIN_NAME_ABV [FlyBase:FBrf0224194]
synonym: "superior AMMCC" EXACT []
synonym: "superior antennal mechanosensory and motor center commissure" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0005970 ! brain commissure
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

