[Term]
id: FBbt:00100480
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn9 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron whose cell body lies in the lateral cell body region. The axon of Lcn9 fasciculates in the anterior optic tract with Lcn6 and terminate in the central part of the dorsal-posterior ventrolateral protocerebrum. Dendrites arborize in lobula layers 3, 4, 5 and 6." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC9" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100481
name: adult antennal lobe projection neuron VM3 adPN (Drosophila)
def: "Antennal lobe projection neuron from the ad neuroblast lineage (embryonic born) whose dendrites innervate only antennal lobe glomerulus VM3. Neurons of this class are born during the 17th and 19th divisions of the neuroblast ALad1 (FBbt:00067346) during embryogenesis (Yu et al., 2010)." [doi:10.1371/journal.pbio.1000461.g004, FlyBase:FBrf0183938, FlyBase:FBrf0211729]
synonym: "VM3 adPN" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003991 ! unilateral ACT relay interneuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007456 ! persistent antennal lobe projection neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100368 ! adult uniglomerular antennal lobe projection neuron adPN (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100482
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn10 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron whose cell body lies in the lateral cell body region. Its axon crosses ipsilaterally along the anterior optic tract, projecting to the optic tubercle. It arborizes in lobula layers 3, 4, 5 and 6." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC10" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "lobular columnar neuron Lcn10" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100483
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn11 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron whose cell body lies in the dorsal area of the lateral cell body region. It arborizes in lobula layers 2, 3 and 4, and terminates in the posteriolateral part of the ventrolateral protocerebrum. There are 36-40 cells in this class." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC11" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100484
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn12 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron whose cell body lies in the anterior-ventral area of the lateral cell body region. It has synaptic varicosities in lobula layers 3 and 4, and terminates in the ventrolateral protocerebrum. There are 30-35 cells in this class." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC12" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100485
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn13 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron that arborizes in lobula layers 3, 4 and 5, and terminates in the posteriolateral protocerebrum. There are 16-17 cells in this class, and they have their cell bodies in the anterior ventral area of the lateral cell body region." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC13" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100486
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn14 (Drosophila)
def: "An extrinsic columnar neuron that projects across the great commissure and contacts the surface of the lobula, but does not penetrate into any of its layers. There are 32-38 neurons in this group, and they have their cell bodies in the mid-dorsal area of the lateral cell body region." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LC14" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003870 ! lobula columnar neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007407 ! great commissural interneuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100487
name: lobula tangential neuron Lt11 (Drosophila)
def: "A lobula tangential neuron whose cell body is located in the anterior dorsal area of the lateral cell body region. It forms varicosities in lobula layers 3, 4 and 5, and in the ventrolateral protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "lobular tangential neuron Lt11" EXACT []
synonym: "LT11" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003859 ! lobula tangential neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100488
name: lobula tangential neuron Lt12 (Drosophila)
def: "A lobula tangential neuron whose cell body is located in the anterior area of the lateral cell body region. The cell body fiber bifurcates at the neck of the lobula. The branch towards the lobula arborizes at the posterior edge of the lobula and enters the neuropil in lobula layer 4. The branch towards the central brain projects along the lobula/lobula-plate bundle and terminates in the medial ventrolateral protocerebrum." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LT12" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003859 ! lobula tangential neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100489
name: lobula tangential neuron Lt31 (Drosophila)
def: "A lobula tangential neuron whose cell body is located in the central brain cortex, posterior to the posterior lateral protocerebrum (plpr). The cell body fiber runs anteriorly through the plpr neuropil and bifurcates in the ventrolateral protocerebrum. The lateral branch makes a turn and runs ventroposterior towards the neck of the lobula. From there the neuron forms extensive tree-like branches in lobula layer 4. The medial branch makes a right-angle turn to run ventroposterior towards the posterior plpr. It forms terminals in the area that is close to the position of the cell body. There is only a single neuron in this class." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LT31" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003859 ! lobula tangential neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00100490
name: lobula tangential neuron Lt32 (Drosophila)
def: "A lobula tangential neuron whose cell body is located lateral to the esophageal foramen. The cell body fiber runs posteriorly along the esophagus and turns upwards near the posterior end of the brain where it forms a Y-shaped branch. One branch runs laterally to project to the lobula, and the other crosses the midline to innervate the contralateral lobula. Along the trajectory towards the lobula, the fiber forms another collateral branch which innervates the posterior lateral protocerebrum. The main branch reaches the lobula and forms extensive tree-like arborizations with varicosities in lobula layers 5 and 6. There is only one neuron per brain hemisphere in this group." [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
synonym: "LT32" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0193607]
is_a: FBbt:00003859 ! lobula tangential neuron (Drosophila)

