[Term]
id: FBbt:00110065
name: lamina wide-field cell Lawf2 (Drosophila)
def: "An intrinsic columnar neuron of the visual system whose cell body is located in the medulla cortex and that has a main projection into the lamina making wide-field arborizations in the distal lamina, innervating 28 cartridges. These neurons also arborize in the medulla (Hasegawa et al., 2011). In the M1 layer, the branches are large and overlapping, encompassing around 120 cartridges. In medulla layers M8 to M10 the branches are smaller, encompassing around 17 cartridges and show less overlap. Putative cholinergic presynaptic sites are observed in the lamina." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020, FlyBase:FBrf0225131]
synonym: "Lawf2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00007173 ! cholinergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007578 ! intrinsic columnar neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003708 ! lamina (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110066
name: proximal medullary amacrine neuron Pm3 (Drosophila)
def: "Proximal medullary amacrine neuron that branches at the proximal surface of the medulla, with both branches forming a broad terminal arbor in medulla layers M8 to M10 (Hasegawa et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "Pm3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003832 ! proximal medullary amacrine neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110067
name: transmedullary Y neuron Tm27Y (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary Y neuron that terminates in lobula layer 4 and lobula plate. It displays arborizations in medulla layers M1, M4, M5, M8, M9 and M10 (Hasegawa et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "Tm27Y" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003817 ! transmedullary Y neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003748 ! medulla (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110068
name: distal medullary amacrine neuron Dm8a (Drosophila)
def: "Distal medullary wide-field amacrine neuron that branches extensively in medulla layer M6 and extends small centrifugal processes to medulla layer M4 (Gao et al., 2008, Hasegawa et al., 2011). In medulla layer M6, it extends over 14-15 columns in both the anterior-posterior and dorsal-ventral axes (Jagadish et al., 2014). In layer M6 it is postsynaptic to photoreceptor cell R7 and R8 (Jagadish et al., 2014) and presynaptic to Tm5 (Gao et al., 2008). It also makes synaptic contacts with Tm9 (in M4) (Gao et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0204652, FlyBase:FBrf0206213, FlyBase:FBrf0213020, FlyBase:FBrf0225846]
synonym: "Dm8" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0049410]
synonym: "Dm8a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003767 ! distal medullary amacrine neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100291 ! glutamatergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110137 ! wide-field columnar neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110069
name: distal medullary amacrine neuron Dm8b (Drosophila)
def: "Distal medullary amacrine neuron that branches in medulla layers M6, M7 and M8 (Hasegawa et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "Dm8b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003767 ! distal medullary amacrine neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110070
name: medullary intrinsic neuron Mi10b (Drosophila)
def: "Medullary intrinsic neuron with arborizations in medulla layers M1, M2, M4-M10 (Hasegawa et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "Mi10b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003775 ! medullary intrinsic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110071
name: transmedullary neuron Tm3b (Drosophila)
def: "Transmedullary neuron that terminates in lobula layers 1 and 4 with bleb-like terminal arborizations. It has fine arborizations in medulla layers M1, M4, and M5, and has bleb-type arborization in medulla layers M1, M4, M9 and M10 (Fischbach and Dittrich, 1989). It has a small branch at medulla layer M8 that projects towards medulla layer M10 (Hasegawa et al., 2011)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
synonym: "Tm3b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0213020]
is_a: FBbt:00003788 ! transmedullary neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110072
name: transmedullary neuron Tm5a (Drosophila)
def: "Subtype of the transmedullary neuron Tm5. It is very similar to the subtype Tm5b, differing from it by the size and shape of its arborization, which is very extensive in medulla layer M6. It receives synaptic contacts from photoreceptor cell R7 and laminar cell L3 (Gao et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0206213]
synonym: "Tm5b" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10157]
is_a: FBbt:00003793 ! transmedullary neuron Tm5 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110073
name: transmedullary neuron Tm5b (Drosophila)
def: "Subtype of the transmedullary neuron Tm5. It is very similar to the subtype Tm5a, differing from it by the size and shape of its arborization, which extends across distal and proximal medulla layers (Gao et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0206213]
synonym: "Tm5b" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10157]
is_a: FBbt:00003793 ! transmedullary neuron Tm5 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110074
name: transmedullary neuron Tm5c (Drosophila)
def: "Subtype of the transmedullary neuron Tm5. It differs from the subtypes Tm5a and Tm5b by its arborization pattern. It has dendritic terminals in medulla layer M1 and projects to lobula layers 4 and 5. It is a glutamatergic neuron (Gao et al., 2008)." [FlyBase:FBrf0049410, FlyBase:FBrf0206213]
synonym: "Tm5c" RELATED [FlyBrain_NDB:10157]
is_a: FBbt:00003793 ! transmedullary neuron Tm5 (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00100291 ! glutamatergic neuron (Drosophila)

