[Term]
id: FBbt:00110107
name: adult dorsomedial neurosecretory cell (Drosophila)
def: "Neurosecretory cell of the pars intercerebralis that innervate the corpus cardiacum and corpus allatum, and branch before exiting the brain. It extends thin branches laterally in the dorsal protocerebrum, shorter branches along the cell neurites in the dorsal part of the median bundle and extensive arborizations in the tritocerebrum (Enell et al., 2010). A single axon extends ventrally, branching just before exiting the brain, and emerging as two branches that follow the aorta and innervate the corpus cardiacum in the ring gland and the hypocerebral ganglion, near the cardiac valve of the midgut. One of the branches follows the stalk of the crop, whilst the other bifurcates, with each of these branches extending along each side of the midgut (Cao and Brown, 2001). There are seven of these cells from each hemisphere with their cell bodies clustering in the pars intercerebralis at late pupal stages (Cao and Brown, 2001, Broughton et al., 2005, Cao et al., 2014)." [FlyBase:FBrf0134726, FlyBase:FBrf0136823, FlyBase:FBrf0184236, FlyBase:FBrf0212696, FlyBase:FBrf0224974]
synonym: "insulin producing cell" EXACT []
synonym: "IPC cell" EXACT []
synonym: "m-NSC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0184236]
synonym: "median neurosecretory cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0184236]
synonym: "MNC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0136823]
synonym: "mNSC" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00004011 ! dorsomedial neurosecretory cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003700 ! adult pars intercerebralis (Drosophila)

