name: VUM motorneuron (Drosophila)
def: "Ventral unpaired median motorneuron that are part of the median neuroblast lineage that innervate the larval body wall muscles. There are three of these cells per segment. They are modulatory motor neurons, with one VUM motor neuron innervating the dorsal, and the other the ventral ISN innervated muscles; the third VUM neuron innervates the SN innervated lateral muscles." [FlyBase:FBrf0072659, FlyBase:FBrf0112030, FlyBase:FBrf0180108, FlyBase:FBrf0208790]
