[Term]
id: FBbt:00110626
name: nervus corporis cardiaci II (Drosophila)
def: "Bilaterally paired nerve bundle that connects the larval ring gland to the brain. It comprises the axons of neurons from the neurosecretory cells of the pars lateralis. After leaving the pars lateralis, the axons pass the mushroom body calyx and peduncle medially, before reaching the medial edge of the protocerebrum where it joins the nervus corporis cardiaci I (NccI), continuing towards the ring gland (de Velasco et al., 2007; Hartenstein, 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0134726, FlyBase:FBrf0193772]
synonym: "NCC" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
synonym: "NccII" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001911 ! insect embryonic/larval nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110627
name: nervus corporis cardiaci III (Drosophila)
def: "Bilaterally paired nerve bundle that connects the larval ring gland to the brain. It comprises the axons of neurons from the neurosecretory cells of the tritocerebrum and subesophageal ganglion (Hartenstein, 2006)." [FlyBase:FBrf0194938]
synonym: "NCC" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
synonym: "NccIII" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134726]
is_a: UBERON:0001021 ! nerve
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001911 ! insect embryonic/larval nervous system

