[Term]
id: FBbt:00110662
name: adult posterior abdominal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron located in the posterior region of the abdominal ganglion. These neurons are sexually dimorphic, fasciculate with the abdominal nerve trunk and innervate the reproductive organs of the adult. These neurons are generated by post-embryonic neurogenesis in late L3 larvae." [FlyBase:FBrf0134722, FlyBase:FBrf0135850, FlyBase:FBrf0179138, FlyBase:FBrf0222499]
synonym: "s-Abg neuron" NARROW [FlyBase:FBrf0135850]
is_a: FBbt:00001987 ! abdominal neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003023 ! adult abdomen

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110663
name: adult male posterior abdominal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Serotonergic neuron of the adult male that is located in the posterior region of the abdominal ganglion. It fasciculates with the abdominal nerve trunk and innervates the testicular duct, seminal vesicles, accessory glands and an anterior part of the ejaculatory duct. There are 8 to 10 of these neurons, in a dorsal cluster." [FlyBase:FBrf0134722, FlyBase:FBrf0135850, FlyBase:FBrf0179138, FlyBase:FBrf0222499]
synonym: "s-Abg neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0134722, FlyBase:FBrf0135850]
synonym: "SAbg neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222499]
is_a: FBbt:00110662 ! adult posterior abdominal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110975 ! serotonergic abdominal neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003101 ! male organism

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110664
name: adult female posterior abdominal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Glutamatergic neuron of the adult female that is located in the posterior region of the abdominal ganglion. It fasciculates with the abdominal nerve trunk and innervates the oviduct. There are 3 to 4 of these neurons, in a ventral cluster." [FlyBase:FBrf0222499]
synonym: "s-Abg neuron" RELATED [FlyBase:FBrf0222499]
is_a: FBbt:00100291 ! glutamatergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110662 ! adult posterior abdominal ganglion neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003100 ! female organism

