[Term]
id: FBbt:00110890
name: adult midgut region R1 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the adult midgut located in the thorax. It ends at a position that corresponds to an anatomical hub where the midgut, the crop, and the Malpighian tubules physically interact. It can be subdivided into 2 subregions: R1a, composed of flat enterocytes, and R1b composed of long folded enterocytes." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
