id: FBbt:00110892
name: adult midgut region R1b (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the posterior end of the adult midgut region R1. It is composed of long enterocytes, with an extended labyrinth and a highly folded lumen." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "R1b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110890 ! adult midgut region R1 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110893
name: adult midgut region R2 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the adult midgut located in the abdomen that is dorsally located and that falls back ventrally at the posterior part. It can be divided into 3 subregions, based on histology and gene expression. It is composed of enterocytes with a typical columnar morphology." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "anterior adult midgut" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "R2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110888 ! adult midgut region (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110894
name: adult midgut region R2a (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the anterior end of the adult midgut region R2. It is composed of enterocytes containing lipid vesicles with an apical extrusion and a typical columnar morphology. It is distinguished from region R2b by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut A2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut anterior 2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R2a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110893 ! adult midgut region R2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110895
name: adult midgut region R2b (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the middle of the adult midgut region R2. It is composed of enterocytes containing lipid vesicles with an apical extrusion and a typical columnar morphology. It is distinguished from region R2a by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut A2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut anterior 2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R2b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110893 ! adult midgut region R2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110896
name: adult midgut region R2c (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the posterior of the adult midgut region R2. It is composed of enterocytes containing less lipid vesicles than in regions R2a or R2b, with a typical columnar morphology, and with cells not as long in R2a or R2b." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut A3 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut anterior 3 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R2c" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110893 ! adult midgut region R2 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110897
name: adult midgut region R3 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the adult midgut that contains the copper cells. This region initiates a retrograde folding of the midgut, (from posterior to anterior), and it follows a ventral-dorsal axis. It can be subdivided into an anterior section containing the copper cells (R3ab) and a posterior one with large flat cells (R3c)." [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult middle midgut" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "R3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110888 ! adult midgut region (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110898
name: adult midgut anterior region R3a (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the anterior end of the adult midgut region R3. It is composed of copper cells (cuprophilic cells) interspersed with interstitial cells. The posterior region R3b is distinguishable from R3a by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut copper cells region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "CCR" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "copper cell region of the adult midgut" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "R3a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "region B of the adult middle midgut" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
is_a: FBbt:00110897 ! adult midgut region R3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110899
name: adult midgut anterior region R3b (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the middle zone of the adult midgut region R3. It is composed of copper cells (cuprophilic cells) interspersed with interstitial cells. The anterior region R3a is distinguishable from R3b by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut copper cells region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "CCR" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "copper cell region of the adult midgut" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "R3b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "region C of the adult middle midgut" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
is_a: FBbt:00110897 ! adult midgut region R3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110900
name: adult midgut posterior region R3c (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the posterior zone of the adult midgut region R3, located posterior to the copper cell region. It is composed by large flat cells." [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "large flat cell region of the adult midgut" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "LFC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R3c" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "region D of the adult middle midgut" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
is_a: FBbt:00110897 ! adult midgut region R3 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110901
name: adult midgut region R4 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the adult midgut that forms a complex loop and that re-orients the gut towards the posterior part of the abdomen and ends ventrally. It can be subdivided into an anterior part containing an extremely folded epithelium (R4a) and two posterior regions composed of cells with short apical protrusions resulting in an enlarged lumen (R4b and R4c)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "R4" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110888 ! adult midgut region (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110902
name: adult midgut region R4a (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the anterior zone of the adult midgut region R4. It contains a highly folded lumen, with enterocytes sometimes organized in multilayers, and containing lipid vesicles." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut P1 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut posterior 1 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R4a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110901 ! adult midgut region R4 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110903
name: adult midgut region R4b (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the middle of the adult midgut region R4. It is composed of enterocytes with small apical protrusions. It can be distinguished from the posterior region R4c by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut P1 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut posterior 1 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R4b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110901 ! adult midgut region R4 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110904
name: adult midgut region R4c (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the posterior end of the adult midgut region R4. It is composed of enterocytes with small apical protrusions. It can be distinguished from the anterior region R4b by gene expression." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut P2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut posterior 2 region" BROAD [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R4c" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110901 ! adult midgut region R4 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110905
name: adult midgut region R5 (Drosophila)
def: "Region of the adult midgut that corresponds to an ascending segment of the midgut that joins the hindgut. It is composed of an anterior region containing enterocytes with a typical columnar morphology, containing lipid vesicles and a posterior region which contains fewer cells with a smoothed brush border." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "R5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110888 ! adult midgut region (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110906
name: adult midgut region R5a (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the anterior end of the adult midgut region R5. It is composed of enterocytes of a typical columnar morphology, containing lipid vesicles." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut P3 region" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut posterior 3 region" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R5a" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110905 ! adult midgut region R5 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110907
name: adult midgut region R5b (Drosophila)
def: "Subregion at the posterior end of the adult midgut region R5. It contains fewer enterocytes, with a smoothed brush border." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "adult midgut P4 region" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "adult midgut posterior 4 region" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0222542]
synonym: "R5b" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00110905 ! adult midgut region R5 (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110908
name: adult copper cell (Drosophila)
def: "Specialised cell of the adult midgut found in the anterior and middle midgut sections of region R3 (R3a and R3b, copper cell region). It secretes acid and accumulates copper. They show a distinct apical invagination, basally located nuclei, numerous mitochondria and a deeply invaginated apical membrane covered with long microvilli. Interstitial cells arch over the apex of the copper cell, forming a narrow channel that connects the apical invagination of the copper cell to the gut lumen. The highly folded area of apicolateral contact between copper and interstitial cells contains smooth septate junctions." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0139611, FlyBase:FBrf0174753, FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "adult cuprophilic cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0139611]
is_a: FBbt:00005782 ! copper cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110898 ! adult midgut anterior region R3a (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110899 ! adult midgut anterior region R3b (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110909
name: adult midgut interstitial cell (Drosophila)
def: "Interstitial cell of the adult midgut. It is found in the anterior midgut subregions of region R3 (R3a and R3b, copper cell region), interspersed with copper cells. They have apically localized nuclei, short microvilli in the apical membrane and a broad apical profile. The interstitial cell arches over the apex of the copper cell, forming a narrow channel that connects the apical invagination of the copper cell to the gut lumen. The highly folded area of apicolateral contact between copper and interstitial cells contains smooth septate junctions." [FlyBase:FBrf0064792, FlyBase:FBrf0139611, FlyBase:FBrf0174753, FlyBase:FBrf0216495, FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
is_a: FBbt:00005783 ! midgut interstitial cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110898 ! adult midgut anterior region R3a (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110899 ! adult midgut anterior region R3b (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110910
name: midgut large flat cell (Drosophila)
def: "Large flat cell of the middle midgut, located posteriorly to the copper cell region. It has a large nuclei." [FlyBase:FBrf0013091, FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "LFC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0013091, FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
is_a: CL:0002251 ! epithelial cell of alimentary canal
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001045 ! midgut

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110911
name: embryonic/larval midgut large flat cell (Drosophila)
def: "Large flat cell of the embryonic/larval lower middle midgut, located posteriorly to the copper cell region." [FlyBase:FBrf0013091]
synonym: "LFC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0013091]
is_a: FBbt:00001886 ! embryonic/larval midgut cell (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110910 ! midgut large flat cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001884 ! mid embryonic/larval midgut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110912
name: adult midgut large flat cell (Drosophila)
def: "Large flat cell of the adult midgut region R3c. It is located posteriorly to the copper cell region." [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
synonym: "LFC" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216495]
is_a: FBbt:00110910 ! midgut large flat cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00110900 ! adult midgut posterior region R3c (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110913
name: adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)
def: "Constriction of the adult midgut. There are 6 of these that delimit 5 distinct regions." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure
relationship: part_of FBbt:00007513 ! adult gut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110914
name: adult midgut constriction R0-R1 (Drosophila)
def: "Constriction of the adult midgut that separates the endodermal part of the proventriculus (cardia) (R0) from the anterior part of the midgut (R1)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "boundary R0-R1" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "BR0-R1" EXACT [http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: FBbt:00110913 ! adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110915
name: adult midgut constriction R1-R2 (Drosophila)
def: "Constriction of the adult midgut that is at the border between the thorax and abdomen, where the crop, the Malpighian tubules and the midgut interact. It separates region 1 (R1) from region (R2)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "boundary R1-R2" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "BR1-R2" EXACT [http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: FBbt:00110913 ! adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110916
name: adult midgut constriction R2-R3 (Drosophila)
def: "One of the two large constrictions of the adult midgut. It corresponds to an area where the midgut abruptly folds and turns up. It is the most ventral point of the midgut. The area is composed of a range of enterocytes with distinct identities. It separates region 2 (R2) from region 3 (R3)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "boundary R2-R3" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "BR2-R3" EXACT [http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: FBbt:00110913 ! adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110917
name: adult midgut constriction R3-R4 (Drosophila)
def: "One of the two large constrictions of the adult midgut. It corresponds to an area where the midgut abruptly folds and turns up. It is the most dorsal point of the midgut. The cells in this area accumulate ferritin. It separates region 3 (R3) from region 4 (R4)." [FlyBase:FBrf0008422, FlyBase:FBrf0221749, FlyBase:FBrf0222542, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "boundary R3-R4" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "BR3-R4" EXACT [http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: FBbt:00110913 ! adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110918
name: adult midgut constriction R4-R5 (Drosophila)
def: "Constriction of the adult midgut. It corresponds to the beginning of the midgut ascension towards the hindgut, where the radius of the midgut uniformly decreases. It separates region 4 (R4) from region 5 (R5)." [FlyBase:FBrf0221749, http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
synonym: "boundary R4-R5" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0221749]
synonym: "BR4-R5" EXACT [http://flygut.epfl.ch/]
is_a: FBbt:00110913 ! adult midgut constriction (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110919
name: adult hindgut muscle (Drosophila)
def: "Muscle of the adult hindgut." [FBC:MMC]
synonym: "adult intestine muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007735]
is_a: UBERON:0001135 ! smooth muscle tissue
relationship: part_of FBbt:00003143 ! adult hindgut (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110920
name: larval secretory cell of the proventriculus (Drosophila)
def: "Secretory cell of the larval proventriculus that synthesizes and secretes the peritrophic membrane. They are part of the outer layer of the proventriculus, near the anterior end. They have large secretory granules and a highly polarized secretory apparatus." [FlyBase:FBrf0010887, FlyBase:FBrf0225140]
synonym: "PR cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0225140]
is_a: FBbt:00100318 ! somatic cell (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00001874 ! embryonic/larval proventriculus outer layer (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110921
name: larval Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Larval neuron that expresses Hugin (FBgn0028374). These neurons have their soma in the subesophageal ganglion and can be divided into 4 subsets depending on their innervation: protocerebrum, ventral nerve cord, corpora cardiaca in the ring gland and the pharynx. There is a cluster of 20 hugin neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0188215, FlyBase:FBrf0200884]
synonym: "larval hugin cell" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00001446 ! embryonic/larval neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110925 ! Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001919 ! embryonic/larval central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110922
name: larval Hugin neuron of the protocerebrum (Drosophila)
def: "Larval neuron that expresses Hugin (FBgn0028374) and that arborizes the protocerebrum. This neuron arborizes the ipsilateral or both hemispheres of the protocerebrum and the ventrolateral region of the esophagus foramen. It is likely that there are 8 of these neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0188215, FlyBase:FBrf0200884]
synonym: "larval hugin cell of the protocerebrum" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00001446 ! embryonic/larval neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110925 ! Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110923
name: larval Hugin neuron of the ventral nerve cord (Drosophila)
def: "Larval neuron that expresses Hugin (FBgn0028374) and that projects to the ventral nerve cord. This neuron has a long projection travelling down contralaterally along the lateral neuropil border of the ventral nerve cord. Three or four shorter fibers project on either side of the midline. Two fibers project anteriorly and pass along either side of the esophagus foramen, terminating at the medial end of the protocerebrum. It is likely that there are 4 of these neurons." [FlyBase:FBrf0188215, FlyBase:FBrf0200884]
synonym: "larval hugin cell of the ventral nerve cord" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00001446 ! embryonic/larval neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00110925 ! Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001919 ! embryonic/larval central nervous system

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110924
name: adult Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Adult neuron that expresses Hugin (FBgn0028374). These neurons have their soma in the gnathal ganglion and arborize the thoracico-abdominal ganglion, corpus cardiacum and the protocerebrum. The latter neurites traverse along the median neurosecretory cells in the pars intercerebralis and terminate near the mushroom bodies." [FlyBase:FBrf0188215]
synonym: "adult hugin cell" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: FBbt:00110925 ! Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110925
name: Hugin neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Neuron that expresses hugin (FBgn0028374). These neurons have their soma in the subesophageal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0188215, FlyBase:FBrf0200884]
synonym: "hugin cell" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00004101 ! peptidergic neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110926
name: penis retractor muscle (Drosophila)
def: "Muscle of the adult male 9th sternite that originates from the inner side of the basal part of the sternite and inserts upon the base of the penis. There is a pair of these muscles." [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
synonym: "aedeagus retractor muscle" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0007734]
is_a: FBbt:00003551 ! ejaculatory bulb muscle (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of FBbt:00004852 ! penis (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110927
name: larval dopaminergic DM1a neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Subtype of the dopaminergic neuron of the DM cluster of the larval brain. Its arborizations are restricted to the ipsilateral side. The primary neurite extends ventrally into the lower part of the ipsilateral brain lobe. There is one of these neurons per hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
synonym: "DM1a neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
is_a: FBbt:00110331 ! larval dopaminergic DM neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110928
name: larval dopaminergic DM1b neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Subtype of the dopaminergic neuron of the DM cluster of the larval brain. Its arborizations are restricted to the ipsilateral side. The primary neurite extends ventrally and bifurcates in the basolateral protocerebrum. One small axon innervates the basomedial protocerebrum. It densely innervates the mushroom body spur, with one single fiber extending into the lateral appendix. One axon projects further ventrally and branches in the subesophageal ganglion and dorsal thoracic ganglion. There are 3 of these neurons per hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0208252, FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
synonym: "DM1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0208252]
synonym: "DM1b neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0216686]
is_a: FBbt:00110331 ! larval dopaminergic DM neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110929
name: alpha/beta core Kenyon cell (Drosophila)
def: "Alpha/beta mushroom body neuron that has dendrites in the main calyx, with their axons occupying the core layer of the peduncle, alpha and beta lobes. They can be morphologically subdivided into inner and outer core cells, although the border between these regions is not well defined. There are around 400 neurons in each hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0162233, FlyBase:FBrf0174482, FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta c Kenyon cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta core neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "mushroom body alpha/beta core neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100248 ! alpha/beta Kenyon cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110930
name: alpha/beta surface Kenyon cell (Drosophila)
def: "Alpha/beta mushroom body neuron that has dendrites in the main calyx and projects axons to the surface layer of the alpha and beta lobes, where they form a continuous layer surrounding the alpha/beta core. There are around 500 neurons in each hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0162233, FlyBase:FBrf0174482, FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta s Kenyon cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta surface neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "mushroom body alpha/beta surface neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100248 ! alpha/beta Kenyon cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110931
name: alpha/beta posterior Kenyon cell (Drosophila)
def: "Alpha/beta mushroom body neuron that has dendrites in the accessory calyx. It occupies the outermost stratum and the posterior layer at the tip of the alpha and beta lobes. In the shaft region of the alpha lobe, alpha/beta posterior Kenyon cell form mesh-like arrangements, with one or two nodes where axons appear to gather. In the pedunculus, their axons form several bundles, which run through the outermost layer of the central zone. In the calyx, the dendrites run along the surface of the main calyx without forming any arborization. They are the first-born Kenyon cells. There are around 90 neurons in each hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0201372, FlyBase:FBrf0205263, FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta p Kenyon cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "alpha/beta pioneer neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0218860]
synonym: "alpha/beta posterior neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100248 ! alpha/beta Kenyon cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110932
name: gamma dorsal Kenyon cell (Drosophila)
def: "Gamma mushroom body neuron. Its dendritic arbor occupies the ventral accessory calyx, and its axon extends to the gamma lobe, taking the most peripheral layer in the pedunculus, the ventral anterior layers in gamma lobe slices 1 to 4, terminating in the dorsal region in slice 5. There are around 75 neurons of this type per hemisphere." [FlyBase:FBrf0207600, FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "gamma d Kenyon cell" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0227179]
synonym: "gamma d neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "gamma dorsal neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "mushroom body gamma dorsal neuron" EXACT []
is_a: FBbt:00100247 ! gamma Kenyon cell (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110933
name: lobula columnar neuron Lcn10A (Drosophila)
