is_a: FBbt:00001987 ! abdominal neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110976
name: serotonergic abdominal medial neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell body is located medially in one of two clusters either side of the ventral midline in the larval abdominal segments A1 to A7 or adult abdominal neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551, FlyBase:FBrf0207378]
is_a: FBbt:00110975 ! serotonergic abdominal neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110977
name: serotonergic abdominal lateral neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Serotonergic neuron whose cell body is located laterally in one of two clusters either side of the ventral midline in the larval abdominal segments A1 to A7 or adult abdominal neuromere." [FlyBase:FBrf0048551, FlyBase:FBrf0207378]
is_a: FBbt:00110975 ! serotonergic abdominal neuron (Drosophila)

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110978
name: antennal mechanosensory and motor center D1 projection neuron (Drosophila)
def: "Projection neuron whose cell body is located in the posterior brain, close to the superior posterior slope. It projects ipsilaterally to the posterior side of AMMC zone D, branching to arborize zones B, C D and E. It then passes through the posterior side of the gnathal ganglion, extending into the dorsolateral region of the thoracico-abdominal ganglion." [FlyBase:FBrf0225118]
synonym: "AMMC-D1 neuron" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0225118]
synonym: "AMMC-D1 PN" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0225118]
is_a: FBbt:00007392 ! projection neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6003624 ! adult brain

[Term]
id: FBbt:00110979
name: larval mushroom body anterior paired lateral cell (Drosophila)
def: "Intrinsic GABAergic neuron of the larval mushroom body whose large cell body is located ventromedially. It extends one primary process dorsally that bifurcates at the level of the pedunculus, sending one secondary process to innervate the calyx and another one to the lobes. The calyx process branches into fine processes that terminates in boutons. The lobe secondary process runs along the lower pedunculus and terminates in fine branches in the terminal regions of the medial lobe, the proximal region of the vertical lobe and an area connecting the lower pedunculus and vertical lobe. Pre-synaptic terminals are mainly found in the calyx, whereas dendrites are observed in the lobes." [FlyBase:FBrf0224838]
synonym: "larval APL" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0224838]
is_a: CL:0000397 ! ganglion interneuron
is_a: CL:0000402 ! CNS interneuron
is_a: CL:0011005 ! GABAergic interneuron
is_a: FBbt:00001446 ! embryonic/larval neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007228 ! GABAergic neuron (Drosophila)
is_a: FBbt:00007484 ! mushroom body intrinsic neuron (Drosophila)
relationship: part_of UBERON:6001920 ! insect embryonic/larval brain

