[Term]
id: PORO:0000000
name: sponge cell
is_a: GO:0005623 ! cell
relationship: part_of PORO:0000001 ! sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000001
name: sponge
def: "Sponge bodies consist of jelly-like mesohyl sandwiched between two thin layers of cells. While all animals have unspecialized cells that can transform into specialized cells, sponges are unique in having some specialized cells that can transform into other types, often migrating between the main cell layers and the mesohyl in the process. Sponges do not have nervous, digestive or circulatory systems. Instead, most rely on maintaining a constant water flow through their bodies to obtain food and oxygen and to remove wastes, and the shapes of their bodies are adapted to maximize the efficiency of the water flow. All are sessile aquatic animals and, although there are freshwater species, the great majority are marine (salt water) species, ranging from tidal zones to depths exceeding 8,800 metres (5.5 mi)" [Wikipedia:Sponge]
is_a: UBERON:0000468 ! multi-cellular organism

[Term]
id: PORO:0000002
name: mesohyl
def: "An extracellular matrix enclosed by pinacoderm and choanoderm, the mesohyl is composed primarily of galectin, collagen, fibronectin-like molecules, dermatopontin, and other polypeptides. The mesohyl contains cells (microbial and eukaryotic) and skeletal elements (collagen, spongin, chitin, and/or minerals). (Boury-Esnault and Rützler 1997; Müller 2003)" []
synonym: "mesenchyme" RELATED DEPRECATED []
synonym: "mesoglea" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000700 ! body layer

[Term]
id: PORO:0000003
name: choanocyte
def: "A cell that lines the interior of Asconoid, syconoid and leuconoid body type sponges that contain a central flagellum surrounded by a collar of microvilli which are connected by a thin membrane. The choanocyte is ovoid, with one end adjacent to the mesohyl (in some species). It is the closest family member to the free-living ancestor called choanoflagellate. The flagellae beat regularly, creating a water flow across the microvilli which can then filter nutrients and other food from the water taken from the collar of the sponge. Food particles are then phagocytosed by the cell. Choanocytes are found dotting the surface of the spongocoel in asconoid sponges and the radial canals in syconoid sponges, but they comprise entirely the chambers in leuconoid sponges. By cooperatively moving their flagella, choanocytes generate a flow of water through the sponges pores, into the spongocoel, and out through the osculum. This improves both respiratory and digestive functions for the sponge, pulling in oxygen and nutrients and allowing a rapid expulsion of carbon dioxide and other waste products. Although all cells in a sponge are capable of living on their own, choanocytes carry out most of the sponge's ingestion, passing digested materials to the amoebocytes for delivery to other cells." [ISBN:0030229073, Wikipedia:Choanocyte]
synonym: "collar cell" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000914 ! flagellated cell
relationship: part_of PORO:0000022 ! spongocoel lining

[Term]
id: PORO:0000005
name: lophocyte
def: "amoeba-like cells that move slowly through the mesohyl and secrete collagen fibres." []
is_a: PORO:0000222 ! collencyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000007
name: rhabdiferous cell
def: "Large cell with numerous rod-like inclu sions parallel to the long axis of the cell containing acid mucopolysaccharides" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000011
name: sclerocyte
def: "spicule secreting cells, found in sponges. They secrete calcareous or siliceous spicules which are found in the mesohyl layer of sponges. The sclerocytes produce spicules via formation of a cellular triad" [Wikipedia:Sclerocyte]
is_a: PORO:0000012 ! secretory cell
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000016 ! archaeocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000012
name: secretory cell
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000013
name: spongocyte
def: "In addition to or instead of sclerocytes, demosponges have spongocytes that secrete a form of collagen that polymerizes into spongin, a thick fibrous material that stiffens the mesohyl." []
is_a: PORO:0000012 ! secretory cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000014
name: myocyte
def: "conduct signals and cause parts of the animal to contract. They are assumed to regulate the flow of water by increasing or decreasing the diameter of these openings to the aquiferous system." []
synonym: "muscle cell" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell
relationship: part_of PORO:0000002 ! mesohyl
relationship: part_of PORO:0000143 ! aquiferous system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000015
name: gray cell
def: "cells that acts as sponges' equivalent of an immune system." []
synonym: "immune cell" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000016
name: archaeocyte
def: "amoeba-like large cells with large nuclei that are totipotent. They also have important roles in feeding and in clearing debris that block the ostia." [ISBN:0030229073]
synonym: "amoebocyte" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000017
name: spicule
def: "siliceous or calcareous entities that form the mineral skeleton of a sponge" []
relationship: part_of PORO:0000002 ! mesohyl
relationship: part_of PORO:0002042 ! mineral skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000018
name: osculum
def: "an excretory structure in the living sponge, a large opening to the outside through which the current of water exits after passing through the spongocoel. Wastes diffuse into the water and the water exits through the osculum at a velocity of nearly 8.4 cm/second, carrying away with it the sponge's wastes. The size of the osculum is regulated by the myocyte. Its size, in turn, determines the amount of water flowing through the sponge." [Wikipedia:Osculum]
is_a: PORO:0000019 ! immaterial anatomical entity

[Term]
id: PORO:0000019
name: immaterial anatomical entity
is_a: UBERON:0001062 ! anatomical entity

[Term]
id: PORO:0000020
name: spongeocoel
def: "large, central cavity of sponges. Water enters the spongocoel through hundreds of tiny pores (Ostia) and exits through the larger opening (osculum). Depending on the body plan of the sponge (which can be asconoid, syconoid, or leuconoid), the spongocoel could be a simple interior space of the sponge or a complexly branched inner structure. Regardless of body plan or class, the spongocoel is lined with choanocytes, which have flagella that push water through the spongocoel, creating a current." []
synonym: "atrium" RELATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "cloaca" EXACT [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "gastal cavity" EXACT [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000019 ! immaterial anatomical entity

[Term]
id: PORO:0000021
name: ostium
def: "Any opening in the exopinacoderm through which water enters the sponge." []
synonym: "incurrent pore" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000035 ! pore

[Term]
id: PORO:0000022
name: spongocoel lining
relationship: part_of PORO:0000020 ! spongeocoel

[Term]
id: PORO:0000023
name: pinacocyte
def: "flat cells found on the outermost layer of sponges. They can expand and contract to slightly alter the size of the sponge, and can also produce collagen. Delimits the sponge from the external milieu and always only in a layer one-cell deep" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus, Wikipedia:Pinacocyte]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell
relationship: part_of PORO:0000043 ! pinacoderm

[Term]
id: PORO:0000024
name: prosopyle
def: "a pore through which water is drawn from the outside into one of the saclike chambers formed by the evagination of the body wall." []
is_a: PORO:0000035 ! pore
relationship: part_of PORO:0000355 ! inhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000025
name: choanocyte chamber
def: "Any cavity lined by choanocytes and located between inhalant and exhalant systems[portol]. either the choanocyte-lined radial canal in syconoid, or the choanocyte-lined filter chamber in leuconoid[cjm]." []
synonym: "choanocyte lined chamber" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal
is_a: PORO:0000915 ! chamber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000026
name: asconoid sponge
def: "Asconoid is one of three possible body plans for sponges, which form the phylum Porifera in kingdom Animalia and subkingdom Parazoa which means that they do not have a definite body shape. The asconoid body plan is characterized by a stalk-like spongocoel surrounded by a single layer of choanocytes. These choanocytes are cells that have flagella, and the flagella beat to push water through the spongocoel, creating a current. At somewhat regular intervals along the lining of the spongocoel are openings called ostia (singular, ostium). These protrude through the outer layer of the sponge (somewhat like an epidermis, but not entirely like it, since this terminology implies germ layers, which sponges do not have). Finally, at the top of the sponge is the osculum, which is the final exit for water circulating through the sponge. This single layer of choanocytes limits the size of asconoids, with the largest having a diameter of only 1 mm. This is due to the surface area : mass ratio which would not allow an asconoid sponge of larger size sufficient nutrition." [Wikipedia:Asconoid]
is_a: PORO:0000001 ! sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000027
name: syconoid sponge
def: "Sponge in which the body wall is pleated. The inner pockets of the pleats are lined with choanocytes, which connect to the outer pockets of the pleats by ostia. This increase in the number of choanocytes and hence in pumping capacity enables syconoid sponges to grow up to a few centimeters in diameter" [Wikipedia:Sea_sponge]
is_a: PORO:0000001 ! sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000028
name: leuconoid sponge
def: "The \"leuconid\" pattern boosts pumping capacity further by filling the interior almost completely with mesohyl that contains a network of chambers lined with choanocytes and connected to each other and to the water intakes and outlet by tubes. Leuconid sponges grow to over 1 metre (3.3 ft) in diameter, and the fact that growth in any direction increases the number of choanocyte chambers enables them to take a wider range of forms, for example \"encrusting\" sponges whose shapes follow those of the surfaces to which they attach. All freshwater and most shallow-water marine sponges have leuconid bodies. The networks of water passages in glass sponges are similar to the leuconid structure." [Wikipedia:Sea_sponge]
is_a: PORO:0000001 ! sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000029
name: spongin
def: "Skeletal substance in Demospongiae made up of collagen microfibrils of ~10 fim diameter[portol]. a modified type of collagen protein, forms the fibrous skeleton of most organisms among the phylum Porifera, the sponges. Spongin gives a sponge its flexibility. True spongin is found only in members of the class Demospongiae" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus, Wikipedia:Spongin]
synonym: "collagen" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000030
name: calcareous spicule
def: "A spicule composed largely of calcite having a radiate form, the number of rays being either two (diactine), three (triactine), or four (tetractine)." []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule
disjoint_from: PORO:0000031 ! siliceous spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000031
name: siliceous spicule
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000032
name: spongin spicule
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000033
name: calcium carbonate exoskeleton
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000034
name: trab
def: "A trab is structural element within a sponge formed by the fusion of dendroclones. In the Anthaspidellidae, when spicules (usually dendroclones) connect at their tips to form a ladder-like structure, trabs may be formed.[1] Oxeas are sometimes employed in the central rod.[1][2] Trabs have a feather-like structure, or may form rods.[1][3] Trabs are usually regularly spaced, usually at sub-millimetric intervals.[1] Further dendroclones may interconnect adjacent trabs, forming ladder-like structures" [Wikipedia:Trab]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000035
name: pore
is_a: PORO:0000019 ! immaterial anatomical entity

[Term]
id: PORO:0000038
name: dermal pore
is_a: PORO:0000035 ! pore

[Term]
id: PORO:0000039
name: canal
is_a: UBERON:0000061 ! anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000041
name: flagellated canal
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000043
name: pinacoderm
def: "The pinacoderm is the outer most layer of cells (pinacocytes) in the phylum Porifera (sponges), similar to the epidermis in other organisms. The pinacocytes are on the external surface of the sponge body and characterized as an epithelial layer of flattened cells." [Wikipedia:Pinacoderm]
is_a: PORO:0000700 ! body layer
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000044
name: porocyte
def: "cell that surrounds a pore (ostium). In an asconoid sponge, water enters the sponge through the porocytes, passes directly to the choanocyte-lined spongocoel, and then out of the sponge through the osculum." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus, UBERON:cjm]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000023 ! pinacocyte
relationship: part_of PORO:0000043 ! pinacoderm

[Term]
id: PORO:0000045
name: spicule ray
relationship: part_of PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000046
name: apopyle
def: "a pore in each of the saclike chambers formed by the evagination of the body wall, through which water passes into the excurrent canals." [http:dictionary.reference.com/browse/apopyle]
is_a: PORO:0000035 ! pore

[Term]
id: PORO:0000094
name: crystal
synonym: "silicate crystal" RELATED []
synonym: "spicule crystal" RELATED []
relationship: part_of PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000095
name: arrangement of spicules
is_a: UBERON:0000480 ! anatomical group

[Term]
id: PORO:0000096
name: arrangement of megascleres
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000097
name: microsclere
def: "Small spicule, often ornate in shape." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule
disjoint_from: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000098
name: megasclere
def: "A large spicule, visible to the naked eye." [Wikipedia:Sponge_spicule]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000102
name: acanthophore
def: "Spicule having two to six stout spined rays, typically surrounding the point of insertion of the root tuft in Hyalonema species." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000103
name: accessory spicule
def: "A megasclere echinating the primary skeleton. See ECHINATING SPICULE." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000104
name: accretive reticulation
def: "Regularly anisotropic reticulation with ascending (primary and radial) fibers or tracts and interconnecting fibers or tracts about equal in thickness" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000499 ! reticulate skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000105
name: acerate spicule
def: "Pointed like a needle; adjective referring to the extremities of megascleres. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000106
name: actine ray
def: "A centered ray containing an axis or axial canal. See also CLAD." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "ray" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000045 ! spicule ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000107
name: actinocyte
def: "Elongated contractile cell often grouped in sphincter- like structure around the osculum, below the sieve- plates, and around the large exhalant canals. Characterized by numerous filaments of actin within their cytoplasm. New term for the contractile cell (ac in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "contractile cell" RELATED []
synonym: "myocyte" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000108
name: agglutinated support
def: "Creating substrate or support by cementing together a mixture of foreign material, such as sand, shell, or rock." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000922 ! substrate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000109
name: ala
def: "One of the thin, wing-like or spatulate structures in each recurved portion of a chela. The anterior ala is the one facing the shaft; others are lateral alae. See CHELA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000192 ! chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000110
name: alveolate skeleton
def: "Skeleton arranged around choanosomal cavities" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000111
name: amararhysis
def: "Paleontological term for longitudinal, tunnellike canal opening to the exhalant surface by slit-like apertures." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000298 ! exhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000112
name: ambucinate
def: "Diactin with spines recurved toward the center" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000114
name: amphiaster
def: "A microsclere with microspined rays radiating from both ends of a shaft; the rays are shorter than the shaft" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000115
name: amphiblastula
def: "Hollow, ovoid larva, with anterior flagellated and posterior nonflagellated groups of cells; typical of Calcaronea" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000926 ! sponge larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000116
name: amphidisc
def: "Dumbbell-shaped microsclere with ends developed into umbel-like expansions. Three size classes, termed macramphidisc, mesamphidisc, micramphidisc" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000117
name: amphitriaene
def: "A double triaene with a short rhabd bearing two opposed cladomes" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000118
name: amphitrider
def: "Tetraclone resembling an amphitriaene." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000585 ! tetraclone

[Term]
id: PORO:0000120
name: anatriaene
def: "A triaene in which the clads are sharply curved backward" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000121
name: anaxial desma
def: "Desma without central axis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000122
name: anchor
def: "Anchor-like spicule, protruding free from the basal part of the sponge; derived from diactine, triactine, or tetractine spicules, with terminal rays or spines, curved in the proximal direction along the main ray" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000123
name: anchorate chela
def: "An isochela with three or more free alae (at each end) in the form of recurved processes shaped like anchor claws (unguiferous) or anchor blades (spatuliferous); with two incipient lateral alae fused with the shaft over their entire length and a gently curved, not abruptly arched shaft. An anchorate chela with three teeth is called a tridendate chela." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000124
name: angulate spicule
def: "Sharply bent; referring to overall spicule shape, as in oxea or sigmas. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000126
name: anisochela
def: "A chela with unequal ends" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000192 ! chela
disjoint_from: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000127
name: anisotropic skeleton
def: "Reticulate skeleton with primary and secondary tracts, lines, or fibers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "chalinid skeleton" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000499 ! reticulate skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000129
name: anterior pole
def: "Pole directed forward when larva is swimming." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000912 ! pole of larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000130
name: anthaster
def: "An euaster with tuberculate, denticulate, or spined, sometimes digitate, expansions at the ray tips (Chondrilla grandis)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000295 ! euaster
relationship: part_of PORO:0000045 ! spicule ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000133
name: aphodal
def: "Type of choanocyte chamber that connects directly with the inhalant canals through prosopyles and with the exhalant canal through an apopyle extended by an aphodus. Only one chamber opens into one aphodus" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000025 ! choanocyte chamber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000134
name: aphodus
def: "Small exhalant canal leading from the apopyle to an exhalant canal (ap in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000298 ! exhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000135
name: apical actine (ray)
def: "The fourth actine of a tetractine that is joined to the basal triradiate system" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000106 ! actine ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000136
name: apochete
def: "Exhalant canal in fossil sponges." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000298 ! exhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000137
name: apopinacocyte
def: "Endopinacocyte lining the exhalant canal (ai in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000285 ! endopinacocyte
relationship: part_of PORO:0000298 ! exhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000138
name: apopinacoderm
def: "Surface lined by apopinacocytes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000286 ! endopinacoderm

[Term]
id: PORO:0000140
name: apopylar cell
def: "Cell surrounding the apopyle and located between the choanocytes and the apopinacocytes (ay in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000142
name: aporhysis
def: "In fossil sponges, canal closed at the outer end (cf. epirhysis)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000143
name: aquiferous system
def: "The entire water-conducting system between the ostia and the oscula, which comprises the inhalant system, choanocyte chambers, and the exhalant system" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000467 ! anatomical system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000146
name: arcuate chela
def: "An isochela with three free alae and the shaft characteristically curved outward, often bow-shaped." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000147
name: areolated surface
def: "Surface covered by numerous circular ectosomal areas (Hamigera)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000148
name: articulate skeleton
def: "Choanoskeleton composed of several rows of similar spicules" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000201 ! choanoskeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000149
name: asconoid
def: "Aquiferous system in which the internal cavity of the sponge is entirely lined by choanocytes" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000143 ! aquiferous system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000150
name: aspidaster
def: "An elongate-compressed microsclere in which the numerous rays are fused and end in minute spinose projections (Erylus spp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000151
name: aspidoplumicome
def: "Hexaster with numerous S-shaped terminal rays whose external curved ends form several successive tiers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000152
name: astroclone
def: "Desma made up of radiating arms" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000153
name: astrorhiza
def: "Traces of the excurrent canal system on or within a rigid skeleton that appear as radiating or star-shaped grooves." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000917 ! groove, pit or depression

[Term]
id: PORO:0000154
name: asymmetric megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of a megasclere. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000155
name: atrial skeleton
def: "Spicules surrounding the atrium." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "atrial spicule" RELATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "atrial spicule/skeleton" RELATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "gastral" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "gastral spicule/skeleton" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000157
name: autodermalia
def: "Dermalia belonging wholly or at least primarily to the outer bounding skin, without actin protruding inside the sponge body" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000252 ! dermalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000158
name: autogastralia
def: "Gastralia with one actin protruding into the atrium" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000329 ! gastralia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000159
name: axial filament
def: "The organic core around which a siliceous spicule is organized." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000031 ! siliceous spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000160
name: axial skeleton
def: "A type of skeletal organization in which some components are condensed to form a central region or axis" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000161
name: axinellid skeleton
def: "Structure with a dense core of parallel fibers or strands fanning out toward the periphery of a sponge See also PLUMOSE or PLUMORETICULATE." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000162
name: bacteriocyte
def: "Cell containing prokaryotic microsymbionts" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000163
name: bark
def: "The dense area of compacted spongin surrounding the central zone in pithed fibers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000480 ! anatomical group
relationship: part_of PORO:0000457 ! pithed fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000164
name: basal spongin plate
def: "A spongin layer covering the substratum" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "basal lamina" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000910 ! plate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000165
name: basal triradiate system
def: "The three rays of a tetractine that correspond to those of a triactine" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000166
name: basalia
def: "Spicules protruding from lower sponge surface; sometimes called root spicules, anchors, barbed basalia; in some species, forming a root tuft" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "anchor" RELATED []
synonym: "barbed basalia" RELATED []
synonym: "root spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000167
name: basidictyonal plate
def: "Rigid basal skeletal framework." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000168
name: basopinacocyte
def: "Pinacocyte affixing the sponge to the substratum by external secretion of a collagenous matrix (bs in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000012 ! secretory cell
is_a: PORO:0000023 ! pinacocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000169
name: bipocillum
def: "A modified anisochela with fused alae connected by a short curved shaft (genus Iophon)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000126 ! anisochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000170
name: birotula
def: "A type of microsclere with a straight shaft and umbrella-shaped ends" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "amphidisc" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000172
name: blunt megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of megascleres. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000173
name: bouquet
def: "Ectosomal brush of spicules perpendicular to the surface of the sponge, with pointed ends outward." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000174
name: brachyome
def: "Shortened arm of a trider." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000997 ! arm of trider

[Term]
id: PORO:0000176
name: bud
def: "An asexual reproductive body composed of various types of cells (e.g., Tethya spp., Axinella damicornis)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000900 ! reproductive body

[Term]
id: PORO:0000178
name: calcareous tripod
def: "Regular triactine whose center is not in the same plane as the extremities of the recurved rays." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000496 ! regular spicule
is_a: PORO:0000600 ! triactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000180
name: calthrop
def: "Equiangular tetraxon with equal rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000181
name: calycocome
def: "Hexaster with stout main rays and with terminal rays directed outward" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000182
name: canalaria
def: "Spicules lining canals" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000183
name: candelabrum
def: "A special form of lophocalthrop characterized by branching, multispined rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000381 ! lophocalthrop

[Term]
id: PORO:0000184
name: canonochela
def: "Modified, ellipsoid isochela with wing-like extensions on one (the bottom) side (genus Cercidochela)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000185
name: carrier cell
def: "Modified choanocyte that transports a captured spermatozoid to an oocyte" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000003 ! choanocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000186
name: cellules en croix
def: "Nonflagellated cells arranged in tetraradial fashion in the amphiblastula of Calcaronea" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000929 ! multicellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000115 ! amphiblastula

[Term]
id: PORO:0000187
name: cemented spicule
def: "Interlocked or adjacent spicules firmly linked by calcareous cement; the cement may be restricted to the junction area or may progressively encase the entire spicule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "fused spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000188
name: spicule center
def: "Point of union of the three rays of a triactine or of a basal triradiate system." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "center" BROAD []
synonym: "centrum" RELATED []
relationship: part_of PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000189
name: central cell
def: "Single cell located at the apopyle of choanocyte chambers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell
relationship: part_of PORO:0000046 ! apopyle

[Term]
id: PORO:0000190
name: centrotriaene
def: "A triaene with three clads and two small rhabds (genus Triptolemus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000191
name: centrotylote
def: "Spicule with a median tyle (globular swelling). See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000192
name: chela
def: "A microsclere with a curved shaft and recurved ala at each end." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000193
name: chiactine
def: "Tetractine with the unpaired ray of the basal system and the apical ray in the same alignment" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000194
name: chiastoclone
def: "Dendroclone with a very short central shaft." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000250 ! dendroclone

[Term]
id: PORO:0000195
name: chiastosigma
def: "Microsclere composed of two crossed sigmas (genus Chiastosia)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000196
name: choanoblast
def: "Cell that buds anucleate outgrowth called COLLAR BODY; in Hexactinellida" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000197
name: choanochamber
def: "Hexactinellida equivalent of the choanocyte chambers of Demospongiae and Calcarea." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "flagellated chamber" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000915 ! chamber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000200
name: choanoderm
def: "Surface lined by choanocytes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000700 ! body layer

[Term]
id: PORO:0000201
name: choanoskeleton
def: "Skeleton of the part of the sponge that contains choanocytes" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000202
name: choanosomal skeleton
def: "Skeleton of the main body, supporting the canal system and responsible for the form of the sponge." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "endosomal skeleton" EXACT []
synonym: "main skeleton" EXACT []
synonym: "primary skeleton" EXACT []
synonym: "principal skeleton" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000203
name: choanosome
def: "The internal region of a sponge, including the choanocyte chambers." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "endosome" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000938 ! organism subdivision

[Term]
id: PORO:0000204
name: choristid megasclere arrangement
def: "Predominantly radiate, occasionally confused arrangement of megascleres including triaenes with cladome outward, lacking spongin, and commonly with a cortex." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "astrophorid" RELATED TRAIT []
synonym: "choristid" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000096 ! arrangement of megascleres

[Term]
id: PORO:0000205
name: cinctoblastula
def: "Hollow larva, entirely flagellated, with a central ring of pigmented cells; typical of Homoscleromorpha" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000926 ! sponge larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000206
name: clad
def: "Any ray or axial branch containing an axis or axial canal confluent with that of the protoclad or protorhabd in any type of spicule; term chiefly used in triaene spicules." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000045 ! spicule ray
disjoint_from: PORO:0000500 ! rhabd

[Term]
id: PORO:0000207
name: cladome
def: "The clads of a triaene or triaene-derivative spicule." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000206 ! clad

[Term]
id: PORO:0000208
name: cladotylote
def: "Monaxon megasclere, one end with knobs, the other with hooks" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000210
name: clathrate skeleton
def: "Polyhedral arrangement of fibroreticulate sheets" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000211
name: clathriid skeleton
def: "Isodictyal or subisodictyal arrangement of fibers cored and/or echinated by styles in the family Microcionidae" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000213
name: clavidisc microsclere
def: "A ring-shaped microsclere (genus Merlia)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "clavidisc" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000214
name: clavule
def: "Sceptrule with one terminal umbel or with terminal anchor teeth" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000518 ! sceptrule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000215
name: cleistochela
def: "A chela with the ends (anterior alae) very close to each other (e.g., Clathria echinata)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000192 ! chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000216
name: clone
def: "Ray-like arm that is entirely anaxial." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000217
name: codonhexactin
def: "Discohexactin with long, dendate, umbel-like structures" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000273 ! discohexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000218
name: coeloblastula
def: "Hollow larva composed of an envelope of morphologically similar equipotent cells, to which a few larger nonflagellated cells may be added at the posterior pole." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "blastula" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000926 ! sponge larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000220
name: collagen fascicle
def: "A dense band of intercellular collagen fibrils, which has a skeletal role in some sponges (e.g., genus Chondrosia)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000221
name: collar body
def: "Anucleate choanocyte in hexactinellids." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000003 ! choanocyte
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000196 ! choanoblast

[Term]
id: PORO:0000222
name: collencyte
def: "Cell with branching pseudopods/cytoplasmic strands, involved in the secretion of collagen (co in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "collenocyte" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000012 ! secretory cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000223
name: column
def: "Radial skeletal element in stromatoporoids, with a greater degree of continuity and larger than PILLARS." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000998 ! skeletal element of sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000225
name: comitalia
def: "Parenchymalia located close and parallel to principalia" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000445 ! parenchymalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000227
name: compound fiber
def: "Several fibers merged or intricately interconnected" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "fasciculate fiber" RELATED []
synonym: "fibrofascicle" RELATED []
synonym: "trellised fiber" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000229
name: confused skeleton
def: "Irregularly positioned megascleres." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000096 ! arrangement of megascleres

[Term]
id: PORO:0000230
name: conical megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of megascleres. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "abruptly pointed" RELATED TRAIT []
synonym: "conical" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000231
name: conulose surface
def: "Surface with numerous cone-shaped projections raised up by underlying skeleton (Dysidea sp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000233
name: cored fiber
def: "A fiber that incorporates indigenous spicules or foreign material (spicules and sediment); coring may be light and limited to a central axis or may fill in the whole fiber" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000234
name: corrugated surface
def: "Surface with alternating parallel ridges and grooves (Callyspongia plicifera)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000235
name: cortex
def: "A superficial region of a sponge reinforced by a special organic or inorganic skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "crust" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000938 ! organism subdivision

[Term]
id: PORO:0000236
name: cortical skeleton
def: "Ectosomal skeleton reinforced by a layer of special skeleton elements." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000280 ! ectosomal skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000237
name: cortical spicule
def: "Spicule or skeleton of the external layer or cortex of the sponge" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "dermal spicule/skeleton" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000239
name: crepis
def: "The fundamental, inceptional body of a desma before it is modified by deposition of multiple layers of silica. A monocrepid desma develops from a monaxon spicule that is recognized by a straight, undivided axial thread (canal); a tetracrepid desma is based on a tetraxon spicule with a four-rayed axial thread (a small calthrops; see bottom of figure); an acrepid desma is based on a polyaxon fundamental structure lacking axial threads." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "acrepis" RELATED []
synonym: "monocrepid" RELATED []
synonym: "tetracrepid" RELATED []
relationship: part_of PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000241
name: croca
def: "A J-shaped microsclere" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000242
name: crypt tissue
def: "Masses of thesocyte-like cells lodged within the basal crypts (chambers) of the calcareous skeleton (see ct in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue

[Term]
id: PORO:0000243
name: crystal ultrastructure
def: "Organization of the skeletal crystals observed after special preparation showing the relationship between organic and mineral phases." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000480 ! anatomical group

[Term]
id: PORO:0000245
name: cuticle
def: "A spongin layer covering the surface or a part of the surface of a sponge." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000246
name: cyrtancistra
def: "A sigma with semilanceolated extremities (genus Pozziella)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000529 ! sigma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000247
name: cystencyte
def: "Cell with a single large vesicle containing amorphous material identified as polysaccharide and occupying most of the cell volume" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000249
name: dendritic skeleton
def: "A skeleton consisting of single or ramifying fibers or tracts that branch but rarely anastomose (tree-like branching)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000250
name: dendroclone
def: "Desma with branched ends or tetracladine, amphitrider-like; always positioned perpendicular to skeletal fibers." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000252
name: dermalia
def: "Spicules of the external sponge surface. See AUTODERMALIA, HYPODERMALIA" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000253
name: desma
def: "A typical interlocked megasclere with hypertrophic terminal secretion of silica." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "desmome" RELATED []
synonym: "desmone" RELATED []
synonym: "desmone megasclere" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000254
name: deuteroclad
def: "An actinal branch or a distal, branched portion of a ray. See DICHOTRIAENE." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000045 ! spicule ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000255
name: diactin
def: "Megascleres with two rays and frequently with central swellings indicating the hexactin origin." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000256
name: diactine
def: "Megasclere with two actines (two rays or two points)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "diact" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000412 ! monaxonic megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000257
name: diaene
def: "Reduced triaene with two clads" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000258
name: diancistra
def: "A microsclere with hooked, knife-shaped ends, notched where they join the shaft and in the middle of the shaft (genus Hamacantha)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000259
name: diapason
def: "Sagittal triactine with parallel paired rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "tuning-fork spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000513 ! sagittal spicule
is_a: PORO:0000600 ! triactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000260
name: diarhysis
def: "In fossil sponges, radial canal in the honeycomb- like skeleton of Aphrocallistidae." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000261
name: dichotriaene
def: "An ortho or plagiotriaene in which the clads are bifurcate" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000262
name: dicranoclone
def: "Tuberculate monaxial desma, arch shaped, tripodal, tetrapodal, or rarely polygonal; zygomes are terminal, like those of the tetraclone." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000263
name: dictyonal skeleton
def: "Three-dimensional network of fused, regular hexactins" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "dictyonine" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000264
name: dictyonalia
def: "Spicules fused into a rigid framework." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000061 ! anatomical structure
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000265
name: didiscorhabd
def: "Microxea or microstrongyle ornamented by two discs along the shaft (genus Didiscus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000267
name: diod spicule
def: "Any diactine spicule with a central double-bent kink" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000268
name: diplaster
def: "An astrose microsclere in which the rays or spines radiate from two, slightly distant, points" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000269
name: diplodal
def: "Type of choanocyte chamber that connects with the inhalant canals through a canaliculum called the prosodus and with the excurrent canal through an apopyle extended by an aphodus" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000025 ! choanocyte chamber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000271
name: dischela
def: "A modified isochela whose disc-shaped alae are very close to each other and connected on their margins by two extremely reduced shafts (genus Coelodischela)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "coelodischela" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000272
name: discoctaster
def: "Octaster with terminal rays ending in umbel-like disks" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000419 ! octaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000273
name: discohexactin
def: "Hexactin with rays terminating in dentate, umbel-like structures" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000341 ! hexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000274
name: discohexaster
def: "Hexaster with dentate, umbel-like terminal rays." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000275
name: discorhabd
def: "A rod-shaped microsclere with several smooth or serrated discs along the shaft (genera Latrunculia, Podospongia, Sceptrinus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "sceptrum" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000276
name: discotriaene
def: "A triaene with a disc-shaped cladome. The single clads may be distinguished by the presence of short axial canals (genus Discodermia)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000277
name: drepanocome
def: "Hexaster with sickle-like terminations (genus Dictyaulus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000278
name: echinating spicule
def: "Megasclere that protrudes from the spongin plate, a fiber, or a spicule tract" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000279
name: ectochrote
def: "Outer layer of the cortex" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000235 ! cortex

[Term]
id: PORO:0000280
name: ectosomal skeleton
def: "Skeleton found in the superficial region of a sponge, distinct from that of the choanosome." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "dermal skeleton" RELATED []
synonym: "ectosomal crust" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000281
name: ectosome
def: "The superficial region of a sponge that has no choanocyte chambers." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000938 ! organism subdivision

[Term]
id: PORO:0000283
name: encrusted substrate
def: "Thin, sheet-like coating of the substrate (Hymedesmia spp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000922 ! substrate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000285
name: endopinacocyte
def: "Pinacocyte lining the inhalant and exhalant canals. In some Demospongiae orders, it has a flagellum (en in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000023 ! pinacocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000286
name: endopinacoderm
def: "Surface lined by endopinacocytes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000288
name: entrapped spicules
def: "Calcareous or siliceous spicules that are not part of the primary spicule framework but are progressively enclosed within a solid skeleton during growth" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000289
name: eosinophilic cell
def: "Cell with inclusions that react positively with eosine." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000290
name: epirhabd
def: "Part of the developed desma formed by the deposition of concentric layers immediately around the crepis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000291
name: epirhysis
def: "In fossil sponges, canal closed at inner end (cf. aporhysis)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000292
name: epitheca
def: "A thin, wrinkled, calcareous layer, different in structure from the normal skeleton, covering the dead basal part of a rigid calcareous skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000920 ! calcareous skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000293
name: equal megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of megascleres. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "equal" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000295
name: euaster
def: "A collective term for astrose microscleres in which the rays radiate from a central point" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000296
name: eurypylous
def: "Type of choanocyte chamber that connects directly with the inhalant canals through prosopyles and with the excurrent canal through an apopyle. There is no special canal after the apopyle, and several chambers open into the same exhalant canal" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000025 ! choanocyte chamber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000298
name: exhalant canal
def: "Any canal forming part of the exhalant system, lined by the apopinacoderm." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "excurrent canal" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000299
name: exhalant system
def: "Part of the aquiferous system between the apopyle and oscule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000467 ! anatomical system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000300
name: exopinacocyte
def: "Fusiform or T-shaped pinacocyte covering the free surface of a sponge. In exceptional cases, it has a flagellum (Homoscleromorpha) (ex in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000023 ! pinacocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000301
name: exotyle
def: "Styles or tylostyles with enlarged or omated distal end, projecting from the sponge surface" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000567 ! style

[Term]
id: PORO:0000302
name: extra-axial skeleton
def: "Structurally distinct skeleton arising from or surrounding an axial region" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000303
name: facial plane
def: "The plane passing through tips of the three rays of a triactine or of a basal triradiate system of a tetractine." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000019 ! immaterial anatomical entity
relationship: part_of PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000304
name: fascicular fibrous microstructure
def: "Crystal fibers fanning outward and radiating upward. In the penicillate type (e.g., Ceratoporella), crystal fibers are feebly divergent; in the water-jet type (e.g., Merlia), crystal fibers progressively fan outward around the growth axis; in the trabecular type (cnidarian, unknown in sponges), the crystal fibers are symmetrically arranged around the growth axis and axial fibers are absent" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "penicillate" RELATED []
synonym: "trabecular" RELATED []
synonym: "water jet" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000305
name: fiber
def: "A column (strand, thread) of spongin forming a reticulate or dendritic skeleton, with or without indige nous spicules or foreign material." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "fibre" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000499 ! reticulate skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000307
name: fibule
def: "Microsclere consisting of two bent rays derived from greatly reduced oxyhexaster (in Holascus fibulatus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000309
name: filling (tissue) structure
def: "Secondary calcareous skeleton that partitions or fills abandoned parts of the skeleton." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000524 ! secondary calcareous skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000312
name: fistule
def: "A tube-like protuberance projecting from the sponge surface. See also PAPILLA" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000906 ! surface protruberance

[Term]
id: PORO:0000313
name: fistulose
def: "Bearing fistules (Coelosphaera hechteli)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000061 ! anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000317
name: flexuous spicule
def: "Referring to the spicule shape. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "sinuous" RELATED []
synonym: "sinuous spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000318
name: floricome
def: "Discohexaster with S-shaped terminal rays that end in a plate provided with teeth or claws" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000274 ! discohexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000320
name: follicle cell
def: "Cell in a group surrounding an oocyte" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000321
name: foramen
def: "Circular pore in laminae connecting adjoining interlamellar spaces (fo in figure, which also shows cc = choanocyte chamber; ct = crypt tissue; sk = rigid aspicular skeleton; spi = spicule; and ta = tabula)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000035 ! pore

[Term]
id: PORO:0000322
name: forceps
def: "A U-shaped microsclere" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "labis" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000325
name: free actine
def: "A ray that projects through the external or the atrial surface." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000106 ! actine ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000327
name: fuchsinophilic cell
def: "Cell with inclusions that react positively with acid fuchsin." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000329
name: gastralia
def: "All spicules that line the main exhalant cavity. See AUTOGASTRALIA, HYPOGASTRALIA" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule
relationship: part_of PORO:0000298 ! exhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000330
name: gemmule
def: "A resistant asexual reproductive body, composed of a mass of archaeocytes charged with reserves and enclosed in a noncellular protective envelope or coat" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000900 ! reproductive body

[Term]
id: PORO:0000331
name: globoferous cell
def: "Cell with a single large globule, a reduced cytoplasm, and a small conical nucleus (Clathriidae)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000334
name: glycocyte
def: "Cell with conspicuous dictyosomes, characterized by the presence of glycogen rosettes and osmiophilic inclusions. Also known as gray cell" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "gray cell" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000335
name: graphicome
def: "Hexaster with long, thin, parallel branches forming terminal brushes" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "graphihexaster" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000336
name: halichondrioid skeleton
def: "Confused skeleton except at the surface; choanosomal skeleton may be in vague tracts" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000229 ! confused skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000338
name: hastate
def: "Spicule remaining isodiametric for most of its length, with the point or points tapering abruptly. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000339
name: heloclone
def: "Desma with elongate and usually sinuous shaft, without branches, possibly with small digitations at the ends; the zygomes are lateral notches. An axial canal is usually found along most of the length of the spicule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000340
name: hemioxyhexaster
def: "Hexaster in which two opposite rays are longer than the other four; the branched rays are reduced or absent (genus Aphrocallistes)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000341
name: hexactin
def: "Siliceous spicule with six unbranched rays perpendicular to one another." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "hexact" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000031 ! siliceous spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000342
name: hexadisc
def: "Microhexactin with six actins ending in amphidisclike umbels" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000403 ! microhexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000343
name: hexaster
def: "Microsclere with six branched rays." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000344
name: hilum
def: "A more or less distinct, funnel-shaped depression in the surface of a STERRASTER, situated on one side in ellipsoidal forms; also occurs in ASPIDASTERS in reduced form, resembling an umbilicus." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000917 ! groove, pit or depression

[Term]
id: PORO:0000345
name: hispid surface
def: "Surface with long and scattered spicular projections (Stelletta spp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000346
name: hispidation
def: "Spicules projecting through the pinacoderm." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000347
name: homogeneous fiber
def: "A fiber without central pith and without conspicuous layers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000348
name: honeycombed surface
def: "Surface with polygonal pattern of ridges (Verongula gigantea)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000349
name: hymedesmioid skeleton
def: "Skeleton of encrusting sponge where monactine megascleres are arranged singly with heads fixed to a basal plate of spongin and points directed outward" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "leptoclathriid" RELATED []
synonym: "leptoclathriid skeleton" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000350
name: hypodermalia
def: "Dermalia with one actin protruding inside the body and the other ones tangential to the external surface" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000252 ! dermalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000351
name: hypogastralia
def: "Gastralia with one actin protruding inward, the other ones oriented tangentially to the atrium" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000329 ! gastralia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000352
name: inarticulate skeleton
def: "Choanoskeleton composed only of the unpaired rays of the subatrial spicules and of one of the rays of the cortical or subcortical spicules. Without specific spicules of the choanoskeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000201 ! choanoskeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000355
name: inhalant canal
def: "Any canal forming part of the inhalant system and lined by the prosopinacoderm." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "incurrent canal" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000039 ! canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000356
name: inhalant system
def: "Part of the aquiferous system between ostia and prosopyle." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000467 ! anatomical system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000357
name: intermedia
def: "Parenchymalia situated among the principalia or dictyonalia" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000445 ! parenchymalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000358
name: interstitial spicule
def: "Free choanosomal spicule not included in tracts or fibers, common in subectosomal skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "auxiliary spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000951 ! choanosomal spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000360
name: irciniid filament
def: "Long, slender (0.5-15 urn thick) spongin element, terminally knobbed; intertwined or free in the sponge body" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000361
name: irregular microstructure
def: "Structure in which tangled crystal fibers have no preferred orientation (e.g., genus Vaceletia). Shape and nature of the crystal fiber may be diverse" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "felt microstructure" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000363
name: isochela
def: "A chela with equal ends" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000192 ! chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000364
name: isodictyal reticulation
def: "Isotropic reticulation in which the meshes are triangular and have sides one spicule long" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000499 ! reticulate skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000365
name: isotropic reticulation
def: "Reticulation without differentiation into primary or secondary fibers, tracts, or lines." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000499 ! reticulate skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000367
name: lamina
def: "Calcareous plate in stromatoporoids, perpendicular to radial skeletal components" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000935 ! calcareous plate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000368
name: laminated fiber
def: "A fiber in which concentric layers are visible" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "stratified fiber" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000369
name: latilamina
def: "A macroscopic, banded calcareous skeletal plate in stromatoporoids" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000935 ! calcareous plate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000370
name: lax (= loose, vague) skeleton
def: "Skeleton lacking clear tracts or fibers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000371
name: leuconoid system
def: "Aquiferous system in which the choanocytes are restricted to discrete choanocyte chambers, which are dispersed in the mesohyl." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000143 ! aquiferous system
relationship: part_of PORO:0000028 ! leuconoid sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000373
name: line of spicules
def: "Unispicular tract" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000374
name: linked spicules
def: "Spicules that are interlocked by zygosis, without cement" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000376
name: lipostomous surface
def: "Condition of a surface in which oscula and ostia are inconspicuous (in old descriptions)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000377
name: lithistid skeleton
def: "Main skeleton consisting of an interlocked assemblage of desmas" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000381
name: lophocalthrop
def: "Modified calthrop with one (monoloph), three (triloph), or four (tetraloph) rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000180 ! calthrop

[Term]
id: PORO:0000382
name: lophocome (= lophodiscohexaster)
def: "Discohexaster with short, stout main rays and numerous slender secondary rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000274 ! discohexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000384
name: lychnisc
def: "Hexactin with a center resembling a perforated octohedron; building block of fused (dictyonal) framework called LYCHNISCA (lower two lychnics shown in optical section)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000341 ! hexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000385
name: lychnisca
def: "Dictyonal hexactin framework formed by lychnises" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000386
name: lyssacine
def: "Spicular framework formed by the juxtaposition and interlacing of elongate rays of hexactins" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000387
name: mamelon
def: "Rounded regular or irregular elevation of the skeleton surface; may or may not show correlation with astrorhizae" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000388
name: marginalia
def: "Prostalia that project in a wreath-like arrangement from the oscular margin" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000484 ! prostalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000390
name: megaclone
def: "Arch-shaped desma with a short crepis. The zygomes vary from oblique lateral facets to tongue- or hand-like terminal expansions" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000391
name: megarhizoclone
def: "Nontuberculate dicranoclone desma" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000262 ! dicranoclone

[Term]
id: PORO:0000393
name: mesolamella
def: "Sheet of collagen separating the choanochambers of hexactinellids." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000394
name: mesotriaene
def: "A triaene in which the rhabd is extended beyond the cladome" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000395
name: mesotrider
def: "Tetraclone with a mesotriaene crepis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000585 ! tetraclone

[Term]
id: PORO:0000396
name: metaster
def: "A microsclere with a twisted shaft no longer than the spines; intermediate between plesiaster and spi raster" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000398
name: microanchor
def: "A small tetractine anchor (described only from the atrial skeleton)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000399
name: microcionid
def: "Structure of microcionid sponges in which spicules project from an elevation of the basal plate of spongin" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000400
name: microdiactin spicule
def: "A small diactine spicule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000401
name: microgranular cell
def: "A cell with cytoplasm filled with small dense granules" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000704 ! granular cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000402
name: microgranular microstructure
def: "Diverse structure in which small, round elements are scattered" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000403
name: microhexactin
def: "Hexactin microsclere." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000404
name: microholactin
def: "Large category of microscleres lacking spines and appendages (Monorhaphis)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "holactin" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000405
name: microlamellar microstructure
def: "Structure in which the crystal fibers are disposed in criss-cross layers, mostly parallel to the surface of the skeleton (e.g., genus Acanthochaetetes)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000406
name: micropyle
def: "Opening in the gemmule coat through which cells leave a hatching gemmule (mp in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000019 ! immaterial anatomical entity
relationship: part_of PORO:0000330 ! gemmule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000407
name: microrhabd
def: "A general term for a straight, monaxonic microsclere." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000409
name: microstructure
def: "The arrangement of crystals that form the skeletal components, as seen without special preparations." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000480 ! anatomical group

[Term]
id: PORO:0000410
name: microsymbiont
def: "Prokaryotic or more rarely eukaryotic microorganism living inside a sponge. May be unicellular or multicellular filamentous, with or without pigments, and may occur intra- or intercellularly" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000061 ! anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000411
name: monaene
def: "Reduced triaene with only one clad" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000412
name: monaxonic megasclere
def: "Linear, nonradiate spicule, or a spicule type not having more than two rays along one axis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "monaxon" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000413
name: mucronate megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the nipple-like point of a megasclere. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "mucronate" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000414
name: multispicular fiber
def: "Fiber or tract composed of six or more spicules adjacent to one another." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "multispicular fiber tract" BROAD []
synonym: "plurispicular" RELATED []
synonym: "polyserial" RELATED []
synonym: "polyspicular" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000415
name: needle-like biradiate
def: "A diactine with a hole at one end" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000416
name: node
def: "Junction of spicule tips cemented by spongin." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000417
name: nurse cell
def: "Cells that are incorporated in developing oocytes to provide nutrient material for further growth" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000990 ! reproductive system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000418
name: octactin
def: "Spicule with eight rays, generally six in one plane, the other two perpendicular to them." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000419
name: octaster
def: "Octactin microsclere with branched rays." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000421
name: onychaete
def: "A long, thin, finely spined, asymmetric microsclere" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000422
name: onychaster
def: "Hexaster with terminal rays ending in four actins that are perpendicular to the rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "onychohexactin" RELATED []
synonym: "onychohexaster" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000423
name: optic axis
def: "The crystallographic trigonal axis of the calcite spicule." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000909 ! ray axis
relationship: part_of PORO:0000030 ! calcareous spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000424
name: orthodiactin
def: "Diactin in which the two rays belong to different axes of a triaxon and form an angle of 90 degrees" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000255 ! diactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000425
name: orthogonal microstructure
def: "Microstructure in which the crystal fibers are in perpendicular and radial orientation relative to a central axis" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000426
name: orthotriaene
def: "A triaene in which the clads are directed at right angles to the rhabd" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000431
name: oxea
def: "Monaxon (diactinal) spicule pointed at both ends (a-m in figure). Different types are distinguished by shape and tip morphology. Shape may be fusiform (a), angulate (b), centrotylote (c), curved (d), or flexuous (e). Tips may be acerate (f), asymmetrical (g), blunt (h), conical (i), hastate (j), mucronate (k), stepped (1), or symmetrical (m)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine
disjoint_from: PORO:0000954 ! microstrongyle

[Term]
id: PORO:0000433
name: oxyaster
def: "An euaster with acerate free rays and a small centrum less than one-third the diameter of the whole spicule)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000295 ! euaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000434
name: paired actine
def: "One or both equivalent rays of a sagittal spicule." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "oral" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "oral/oscular ray" RELATED []
synonym: "oscular" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000106 ! actine ray
relationship: part_of PORO:0000513 ! sagittal spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000435
name: palisade
def: "Perpendicular arrangement of ectosomal spicules, with points directed outward" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000437
name: palmate chela
def: "An iso- or anisochela in which the lateral alae coalesce with the shaft over their entire length, and the single, median, anterior ala (one at each end) stands free and widens distally" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000192 ! chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000439
name: papilla
def: "Nipple-like protuberance projecting from the sponge surface and bearing either ostia, oscula, or both." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "aquiferous papilla" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000906 ! surface protruberance

[Term]
id: PORO:0000440
name: papillate surface
def: "Surface bearing papillae (Polymastia spp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000441
name: pappocome
def: "Graphicome-like spicule with diverging terminal rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000442
name: parasagittal spicule
def: "Bilaterally symmetrical triactine or tetractine with unequal actines, having equal angles (120 degrees) between the basal rays when projected into a plane perpendicular to the optic axis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "secondary sagittal spicule" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000030 ! calcareous spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000443
name: paratangential skeleton
def: "Arrangement of ectosomal spicules intermediate between the palisade and tangential type" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000444
name: parchment
def: "Tangential ectosomal skeleton in which the megascleres are arranged in a tight feltwork" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000280 ! ectosomal skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000445
name: parenchymalia
def: "All spicules in the choanosome" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules
relationship: part_of PORO:0000203 ! choanosome

[Term]
id: PORO:0000446
name: parenchymella
def: "Larva composed of an envelope of flagellated cells surrounding an internal mass of cells" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000926 ! sponge larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000447
name: paucispicular fiber
def: "Fiber or tract with two to five megascleres adjacent to one another" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "paucispicular fiber tract" BROAD []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000449
name: pentactin
def: "Five-rayed spicule." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "pentact" EXACT [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000450
name: phyllotriaene
def: "A triaene with a leaf-shaped cladome." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000451
name: pillar
def: "Radial skeletal component, relatively short compared with COLUMN" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000998 ! skeletal element of sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000455
name: pinule
def: "Pentact or hexact spicule with four basal rays and one perpendicular ray ornamented by obliquely set spines directed distally." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000456
name: pith
def: "Central area of a fiber made up of more or less diffuse wisps of collagen or of a coarsely granular collagen material. See PITHED FIBER." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000457
name: pithed fiber
def: "A fiber in which pith is easily distinguished from the surrounding bark." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000458
name: placochela
def: "A special type of isochela with plate-like alae. The alae and the shaft are internally ornamented by radial ridges (genus Guitarra)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000459
name: plagiotriaene
def: "A triaene in which the clads are directed forward and form with the rhabd an angle of about 45 degrees, and may be recurved distally" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000461
name: plesiaster
def: "A streptaster with a very short shaft (always shorter than the spines)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000562 ! streptaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000462
name: pleuralia
def: "Spicules protruding from lateral surface." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000463
name: plumoreticulate skeleton
def: "A type of plumose skeletal construction in which cross-connections occur" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000464
name: plumose skeleton
def: "A type of skeletal construction made of primary fibers or spicule tracts from which skeletal elements radiate obliquely" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000465
name: pocket cell
def: "Special kind of bacteriocyte that surrounds an area of the intercellular matrix, including microsymbionts" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000162 ! bacteriocyte

[Term]
id: PORO:0000467
name: polytylote megasclere
def: "Megasclere with several annular swelling along its shaft" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "polytylote" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000468
name: pore groove
def: "A furrow in the ectosome where the ostia are located" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000917 ! groove, pit or depression
relationship: part_of PORO:0000281 ! ectosome

[Term]
id: PORO:0000469
name: pore sieve
def: "A specialized area of the ectosome with a cluster of ostia and an underlying inhalant cavity called the vestibule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "chone (uniporal chone" RELATED []
synonym: "crible" RELATED []
synonym: "cribriporal chone)" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000917 ! groove, pit or depression
relationship: part_of PORO:0000281 ! ectosome

[Term]
id: PORO:0000470
name: porocalyx
def: "Cup-shaped depressions with pore-sieves, typical of some genera of Tetillidae" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000917 ! groove, pit or depression

[Term]
id: PORO:0000472
name: posterior pole
def: "Pole opposite to anterior pole when larva is swimming, often without flagella." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000912 ! pole of larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000473
name: posticum
def: "Cf. apopore (= osculum); in fossil sponges." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000018 ! osculum

[Term]
id: PORO:0000474
name: primary fiber
def: "An ascending fiber ending at a right angle to the surface" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "ascending fiber/tract/line" RELATED []
synonym: "longitudinal fiber/tract" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000475
name: primary calcareous skeleton
def: "Initially formed skeletal components" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000920 ! calcareous skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000476
name: primary spicule
def: "The major structural megasclere in any particular sponge." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000477
name: primary spicule framework
def: "Framework of spicules around which a cement is deposited" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000096 ! arrangement of megascleres

[Term]
id: PORO:0000478
name: principalia
def: "Spicules making up main skeletal framework" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000479
name: prosochete
def: "In fossil sponges, inhalant canal leading to prosopore." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000355 ! inhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000480
name: prosodus
def: "A small inhalant canal leading to a prosopyle." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000355 ! inhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000481
name: prosopinacocyte
def: "Endopinacocyte lining the inhalant canals." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000285 ! endopinacocyte
relationship: part_of PORO:0000355 ! inhalant canal

[Term]
id: PORO:0000482
name: prosopinacoderm
def: "Surface lined by prosopinacocytes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000286 ! endopinacoderm

[Term]
id: PORO:0000484
name: prostalia
def: "Spicules protruding from a surface" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000485
name: protoclad
def: "The proximal, unbranched portion of a branched ray. See DICHOTRIAENE." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000106 ! actine ray

[Term]
id: PORO:0000486
name: protorhabd
def: "The original simple shaft of ornamented monaxons and of triaenes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000487
name: protriaene
def: "A triaene in which the clads are directed or sharply curved forward, away from the rhabd" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000488
name: pseudocalyx
def: "One of a group of skeletal tubes - closely packed together, mostly hexagonal in shape and containing the live material - that resemble the calices or corallites of cnidarians." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "calyx" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000998 ! skeletal element of sponge

[Term]
id: PORO:0000489
name: pseudogemmule
def: "Accumulation of gemmular archaeocytes (crypt cells, tract cells) in basal cavities of a solid calcareous skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000929 ! multicellular anatomical structure
relationship: part_of PORO:0000920 ! calcareous skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000490
name: pseudosagittal spicule
def: "A subcortical triactine essentially sagittal, but having unequally long and differently curved rays on each side of the unpaired angle" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000569 ! subcortical spicule
is_a: PORO:0000600 ! triactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000491
name: punctate surface
def: "Surface appearing dotted because of microscopic pores." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000493
name: radiate skeleton
def: "A type of skeleton in which the structural components diverge from a central region toward the sponge surface" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000494
name: raphide
def: "A very thin, hair-like microsclere, often in bundles called trichodragmas" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000495
name: reduction body
def: "A multicellular mass resulting from the disorganization of a sponge and presumably capable of reorganizing into a new functional sponge." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000929 ! multicellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000496
name: regular spicule
def: "Triactine or tetractine spicule with basal rays of equal length, and with equal angles (120 degrees) between them, when projected into a plane perpendicular to the optic axis" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000499
name: reticulate skeleton
def: "Three-dimensional network of fibers, tracts, lines, or single spicules." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "renieroid skeleton" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000500
name: rhabd
def: "A collective term for a monaxonic megasclere, later applied to the one ray of a triaene that is distinct from the other three, mostly in length (= rhabdome)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "rhabdome" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000045 ! spicule ray
relationship: part_of PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000502
name: rhabdodiactin
def: "Diactin in which the two rays are aligned in a single axis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000255 ! diactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000503
name: rhabdome
def: "The rhabd of a triaene and of a triaene-derived spicule." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000500 ! rhabd

[Term]
id: PORO:0000504
name: rhabdostyle
def: "A style with a pronounced basal bend." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000567 ! style

[Term]
id: PORO:0000506
name: rhizoclone
def: "Nontuberculate irregular monaxial desma, with spiny to root-like zygomes that are usually mainly lateral" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000947 ! monaxial desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000507
name: ribbed surface
def: "Surface with series of ridges (Xestospongia muta) ; ridges not necessarily parallel, as in CORRUGATED." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000508
name: rigid aspicular skeleton
def: "Skeleton that originates from the direct secretion of aspicular elements made up of calcium carbonate; siliceous or calcareous spicules may be secondarily entrapped in the skeleton during the growth process (sk in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000901 ! rigid skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000509
name: rigid spicular skeleton
def: "A skeleton in which the main framework is first made up of fused or linked spicules that may later be invested by an aspicular cement" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000901 ! rigid skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000512
name: rugose surface
def: "Having a rough and ridged surface (Topsentia spp.)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000513
name: sagittal spicule
def: "Triactine or tetractine with two equal angles (paired angles) and one dissimilar angle (unpaired angle) at the center, when projected into a plane perpendicular to the optic axis." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "primary sagittal spicule" RELATED DEPRECATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000514
name: sanidaster
def: "A rhabd-derived, straight microsclere having spines at intervals along the entire length. Spines along the shaft are perpendicular to the axis and may or may not be spirally arranged; those at the ends diverge obliquely (e.g., genera Tribrachium, Disyringa)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000500 ! rhabd

[Term]
id: PORO:0000515
name: sarule
def: "Sceptrule with one end swollen and ornamented with distally directed spines" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000518 ! sceptrule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000516
name: scale
def: "Disc-shaped microsclere forming ectosomal ('dermal') armor (genus Lepidosphera)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000517
name: scepter
def: "Uncinate marginalia, with spiny shaft acerated at one end; terminating in four very short actins at the other (Pheronematidae, genus Semperella)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000388 ! marginalia

[Term]
id: PORO:0000518
name: sceptrule
def: "A small, prostal monactin spicule exhibiting peculiar secondary developments at one end (order Hexactinosa)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000519
name: schizorhysis
def: "In fossil sponges, continuous system of interconected canal spaces (Tretodictyidae)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000467 ! anatomical system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000521
name: sclerodermite
def: "Aggregate of crystals forming a microstructural unit of the calcareous skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000522
name: scopule
def: "Fork-like sceptrule with one end branched (leptoscopule, pachyscopule)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000518 ! sceptrule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000523
name: secondary fiber
def: "In a reticulate skeleton, a fiber that links the primary fibers." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "connective fiber" RELATED []
synonym: "connective tract" BROAD []
synonym: "fibers" RELATED []
synonym: "lines" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000524
name: secondary calcareous skeleton
def: "Skeletal components formed after the deposition of the primary calcareous skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000920 ! calcareous skeleton
relationship: develops_from PORO:0000475 ! primary calcareous skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000525
name: selenaster
def: "A special type of spiraster approaching the shape of a sterraster (genus Placospongia)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000549 ! spiraster (= spinispira)

[Term]
id: PORO:0000527
name: sieve plate
def: "Perforated plate that extends over the broad terminal opening of some tubular-shaped Hexactinellida (Euplectella). See \"Architecture and Spicules of Hexactinellida\"" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000910 ! plate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000529
name: sigma
def: "A microsclere of C or S shape" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000530
name: sigmaspire
def: "A contorted-sigmoid microspined microsclere (family Tetillidae)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000531
name: sigmatocome
def: "Hexaster with long, S-shaped terminal rays (Dictyaulus)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000532
name: skeleton
def: "All structures supporting and protecting the sponge body." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000938 ! organism subdivision

[Term]
id: PORO:0000533
name: smooth surface
def: "Surface without any projections (Chondrosia reniformis)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "glabrous" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000535
name: spatuliferous-anchorate chela
def: "An anchorate chela (usually isochela) having alae that are completely free from the shaft and that are spatulate or shaped like anchor teeth" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "ancora spatulifera" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000123 ! anchorate chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000536
name: spermiocyst
def: "Modified, encysted spermatozoid transported by a carrier cell to the oocyte" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000537
name: sphaerancora
def: "Modified isochela, consisting of two ellipsoid ridged plates intersecting at right angles (genus Melonanchora)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000538
name: sphaeroclone
def: "Anaxial desma in which several ray-like arms extend from one side of a globular centrum that is spiny on the other side" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000121 ! anaxial desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000539
name: sphaerohexactin (sphaerohexact)
def: "Hexactin with rays ending in spherical knobs" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000341 ! hexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000540
name: sphaerohexaster
def: "Hexaster with terminal rays ending in spherical knobs" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000541
name: spheraster
def: "An euaster with short rays and a thick centrum; the diameter of the centrum (more than one-half the total diameter) exceeds the length of the rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000295 ! euaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000542
name: spheroxyaster
def: "Euaster with a discrete centrum that is more than one-third the total diameter" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "oxyspheraster" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000295 ! euaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000543
name: spherulitic microstructure
def: "Globular (centric or excentric) arrangement of crystal fibers radiating from a common center (e.g., genus Astrosclerd)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "spheroidal" EXACT [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000409 ! microstructure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000544
name: spherulous cell
def: "Cell filled with large round spherules that occupy almost the entire cell body, compressing the cytoplasm into thin sheets (sp in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000000 ! sponge cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000547
name: spiculoid spicule
def: "A spongin component of the skeleton that has the form of a diactinal, triactinal, or polyactinal spicule" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "spongin spicule" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000548
name: spiny surface
def: "Surface with scattered, stiff, and sharp spicular or fiber projections (Pleraplysilla spinifera)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "muricate" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000905 ! sponge surface

[Term]
id: PORO:0000549
name: spiraster (= spinispira)
def: "Spiral, rod-shaped microsclere with spines peripherally arranged." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "spinispira" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000550
name: spirodiscohexaster
def: "Discohexaster with a bunch of terminal, spirally twisted rays (genus Rhabdodictyum)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000274 ! discohexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000553
name: statoblast
def: "Particular gemmule that lacks a complex spongin coat and is covered externally by megascleres; typical of the freshwater Potamolepidae." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000330 ! gemmule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000554
name: stauractin
def: "Reduced hexactin with four rays all arranged in one plane" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000341 ! hexactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000555
name: stauraster
def: "Reduced hexaster with four rays all arranged in one plane" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000343 ! hexaster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000556
name: stepped megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of a megasclere. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "stepped" RELATED TRAIT []
synonym: "telescoped" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000557
name: sterraster
def: "A spherical or ellipsoidal microsclere in which the numerous rays are fused and end in stellate terminations (e.g., genus Geodia)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000562
name: streptaster
def: "Aster in which the rays proceed from an axis that is usually spiral" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000902 ! aster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000564
name: strongylaster (= chiaster)
def: "Aster with free, isodiametric, blunt rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "chiaster" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000902 ! aster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000565
name: strongyle
def: "An isodiametric, diactinal megasclere with rounded ends" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000566
name: strongyloxea
def: "A fusiform oxea with one end blunt." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000431 ! oxea

[Term]
id: PORO:0000567
name: style
def: "Monaxon spicule with one end pointed, the other (head or base) blunt" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0002043 ! monactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000568
name: subatrial spicule
def: "Sagittal spicule with paired rays adjacent to the atrial skeleton." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "subgastral spicule" RELATED DEPRECATED [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000569
name: subcortical spicule
def: "A pseudosagittal triactine, with unpaired actine and a shorter paired actine adjacent to the cortex, or a tetractine with basal triradiate system adjacent to the cortex." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000572
name: sublithistid skeleton
def: "Skeleton consisting of a loose assemblage of desmas" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000532 ! skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000573
name: subtylostyle
def: "Tylostyle with one end pointed, the other with a slight swelling or knob; the swelling, more or less distinct, may be displaced along the shaft" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000619 ! tylostyle

[Term]
id: PORO:0000575
name: syconoid
def: "Aquiferous system with elongated choanocyte chamber containing free distal cones or extending from cortex to atrium." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000143 ! aquiferous system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000576
name: sylleibid
def: "Aquiferous system with elongate choanocyte chambers arranged radially around invagination of the atrial cavity (Leucilla uter)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000143 ! aquiferous system

[Term]
id: PORO:0000577
name: symmetrical megasclere
def: "Adjective referring to the extremities of megascleres. See OXEA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "symmetrica" RELATED TRAIT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000578
name: synapticule
def: "Bridges composed of siliceous cement joining spicules" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure

[Term]
id: PORO:0000579
name: tabula
def: "Plate or floor that partitions the basal part of a skeletal cavity (ta in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000910 ! plate

[Term]
id: PORO:0000580
name: tabulate osculum
def: "Osculum in stromatoporoids that has been repeatedly partitioned by secondarily deposited tabulae." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000018 ! osculum

[Term]
id: PORO:0000581
name: tangential skeleton
def: "Ectosomal skeleton arranged parallel to the surface (figure shows upper right, view from the top)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000280 ! ectosomal skeleton

[Term]
id: PORO:0000582
name: tangential spicule
def: "Spicule arranged parallel to the surface." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000583
name: tauactin
def: "Large, smooth triactin (genus Monorhaphis)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000599 ! triactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000584
name: tertiary fiber
def: "In a reticulate skeleton, a fiber interconnecting the secondary fibers" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000305 ! fiber

[Term]
id: PORO:0000585
name: tetraclone
def: "Tetraxial desma that does not show a triaenose symmetry; the zygomes are typically terminal." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000253 ! desma

[Term]
id: PORO:0000586
name: tetractin
def: "Spicule with four rays in one plane" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000587
name: tetractine
def: "A spicule with four rays (in figure, sagittal tetractine at the top and regular tetractine at the bottom)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000588
name: tetradisc
def: "Microsclere with four actins ending in amphidisc like umbels" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000589
name: tetrapocillum
def: "A rare, modified isochela having two small disks both at the extremities and in the middle of a straight shaft; the two in the middle are fused (genus Tetrapocillon)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000363 ! isochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000590
name: thaumatochela
def: "A rare, minute anisochela with the smaller extremity jar- or slipper-shaped and partly enveloped by four alae issuing from the opposite end and forming an umbrella-like structure (Mycale thaumatochela)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000126 ! anisochela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000591
name: thesocyte
def: "Vitelline-rich archaeocyte in a sponge gemmule (th in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000016 ! archaeocyte
relationship: part_of PORO:0000330 ! gemmule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000592
name: thraustoxa
def: "Toxa-like, smooth to spinose microsclere, double- bent in the middle and often with central swelling (genus Rhabderemia)" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000593
name: tignule
def: "Gigantic, isolated diactin (Hyalonema toxeres)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000255 ! diactin

[Term]
id: PORO:0000594
name: tornote
def: "A straight, isodiametric, diactinal megasclere with conical or mucronate extremities" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000596
name: toxa
def: "Bow-shaped microsclere" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000097 ! microsclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000597
name: trabecular tissue
def: "Syncytia in hexactinellids occurring around the choanochambers." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue

[Term]
id: PORO:0000598
name: tract
def: "A column of aligned megascleres." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000096 ! arrangement of megascleres

[Term]
id: PORO:0000599
name: triactin
def: "Spicule with three rays in one plane" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000600 ! triactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000600
name: triactine
def: "A spicule with three rays." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000601
name: triaene
def: "General term for a tetractinal megasclere having one unequal ray (termed rhabd) that is commonly much longer than the other three (termed clads, forming the cladome)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "triaene" RELATED TRAIT []
synonym: "triaene megasclere" EXACT []
is_a: PORO:0000098 ! megasclere
is_a: PORO:0000587 ! tetractine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000602
name: triaxone
def: "Spicule with three axes." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "triaxon" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000603
name: trichaster
def: "Graphicome (genus Trichasterina)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000335 ! graphicome

[Term]
id: PORO:0000604
name: trichimella
def: "Hexactinellid larva, distinguished by median zone with multiflagellated mononucleate cells between anterior and posterior poles; with special larval stauractin skeleton" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000926 ! sponge larva

[Term]
id: PORO:0000605
name: trichodragma
def: "A bundle of raphids." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "dragma" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000095 ! arrangement of spicules

[Term]
id: PORO:0000606
name: trichotriaene
def: "A triaene in which the clads are trifurcate." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000601 ! triaene

[Term]
id: PORO:0000607
name: trichox
def: "Thin, hair-like straight monaxon spicules present in general around the osculum or protruding from the cortex." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000412 ! monaxonic megasclere

[Term]
id: PORO:0000608
name: tridentate chela
def: "A chela with three free alae. See also ANCHORATE CHELA." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000192 ! chela

[Term]
id: PORO:0000609
name: trider
def: "Variant of tetraclone, with triaenose symmetry and three similar arms." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000585 ! tetraclone

[Term]
id: PORO:0000610
name: triod
def: "Triact in which the rays are equal, straight, in one plane, and diverging at an angle of 120 degrees." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000600 ! triactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000611
name: tripod
def: "A modified triod with rays forming a regular pyramid." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000610 ! triod

[Term]
id: PORO:0000612
name: trophocyte
def: "Nurse cell involved in the initial stages of gemmule and oocyte formation." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000417 ! nurse cell

[Term]
id: PORO:0000613
name: truncaster
def: "Aster with crowded, blunt rays (genus Rhabdastrella)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000902 ! aster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000614
name: tuberculate spicule
def: "Spicule ornamented with blunt knobs." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000617
name: tylaster
def: "Aster with free, microtylote rays" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000902 ! aster

[Term]
id: PORO:0000618
name: tyle
def: "Any rounded swelling or knob in a spicule (c in figure)." [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
relationship: part_of PORO:0000017 ! spicule

[Term]
id: PORO:0000619
name: tylostyle
def: "A style with a tyle (globular swelling) at the base" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000567 ! style

[Term]
id: PORO:0000620
name: tylote
def: "Diactinal megasclere with a swelling on each end" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000621
name: uncinate
def: "Diactin covered with short spines directed distally (barbule); size classes are designated by macrouncinate, microuncinate" [http://www.portol.org/thesaurus]
synonym: "barbule" RELATED []
synonym: "macruncinate" RELATED []
synonym: "micruncinate" RELATED []
is_a: PORO:0000256 ! diactine

[Term]
id: PORO:0000622
