property_value: homology_notes "(...) mouth development is very similar in protostomes and 'basal' deuterostomes, whereas the chordate mouth seems to develop at a new position. Recent data for echinoderms and hemichordates further suggest that this change in mouth position may result from change in the influence of a conserved ectodermal patterning system on mouth development. It has been suggested that the mouths of vertebrates and urochordates may constitute a 'new' mouth.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000280", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="DOI:10.1016/j.semcdb.2007.06.002 Christiaen L, Jaszczyszyn Y, Kerfant M, Kanob S, Thermes V, Joly JS, Evolutionary modification of mouth position in deuterostomes. Seminars in Cell and Developmental Biology (2007)"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0000167
name: oral cavity
namespace: uberon
def: "Anatomical cavity at the start of the digestive tract that that is enclosed by the mouth. The boundaries and contents vary depending on the species. In vertebrates, the boundaries are the oral opening, the cheeks, the palate and (if present) the palatoglossal arch - if this is not present then the mouth and pharynx form the oropharyngeal cavity. The buccal cavity contains the teeth, tongue and palate (when present)" [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/wiki/The-digestive-tract, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165, ISBN:0073040584]
subset: pheno_slim
subset: uberon_slim
subset: vertebrate_core
synonym: "bucca" RELATED []
synonym: "buccal cavity" EXACT [FMA:20292, ISBN:0073040584]
synonym: "cavity of mouth" EXACT []
