[Term]
id: UBERON:0000341
name: throat
namespace: uberon
def: "In anatomy, the throat is the anterior part of the neck, in front of the vertebral column. It consists of the pharynx and larynx. An important feature of the throat is the epiglottis, a flap which separates the esophagus from the trachea and prevents inhalation of food or drink. The throat contains various blood vessels, various pharyngeal muscles, the trachea (windpipe) and the esophagus. The hyoid bone and the clavicle are the only bones located in the throat of mammals. It is sometimes considered a synonym for fauces. [WP,unvetted]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Throat]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "gula" RELATED LATIN []
xref: BTO:0000828
xref: EMAPA:37973 {source="MA:th"}
xref: FMA:228738
