namespace: uberon
def: "The ileocecal valve is a sphincter muscle situated at the junction of the small intestine (ileum) and the large intestine. Its critical function is to limit the reflux of colonic contents into the ileum." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ileocecal_valve]
