[Term]
id: UBERON:0001153
name: caecum
namespace: uberon
def: "A pouch in the digestive tract that connects the ileum with the ascending colon of the large intestine. It is separated from the ileum by the ileocecal valve, and is the beginning of the large intestine. It is also separated from the colon by the cecocolic junction." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cecum]
comment: Taxon notes: in some herbivorous lizards, a cecum is present between small and large intestines[Kardong]
