is_a: UBERON:0008571 {source="FMA"} ! suprahyoid muscle
property_value: curator_notes "this class refers to the mereological sum of digastric muscles in an organism (typically two)." xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "The digastric muscle (also digastricus) (named digastric as it has two bellies) is a small muscle located under the jaw. It lies below the body of the mandible, and extends, in a curved form, from the mastoid process to the symphysis menti. It belongs to the suprahyoid muscles group. A broad aponeurotic layer is given off from the tendon of the digastricus on either side, to be attached to body and greater cornu of the hyoid bone; this is termed the suprahyoid aponeurosis. Wikipedia:Digastric_muscle]." xsd:string {source="Digastric:muscle"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In most mammals there is a common tendon between the ant. and post. muscles, which also makes a connection to the hyoid apparatus, and then the other attachment is to the base of the cranium" xsd:string {source="FEED:rd"}

