[Term]
id: UBERON:0002045
name: cuneate nucleus
namespace: uberon
def: "One of the dorsal column nuclei, the cuneate nucleus is a wedge-shaped nucleus in the closed part of the medulla oblongata. It contains cells that give rise to the cuneate tubercle, visible on the posterior aspect of the medulla. It lies laterally to the gracile nucleus and medial to the spinal trigeminal nucleus in the medulla. [WP,unvetted]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuneate_nucleus]
subset: uberon_slim
