property_value: external_definition "Embryonic structure that forms as a thickened annulus at the blastoderm rim. The germ ring is thickened because it is the involuting margin of the blastoderm[ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-576]." xsd:string {source="ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-576"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0002542
name: scale
namespace: uberon
def: "A small rigid plate that grows out of an animal's skin to provide protection. In lepidopteran (butterfly and moth) species, scales are plates on the surface of the insect wing, and provide coloration. Scales are quite common and have evolved multiple times with varying structure and function." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scale_(zoology)]
subset: efo_slim
subset: grouping_class
synonym: "scale (sensu Metazoa)" EXACT []
