[Term]
id: UBERON:0002987
name: anterior spinocerebellar tract
namespace: uberon
def: "Runs through the ventrolateral surface of the spinal cord. It enters the cerebellum through the superior cerebellar peduncle. It crosses the midline at the segmental level and recrosses in the cerebellum. Its terminals are distributed in the cerebellar anterior lobe, preferentially in the ipsilateral intermediate cortex. Rostrally, it extends to lobule II." [BIRNLEX:848]
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "Gower's tract" EXACT [BIRNLEX:848]
synonym: "Gowers' tract" EXACT [FMA:72642]
synonym: "tractus spinocerebellaris anterior" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:808]
synonym: "tractus spinocerebellaris ventralis" RELATED LATIN [NeuroNames:808]
synonym: "ventral spinocerebellar tract" EXACT [FMA:72642]
synonym: "ventral spinocerebellar tract (Gowers)" RELATED [NeuroNames:808]
