[Term]
id: UBERON:0003914
name: epithelial tube
namespace: uberon
def: "Epithelial tubes transport gases, liquids and cells from one site to another and form the basic structure of many organs and tissues, with tube shape and organization varying from the single-celled excretory organ in Caenorhabditis elegans to the branching trees of the mammalian kidney and insect tracheal system." [GO:0060562, http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12526790]
synonym: "epithelial or endothelial tube" EXACT []
