[Term]
id: UBERON:0004068
name: medial nasal prominence
namespace: uberon
def: "The central area of the two limbs of a horseshoe-shaped mesenchymal swelling that lie medial to the olfactory placode or pit in the future nasal region of the embryo; it joins with the ipsilateral maxillary prominence in the formation of half of the upper jaw, and the nasal tip and philtrum of the upper lip develop from it" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medial_nasal_prominence, MP:0009903]
