[Term]
id: UBERON:0004179
name: prostate glandular acinus
namespace: uberon
def: "A saclike structure of the prostate gland, comprised of at least three cell layers: an innermost layer of secretory columnar luminal epithelium, a middle layer of squamous basal epithelium that also contains neuroendocrine cells, transit amplifying cells, and stem cells, and an outer layer of smooth muscle intermixed with other stromal cells" [GO:0060525, http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18977204]
synonym: "prostatic acinus" EXACT [FMA:66808]
synonym: "prostatic follicle" EXACT [FMA:66808]
xref: FMA:66808
is_a: UBERON:0009842 {source="FMA"} ! glandular acinus
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0009843 {source="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18977204"} ! prostate epithelial cord
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000428 {source="GO"} ! prostate epithelium
property_value: development_notes "Concurrent with branching morphogenesis, the solid cords of epithelium formed by budding arborize and differentiate postnatally into glandular acin. The basic prostate architecture is established by puberty and acquires secretory function thereafter[PMID:18977204]" xsd:string
property_value: editor_note "the muscle layer is implicitly treated as outside the acinus" xsd:string

