xref: EHDAA2:0001249
xref: EMAPA:16151
xref: EMAPA:16155
xref: EMAPA:16159
xref: EMAPA:16162
xref: EMAPA:32732
xref: FMA:295618
xref: http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=1364
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0814993
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/361461009
xref: NCIT:C34223
xref: Neural:fold
xref: UMLS:C0814993 {source="ncithesaurus:Neural_Fold"}
xref: XAO:0000293
xref: XAO:0004087
xref: XAO:0005242
is_a: UBERON:0005157 ! epithelial fold
is_a: UBERON:0015212 ! lateral structure
relationship: develops_from EHDAA2:0001251 {gci_relation="part_of", gci_filler="NCBITaxon:9606"} ! trunk neural ectoderm (human)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005061 ! neural groove
property_value: external_definition "In front of the primitive streak two longitudinal ridges, caused by a folding up of the ectoderm, make their appearance, one on either side of the middle line. These are named the neural folds; they commence some little distance behind the anterior end of the embryonic disk, where they are continuous with each other, and from there gradually extend backward, one on either side of the anterior end of the primitive streak. Also, after differentiation it turns into the neural tubes[Wikipedia:Neural_fold]." xsd:string {source="Neural:fold"}

