[Term]
id: UBERON:0005345
name: cerebellum vermis lobule VIIA
namespace: uberon
def: "The folium vermis is a short, narrow, concealed band at the posterior extremity of the vermis, consisting apparently of a single folium, but in reality marked on its upper and under surfaces by secondary fissures. Laterally, it expands in either hemisphere into a considerable lobule, the superior semilunar lobule (lobulus semilunaris superior; postero-superior lobules), which occupies the posterior third of the upper surface of the hemisphere, and is bounded below by the horizontal sulcus. The superior semilunar lobules and the folium vermis form the lobus semilunaris." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folium_(vermis), MP:0009998]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "folium" BROAD [MA:0001004]
synonym: "folium lobule" NARROW [MP:0009995]
synonym: "folium of cerebellum" RELATED []
synonym: "folium of vermis of cerebellum" EXACT [FMA:83889]
synonym: "neuraxis folium" RELATED [FMA:83889]
synonym: "vermic lobule VIIA" EXACT [NLXANAT:20081231]
