[Term]
id: UBERON:0005475
name: sigmoid sinus
namespace: uberon
def: "A portion of the lateral venous sinus, bulging prominently into the mastoid cavity, that serves as a principal conduit by which blood leaves the cranium[EPIC]. The sigmoid is drained by the internal jugular vein" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigmoid_sinus, http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/glossary/glossaryS.html]
synonym: "sulcus sigmoideus" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigmoid_sinus]
