[Term]
id: UBERON:0005490
name: posterior interventricular sulcus
namespace: uberon
def: "The ventricles are separated by two grooves, one of which, the anterior longitudinal sulcus, is situated on the sternocostal surface of the heart, close to its left margin, the other posterior longitudinal sulcus (posterior interventricular sulcus, inferior interventricular groove), on the diaphragmatic surface near the right margin. In it run the posterior interventricular artery and middle cardiac vein." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_interventricular_sulcus]
synonym: "diaphragmatic interventricular groove" EXACT [FMA:7178]
synonym: "inferior interventricular groove" EXACT [FMA:7178]
synonym: "posterior interventricular groove" EXACT [FMA:7178]
synonym: "posterior interventricular groove" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_interventricular_sulcus]
synonym: "posterior longitudinal sulci" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_interventricular_sulcus]
synonym: "posterior longitudinal sulcus" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_interventricular_sulcus]
synonym: "sulcus interventricularis anterior" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_interventricular_sulcus]
