[Term]
id: UBERON:0005594
name: head somite
namespace: uberon
def: "Somite located in the head region, caudal to the otic vesicle" [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11830559]
synonym: "cranial somite" RELATED [XAO:0000313]
synonym: "occipital somite" EXACT [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11830559, XAO:0000313]
xref: EHDAA2:0003437
xref: EMAPA:16172
xref: EMAPA:16173
xref: EMAPA:16174
xref: EMAPA:16175
xref: EMAPA:16176
xref: XAO:0000313
is_a: UBERON:0002329 ! somite
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0009617 {source="EHDAA2"} ! head paraxial mesoderm
relationship: part_of UBERON:0009617 {source="EHDAA2"} ! head paraxial mesoderm
property_value: development_notes "They provide the epaxial and hypaxial muscles of the neck, the pharyngeal and laryngeal muscles that develop in the caudal branchial arches and the musculature of the tongue. Despite their localisation in the head, myogenic precursors from occipital somites essentially follow the trunk programmes (E. H. Walters and S. D., unpublished). during evolution, have been secondarily incorporated into the head (Gans and Northcutt, 1983)" xsd:string {source="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11830559"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "EHDAA2 has both 'head somite' and 'head somite group', with part_of and develops_from for latter" xsd:string {external_ontology="EHDAA2"}
property_value: taxon_notes "in humans this includes somites 1-4" xsd:string

