[Term]
id: UBERON:0005816
name: posterior tubercle of transverse process of cervical vertebra
namespace: uberon
def: "The posterior arch of a cervical vertebra forms about two-fifths of the circumference of the ring: it ends behind in the posterior tubercle, which is the rudiment of a spinous process and gives origin to the Recti capitis posteriores minores. The diminutive size of this process prevents any interference with the movements between the atlas and the skull." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posterior_tubercle_of_cervical_vertebra]
