[Term]
id: UBERON:0005876
name: undifferentiated genital tubercle
namespace: uberon
def: "the embryonic anlage of the external genitalia, which emerges as paired swellings ventral to the cloacal membrane, is proposed to be derived from all three germ layers, and gives rise to the penis, clitoris, scrotum, labia, and foreskin" [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1230, MGI:anna, MP:0011771]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "genital tubercle" RELATED [EMAPA:17382]
synonym: "phallic tubercle" RELATED []
synonym: "tuberculum genitale" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genital_tubercle]
synonym: "tuberculum phallicum" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genital_tubercle]
synonym: "undifferentiated genital tubercle" EXACT [VHOG:0000583]
xref: EHDAA2:0000705
xref: EHDAA:5925
xref: EMAPA:17382
xref: EMAPA:36384
xref: FMA:302888
xref: Genital:tubercle
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/308798005
xref: VHOG:0000583
is_a: UBERON:0002050 ! embryonic structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0004874 ! somatopleure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0009196 {source="EHDAA2"} ! indifferent external genitalia
property_value: external_definition "embryonic anlage of the external genitalia, which emerges as paired swellings ventral to the cloacal membrane, is proposed to be derived from all three germ layers, and gives rise to the penis, clitoris, scrotum, labia, and foreskin; GT development is indistinguishable in male and female mouse embryos until ~E16, when the urethral plate begins to be masculinized to form the penile urethra, marking the beginning of an androgen-dependent phase of sexual differentiation[MP]" xsd:string {ontology="MP"}
property_value: external_definition "The eminence in the embryo which develops into the clitoris or penis. [TFD][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000583", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/genital+tubercle"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "we assume the EMAPA class is the undifferentiated form based on TS timings" xsd:string {external_ontology="EMAPA"}
property_value: homology_notes "In mammalian embryos, male and female external genitalia develop from the genital tubercle.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000583", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="DOI:10.1242/dev.036830 Seifert AW, Yamaguchi T, Cohn MJ, Functional and phylogenetic analysis shows that Fgf8 is a marker of genital induction in mammals but is not required for external genital development. Development (2009)"}
property_value: taxon_notes "All amniotes studied to date initiate external genital development with the formation of paired genital swellings. In mammals, archosaurs, and turtles, these swellings merge to form a single genital tubercle, the precursor of the penis and clitoris[PMID:24960313]" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "GT development is indistinguishable in male and female mouse embryos until approximately E16, when the urethral plate begins to be masculinized to form the penile urethra, marking the beginning of an androgen-dependent phase of sexual differentiation[MP:0011771]" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "todo - add taxon constraints" xsd:string

