[Term]
id: UBERON:0005880
name: prepollex
namespace: uberon
def: "A rudimentary additional digit-like structure on the preaxial side of the thumb of certain amphibians and mammals[dictionary.com]." [http://dictionary.com]
comment: not homologous to digit 1 of tetrapods. Note we treat the prepollex as distinct from the digits, which are not part of the carpus
synonym: "pseudothumb" RELATED [https://doi.org/10.1098/rsbl.2009.1038]
is_a: UBERON:0005881 ! autopodial extension
relationship: part_of UBERON:0004452 ! carpal region
property_value: external_definition "Two or more elements located ventral and medial to the metacarpal of digit II(I). The proximal prepollex is small and round whereas distal prepollex 1 is usually large and wedge-shaped. When more elements are present, they are smaller than previous elements.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000852", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:LAP"}

