[Term]
id: UBERON:0005903
name: duct of seminal vesicle
namespace: uberon
def: "Each seminal vesicle consists of a single tube, coiled upon itself, and giving off several irregular cecal diverticula; the separate coils, as well as the diverticula, are connected together by fibrous tissue. When uncoiled, the tube is about the diameter of a quill, and varies in length from 10 to 15 cm.; it ends posteriorly in a cul-de-sac; its anterior extremity becomes constricted into a narrow straight duct called the excretory duct of seminal gland (or duct of the seminal vesicle), which joins with the corresponding ductus deferens to form the ejaculatory duct[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excretory_duct_of_seminal_gland]
synonym: "ductus excretorius (vesicula seminalis)" EXACT [FMA:19473]
synonym: "ductus excretorius glandulae vesiculosae" EXACT LATIN [FMA:19473, FMA:TA]
synonym: "ductus excretorius glandulae vesiculosae" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excretory_duct_of_seminal_gland]
synonym: "excretory duct of seminal gland" EXACT [FMA:19473]
synonym: "seminal vesicle duct" EXACT [FMA:19473]
xref: EMAPA:29282
xref: FMA:19473
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excretory_duct_of_seminal_gland
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/279675008
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000998 ! seminal vesicle

