is_a: UBERON:0015212 ! lateral structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0006332 {source="ISBN:1588903958"} ! nasal capsule
relationship: part_of UBERON:0011156 ! facial skeleton
property_value: external_ontology_notes "in FMA this is not classified with the other turbinates. In Uberon we subdivide the turbinates into the ethmoturbinates and the inferior turbinate. EDITOR NOTE: TODO check ethmoidal process of inferior nasal concha" xsd:string {external_ontology="FMA"}
property_value: function_notes "While the maxilloturbinates of mammals are located in the path of airflow to collect moisture, sensory turbinates in both mammals and reptiles are positioned farther back and above the nasal passage, away from the flow of air" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "In many carnivores and ungulates, the maxilloturbinal is the most complex element immediately posterior to the vestibule[PMID:25312359]" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0005925
name: ethmoidal process of inferior nasal concha
namespace: uberon
def: "Behind the lacrimal process of the inferior nasal conchae lies a broad, thin plate, the ethmoidal process, which ascends to join the uncinate process of the ethmoid; from its lower border a thin lamina, the maxillary process, curves downward and lateralward; it articulates with the maxilla and forms a part of the medial wall of the maxillary sinus." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethmoid_boneal_process_of_inferior_nasal_concha]
synonym: "ethmoidal process of inferior concha" EXACT [FMA:54742]
synonym: "ethmoidal process of inferior nasal turbinate" EXACT [FMA:54742]
synonym: "ethmoidal process of inferior turbinate" EXACT [FMA:54742]
synonym: "ethmoturbinal" RELATED [UBERON:cjm]
synonym: "processus ethmoidalis (concha nasalis inferior)" EXACT [FMA:54742]
synonym: "processus ethmoidalis conchae nasalis inferioris" EXACT LATIN [FMA:54742, FMA:TA]
synonym: "processus ethmoidalis conchae nasalis inferioris" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethmoidal_process_of_inferior_nasal_concha]
xref: FMA:54742
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethmoid_boneal_process_of_inferior_nasal_concha
is_a: UBERON:0004530 ! bony projection
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005922 ! inferior nasal concha
property_value: taxon_notes "In many carnivores and ungulates, the ethmoturbinals are most complex within a posterosuperior cul-de-sac, the olfactory recess[PMID:25312359]" xsd:string

