[Term]
id: UBERON:0006009
name: cusp of cardiac valve
namespace: uberon
def: "The part of the heart valves that serves to seal the heart valves when closed. There are three cusps for each valve except for the mitral valve, which has only two (hence its alternate name, 'bicuspid valve'). 'Nodules' are located at the tip of the valve, to form a tighter seal[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cusps_of_heart_valves]
synonym: "cardiac valve cusp" EXACT [FMA:7232]
synonym: "cardiac valvular cusp" EXACT [FMA:7232]
synonym: "cardiac valvule" EXACT [FMA:7232]
synonym: "cardial valve cusp" EXACT []
synonym: "semilunar valvule" EXACT [FMA:7232]
xref: FMA:7232
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cusps_of_heart_valves
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0225923
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/30822008
xref: NCIT:C33849
xref: UMLS:C0225923 {source="ncithesaurus:Cardiac_Valve_Cusp"}
