is_a: UBERON:0003496 ! head blood vessel
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001101 ! external jugular vein
property_value: taxon_notes "In humans this refers to either the anterior or posterior auricular vein, passing in front of or behind the ear. This class also groups other auricular veins, including the greater, ventral, central auricular nerves. These may exhibit different branching structures. In the pig, the external jugular branches to the maxillary to the caudal auricular to the middle auricular, then onto various unique patterns" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006198
name: dorsal intercostal artery
namespace: uberon
def: "The highest intercostal artery (supreme intercostal artery, superior intercostal artery) is an artery in the human body that usually gives rise to the first and second posterior intercostal arteries, which supply blood to their corresponding intercostal space. It usually arises from the costocervical trunk, which is a branch of the subclavian artery." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_intercostal_artery]
comment: classes unified on basis of spatial anatomy ontology synonyms
synonym: "arteria intercostalis suprema" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_intercostal_artery]
synonym: "dorsal branch of superior intercostal artery" RELATED [http://www.mondofacto.com/facts/dictionary?dorsal+branch+of+the+superior+intercostal+artery]
synonym: "superior intercostal artery" EXACT [FMA:76998, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_intercostal_artery]
synonym: "supreme intercostal artery" EXACT [FMA:76998, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_intercostal_artery]
xref: EMAPA:37078 {source="MA:th"}
