[Term]
id: UBERON:0006257
name: laryngotracheal groove
namespace: uberon
def: "A groove in the floor of the pharynx formed from the ventral diverticulum of endoderm that arises from the floor of the foregut caudal to the pharynx. This structure is the precursor for the larynx and trachea[WP,edited]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laryngotracheal_groove, http://isc.temple.edu/marino/embryology/resp98/respdev.htm]
synonym: "laryngo-tracheal groove" EXACT [EHDAA2:0004073]
synonym: "laryngo-tracheal tube" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laryngotracheal_groove]
synonym: "laryngotracheal endoderm" RELATED []
synonym: "sulcus laryngotrachealis" EXACT LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laryngotracheal_groove]
xref: EHDAA2:0004073
xref: EHDAA:1005
xref: EMAPA:16739
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C1283960
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/361426003
xref: Laryngotracheal:groove
xref: NCIT:C34198
xref: RETIRED_EHDAA2:0000909
xref: UMLS:C1283960 {source="ncithesaurus:Laryngotracheal_Tube"}
xref: VHOG:0001404
is_a: UBERON:0006846 {source="EHDAA2"} ! surface groove
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000922 ! embryo
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001041 {source="EHDAA2"} ! foregut
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001558 {source="EHDAA2"} ! lower respiratory tract
property_value: editor_note "Note we currently have pharynx as part of the upper respiratory tract - separate by development?" xsd:string
property_value: homology_notes "Lung development begins with the appearance of the laryngotracheal groove, which is a small diverticulum that arises from the floor of the primitive pharynx at E9 in mouse and 4 wk in human.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001404", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="PMID:15817505 Warburton D, Bellusci S, De Langhe S, Del Moral PM, Fleury V, Mailleux A, Tefft D, Unbekandt M, Wang K, Shi W, Molecular mechanisms of early lung specification and branching morphogenesis. Pediatric Research (2005)"}

