name: superior rectus extraocular muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "The superior rectus muscle is a muscle in the orbit. It is one of the extraocular muscles. It is innervated by the superior division of the oculomotor nerve (Cranial Nerve III). In the primary position (looking straight ahead), the superior rectus muscle's primary function is elevation, although it also contributes to intorsion and adduction." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_rectus_muscle]
subset: pheno_slim
subset: vertebrate_core
synonym: "dorsal recti" RELATED PLURAL [ZFA:0000345]
synonym: "dorsal rectus" RELATED [TAO:0000345]
synonym: "dorsal rectus extraocular muscle" EXACT [VHOG:0001128]
synonym: "m. rectus superior" EXACT []
synonym: "musculus rectus superior" EXACT [AAO:0010099]
synonym: "musculus rectus superior bulbi" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_rectus_muscle]
synonym: "superior rectus" EXACT [FMA:49035]
synonym: "superior rectus muscle" EXACT []
xref: AAO:0010099
xref: FMA:49035
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_rectus_muscle
