[Term]
id: UBERON:0006587
name: ligamentum venosum
namespace: uberon
def: "The ligamentum venosum is the fibrous remnant of the ductus venosus of the fetal circulation. Usually, it is attached to the left branch of the portal vein within the porta hepatis (gateway to the liver). It may be continuous with the round ligament of liver (ligamentum teres hepatis). It is invested by the peritoneal folds of the lesser omentum within a fissure on the inferior surface of the liver between the caudate and main parts of the left lobe." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ligamentum_venosum]
synonym: "ligament of arantius" EXACT [FMA:14080]
synonym: "ligamentum venosum (ductus venosus)" EXACT [FMA:14080]
synonym: "ligamentum venosum of liver" EXACT [FMA:14080]
synonym: "ligamentum venosus" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ligamentum_venosum]
xref: FMA:14080
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/80391004
xref: Ligamentum:venosum
is_a: UBERON:0006592 {source="FMA"} ! transformed vein
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002083 ! ductus venosus

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006588
name: round ligament of liver
namespace: uberon
def: "A degenerative string of tissue that exists in the free edge of the falciform ligament of the liver. Anatomically, the round ligament divides the left part of the liver into medial and lateral sections. The round ligament represents the remnant of the fetal left umbilical vein. The round ligament therefore only exists in mammals. Prenatally and for a month or two after birth, the left umbilical vein is patent, subsequently degenerating to fibrous tissue, the round ligament. The umbilical vein/round ligament inserts around the umbilicus and is an important landmark of the inner surface of the anterior abdominal wall[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres" BROAD [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres hepatis" EXACT LATIN [FMA:14079, FMA:TA]
synonym: "ligamentum teres hepatitis" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres of liver" EXACT [FMA:14079]
xref: FMA:14079
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_liver
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0230247
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/262209009
xref: NCIT:C34008
xref: UMLS:C0230247 {source="ncithesaurus:Round_Ligament_of_the_Liver"}
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0006592 ! transformed vein
is_a: UBERON:0013139 ! ligament of liver
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002066 ! umbilical vein

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006589
name: round ligament of uterus
namespace: uberon
def: "The round ligament of the uterus originates at the uterine horns, in the parametrium. It leaves the pelvis via the deep inguinal ring, passes through the inguinal canal and continues on to the labia majora where its fibers spread and mix with the tissue of the mons pubis[WP]. A fibromuscular band that attaches to the uterus and then passes along the broad ligament, out through the inguinal ring, and into the labium majus[MESH]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_uterus, MESH:A02.513.803]
synonym: "Hunter's ligament" EXACT [FMA:20420]
synonym: "ligamentum teres of uterus" EXACT []
synonym: "ligamentum teres uteri" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_uterus]
synonym: "ligamentum teres uteri" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_uterus]
synonym: "round ligament" BROAD [GAID:130]
synonym: "round ligament of the uterus" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_ligament_of_uterus]
