name: long head of biceps brachii
namespace: uberon
def: "The long head originates on the supraglenoid tubercle just above the shoulder joint from where its tendon passes down along the intertubercular groove of the humerus into the joint capsule of the shoulder joint. [1] When the humerus is in motion, the tendon of the long head is held firmly in place in the intertubercular groove by the greater and lesser tubercles and the overlying transverse humeral ligament. During the motion from external to internal rotation, the tendon is forced medially against the lesser tubercle and superiorly against the transverse ligament." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biceps_brachii_muscle#Origin_and_insertion]
synonym: "capus longum of biceps brachii" RELATED [EMAPA:25054]
synonym: "caput longum (musculus biceps brachii)" EXACT [FMA:37683]
synonym: "caput longum musculus bicipitis brachii" EXACT LATIN [FMA:37683, FMA:TA]
synonym: "long head of biceps brachii muscle" RELATED [FMA:37683]
xref: EMAPA:25054
xref: FMA:37683
xref: Origin_and_insertion
is_a: UBERON:0011906 {source="FMA"} ! muscle head
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000043 ! tendon
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001507 ! biceps brachii

[Term]
id: UBERON:0007169
name: short head of biceps brachii
namespace: uberon
def: "Proximally (towards the body), the short head of the biceps attaches to (originates from) the coracoid process at the top of the scapula." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biceps_brachii_muscle#Origin_and_insertion]
