[Term]
id: UBERON:0007193
name: orbital gyrus
namespace: uberon
def: "The inferior or orbital surface of the frontal lobe is concave, and rests on the orbital plate of the frontal bone. It is divided into four orbital gyri by a well-marked H-shaped orbital sulcus. These are named, from their position, the medial, anterior, lateral, and posterior orbital gyri. The medial orbital gyrus presents a well-marked antero-posterior sulcus, the olfactory sulcus, for the olfactory tract; the portion medial to this is named the straight gyrus, and is continuous with the superior frontal gyrus on the medial surface." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orbital_gyri]
synonym: "gyrus orbitales" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orbital_gyri]
synonym: "orbital gyri" EXACT PLURAL [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orbital_gyri]
xref: BAMS:OrG
xref: FMA:256194
xref: http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=91
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/280372002
xref: Orbital:gyri
is_a: UBERON:0000200 ! gyrus
relationship: part_of UBERON:0016525 ! frontal lobe

[Term]
id: UBERON:0007194
name: vesicular gland
namespace: uberon
def: "The vesicular gland is part of the male reproductive system. The vesicular gland contributes fluids, energy substrates, and buffers to semen. It can be found near the Coagulating gland, which also belongs to the reproductive system." [BTO:0003717]
xref: BTO:0003717
xref: EMAPA:19180
xref: MA:0000405
xref: ncithesaurus:Vesicular_Gland
is_a: UBERON:0010147 ! male accessory sex gland
property_value: editor_note "TODO - check this against seminal vesicle" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "bipartite seminal vesicles, with a seminal gland and vesicular gland sharing a common duct are found in lagomorphs" xsd:string {source="Lombardi"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0007195
name: stroma of bone marrow
namespace: uberon
def: "The stroma of the bone marrow is all tissue not directly involved in the primary function of hematopoiesis. The yellow bone marrow belongs here, and makes the majority of the bone marrow stroma, in addition to stromal cells located in the red bone marrow. Yellow bone marrow is found in the Medullary cavity. Still, the stroma is indirectly involved in hematopoiesis, since it provides the hematopoietic microenvironment that facilitates hematopoiesis by the parenchymal cells. For instance, they generate colony stimulating factors, affecting hematopoiesis." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_marrow#Stroma]
synonym: "bone marrow stroma" EXACT [FMA:21426]
xref: CALOHA:TS-0085
xref: FMA:21426
xref: Stroma
is_a: UBERON:0003891 ! stroma
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002371 ! bone marrow

