[Term]
id: UBERON:0007358
name: abomasum
namespace: uberon
def: "The fourth stomach of ruminating animals, which is an elongated pear-shaped sac lying on the floor of the abdomen, on the right-hand side, and roughly between the seventh and twelfth ribs. It leads to the beginning of the small intestine. (Adapted From Black's Veterinary Dictionary, 17th ed)" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum, MESH:A13.869.106, UBERON:cjm]
subset: organ_slim
synonym: "fourth stomach" RELATED [BTO:0000024]
synonym: "maw" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum]
synonym: "read" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum]
synonym: "rennet-bag" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum]
synonym: "ruminant true stomach" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum]
xref: BTO:0000024
xref: GAID:1241
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abomasum
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0000780
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/410028001
xref: MESH:D000018
xref: NCIT:C98702
