[Term]
id: UBERON:0007689
name: thyroid diverticulum
namespace: uberon
def: "endodermal bud derived from the endodermal epithelium of the embryonic pharyngeal floor[MP]. The thyroid diverticulum is the embryological structure from which thyroid follicular cells derive. It grows from the floor of the pharnyx[WP]." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroid_diverticulum, MP:0004662]
synonym: "diverticulum thyroideum" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroid_diverticulum]
