[Term]
id: UBERON:0007703
name: spinothalamic tract
namespace: uberon
def: "A tract that originates from neurons in the spinal central gray and projects to various somatosensory nuclei of the thalamus. It is formed in the medulla by merger of the anterior spinothalamic tract and lateral spinothalamic tract (adapted from Braininfo.org)" [NLXANAT:1010017]
xref: BAMS:spth
xref: BAMS:stt
xref: DHBA:12789
xref: http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=2058
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/280417000
xref: MBA:871
xref: NLXANAT:1010017
xref: Spinothalamic:tract
is_a: UBERON:0007702 ! tract of brain
property_value: external_definition "a long process of a CNS neuron, that carries efferent (outgoing) action potentials from the cell body in the spinal cord towards target cells in the thalamus. This axonal process is a member of those that make up the spinothalamic tract, one of the major routes of nociceptive signaling[GO][GO:0021963]." xsd:string {source="GO:0021963"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0007707
name: superior cerebellar peduncle of midbrain
namespace: uberon
def: "Regional part of superior cerebellar peduncle, located in the midbrain, consisting of a large bundle of fibers largely projecting from the deep cerebellar nuclei to the midbrain and thalamus. It is continuous with the superior cerebellar peduncle of the pons. (MM)." [BIRNLEX:1162]
