[Term]
id: UBERON:0007722
name: interphalangeal joint of manus
namespace: uberon
def: "The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): 'proximal interphalangeal joints' (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges 'distal interphalangeal joints' (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "articulationes digitorum manus" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "articulationes interphalangeae manus" EXACT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "articulations of the digits" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "interphalangeal articulations of hand" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "interphalangeal joint of finger" NARROW SENSU [FMA:35285, NCBITaxon:9606]
synonym: "interphalangeal joint of hand" EXACT [FMA:35285]
synonym: "interphalangeal joints of hand" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand]
synonym: "IP joint" RELATED [FMA:35285]
xref: EMAPA:36336
xref: FMA:35285
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interphalangeal_articulations_of_the_hand
xref: http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0016125
xref: http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/303280009
xref: NCIT:C32868
xref: UMLS:C0016125 {source="ncithesaurus:Interphalangeal_Joint_of_the_Hand"}
