[Term]
id: UBERON:0007843
name: uncinate process of ribs
namespace: uberon
def: "A posterior projection from proximal rib segments. Offers attachment sites for respiratory and shoulder muscles as well as adding structural support to the trunk skeleton[Kardong 2012]." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/96, ISBN:0073040584, PHENOSCAPE:ad]
comment: WP: Although bony uncinate processes are unique to birds, cartilaginous uncinate processes are present in crocodiles. The uncinate process has also been reported in Sphenodon, Caudipteryx, oviraptorids, Confuciusornis and Chaoyangia however it does not occur in Archaeopteryx
synonym: "uncinate process" BROAD INCONSISTENT [AAO:0000741]
xref: AAO:0000741
xref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncinate_processes_of_ribs
relationship: dc-contributor https://github.com/alex-dececchi
relationship: dc-contributor https://github.com/cmungall
relationship: part_of UBERON:0010388 {source="ISBN:0073040584"} ! proximal segment of rib
property_value: external_definition "Posteriorly directed process (occasionally directed anteriorly) usually associated with the rib (sometimes with the transverse process) of the third vertebra; they provide the origin of the mm serratus superior, medius, and inferior.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000741", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:Pugener_2002"}

