[Term]
id: UBERON:0007845
name: regular connective tissue
namespace: uberon
def: "Connective tissue, which consists of fibroblasts, the intercellular matrix of which contains a regular network of collagen and elastic fiber bundles. Examples: bone (tissue), cartilage (tissue), dense regular connective tissue." [FMA:20103]
xref: FMA:20103
is_a: UBERON:0002384 {source="FMA"} ! connective tissue
property_value: editor_note "the connective tissue hierarchy largely follows FMA with definitions from VSAO. Note that in FMA, loose-CT is irregular-CT. This means regular-CT is necessarily equivalent to dense-regular-CT (assuming a JEPD classification)." xsd:string

