[Term]
id: UBERON:0008449
name: trochlear notch
namespace: uberon
def: "The semilunar notch of the ulna (trochlear notch of ulna, greater sigmoid cavity) is a large depression, formed by the olecranon and the coronoid process, and serving for articulation with the trochlea of the humerus. About the middle of either side of this notch is an indentation, which contracts it somewhat, and indicates the junction of the olecranon and the coronoid process. The notch is concave from above downward, and divided into a medial and a lateral portion by a smooth ridge running from the summit of the olecranon to the tip of the coronoid process. The medial portion is the larger, and is slightly concave transversely; the lateral is convex above, slightly concave below." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochlear_notch]
synonym: "incisura semilunaris ulnae" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochlear_notch]
synonym: "incisura trochlearis" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochlear_notch]
synonym: "incisura trochlearis ulnae" RELATED LATIN [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochlear_notch]
synonym: "semilunar notch" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochlear_notch]
synonym: "semilunar notch of ulna" EXACT [FMA:23619]
xref: FMA:23619
xref: Trochlear:notch
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006822 ! proximal epiphysis of ulna

[Term]
id: UBERON:0008450
name: psoas muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A powerful flexor of the thigh at the hip joint (psoas major) and a weak flexor of the trunk and lumbar spinal column (psoas minor). Psoas is derived from the Greek 'psoa', the plural meaning 'muscles of the loin'. It is a common site of infection manifesting as abscess (PSOAS ABSCESS). The psoas muscles and their fibers are also used frequently in experiments in muscle physiology." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psoas, MESH:A02.633.567.825]
synonym: "psoas" EXACT [MA:0002553]
synonym: "psoas" EXACT [BTO:0001140]
