[Term]
id: UBERON:0008523
name: infrahyoid muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "The infrahyoid muscles are a group of four pairs of muscles in the anterior part of the neck. (The term infrahyoid refers to the region below to the hyoid bone in the neck. ) Collectively, they are referred to as the strap muscles, because the muscles are long and flat much like a strap." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrahyoid_muscles]
