relationship: part_of UBERON:0004161 {notes="caudal part", source="EHDAA2"} ! septum transversum
property_value: development_notes "The caudal part of the septum transversum is invaded by the hepatic diverticulum which divides within it to form the liver and thus gives rise to the ventral mesentery of the foregut." xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "in mice, the hepatic diverticulum forms by E9 and expands into an obvious liver bud by E10" xsd:string

