is_a: UBERON:0000325 ! gastric gland
is_a: UBERON:0000414 {source="MP"} ! mucous gland
relationship: part_of UBERON:0004996 {source="FMA"} ! mucosa of cardia of stomach
property_value: external_definition "The cardiac glands of the stomach secrete primarily mucus. They are few in number and occur close to the cardiac orifice where the esophagus joins the stomach. In general, they are more shallow than those in the other parts of the stomach. They are of two kinds: (1) simple tubular glands resembling those of the pyloric end of the stomach, but with short ducts. (2) compound racemose glands resembling the duodenal glands. The cardiac gland is both innervated by the parasympathetic and symapthetic nerve fibres of the autonomic nervous system[Wikipedia:Cardiac_glands]." xsd:string {source="Cardiac:glands"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "Kardong places this in the glandular epithelium, FMA more generally in the mucosa" xsd:string {external_ontology="FMA"}

