[Term]
id: UBERON:0008887
name: rectal venous plexus
namespace: uberon
def: "The hemorrhoidal plexus (or rectal venous plexus) surrounds the rectum, and communicates in front with the vesical venous plexus in the male, and the uterovaginal plexus in the female. A free communication between the portal and systemic venous systems is established through the hemorrhoidal plexus." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectal_venous_plexus]
synonym: "haemorrhoidal plexus" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectal_venous_plexus]
