property_value: development_notes "may be formed from entotympanic and ectotympanic" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "In extant primates, the structure is found in tarsiers, lemurs, and lorises[WP]. When present in marsupials, it usually forms the alisphenoid; in placentals variously constructed of ectotympanic, entotympanic, petrosal, or a combination of these and others" xsd:string {source="Rose"}

