relationship: develops_from UBERON:0010289 {source="ZFA"} ! scleral cartilage
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002241 {source="ZFA"} ! chondrocranium
property_value: external_definition "A pair of small dish-shaped bones that cap the anterior and posterior margin of the eyeball.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0001411", ontology="TAO", source="ZFIN:curator"}
property_value: taxon_notes "The scleral ossicles [of teleosts] are reported to form indirectly by endochondral (Hall and Miyake, 1992) or by perichondral ossification (Patterson, 1977) from a cartilage element that is also present in the sclera. This is unlike the scleral ossicles of reptiles, which develop directly from ectomesenchyme (i.e., intramembranous ossification) and independently from the scleral cartilage" xsd:string {source="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17051547"}

