[Term]
id: UBERON:0010754
name: germinal center
namespace: uberon
def: "A collection of activated B cells at the center of a secondary follicle, formed after B cells become activated and migrate to the center." [CL:tm, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germinal_center, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
comment: A germinal center is a specialized microenvironment formed when activated B cells enter lymphoid follicles. Germinal centers are the foci for B cell proliferation and somatic hypermutation.[GO]
synonym: "central zone of follice" EXACT [CL:tm]
synonym: "light zone of follicle" EXACT [CL:tm]
synonym: "lymhpoid nodule" RELATED [CL:tm]
synonym: "nodule" RELATED [CL:tm]
synonym: "reaction center of follicle" EXACT [CL:tm]
