name: ureteral orifice
namespace: uberon
def: "The slit-like opening of either ureter into the bladder; normally, the two ureteral orifices are placed at the posterolateral angles of the urinary bladder trigone while the internal urethral orifice is placed at its anteroinferior angle (apex); wide gaping usually indicates vesicoureteral reflux" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orifice_of_ureter, MP:0011783]
