[Term]
id: UBERON:0013730
name: mycetome
namespace: uberon
def: "A specialized organ that is linked to the gut in beetles and host to a symbiotic yeast. The yeast cells assist in the digestion of less nutritious foods, supply needed B-vitamins and sterols, and provide resistance to certain toxins." [ENVO:01000166, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lasioderma_serricorne, PLB:plb]
xref: ENVO:01000166
is_a: UBERON:0010001 ! cell cluster organ
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003917 ! arthropod fat body
property_value: external_definition "either of a pair of organs in an insect (as a true bug) that consist of a cellular mass of mycetocytes and are located one in either fat body. a cell in various insects (as most true bugs) of a type that contains unicellular and prob. symbiotic fungi and is usu. clustered with others of its kind into paired mycetomes. ." xsd:string {source="http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/mycetome"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0013731
name: basilar papilla
namespace: uberon
def: "The auditory sensory organ of lizards, amphibians, and birds, which is homologous to the Corti in mammals." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilar_papilla]
synonym: "basilar papillae" RELATED PLURAL [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
synonym: "papilla basilaris" EXACT LATIN [AAO:0011018]
synonym: "sensory epithelium of recessus basilaris" RELATED []
xref: AAO:0011018
xref: VHOG:0001567
xref: XAO:0003145
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001855 {source="MA-abduced"} ! cochlear duct of membranous labyrinth
property_value: editor_note "consider classifying as a sensory epithelium" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "A sensory structure in the lagenar portion of an amphibian's membranous labyrinth between the oval and round windows.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0011018", ontology="AAO", source="XAO:curator"}

