[Term]
id: UBERON:0014685
name: pterygoid plexus
namespace: uberon
def: "The pterygoid plexus is a venous plexus of considerable size, and is situated between the temporalis muscle and lateral pterygoid muscle, and partly between the two pterygoid muscles." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterygoid_plexus]
synonym: "middle meningeal vein" RELATED [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterygoid_plexus]
