[Term]
id: UBERON:0014719
name: intralobular duct
namespace: uberon
def: "A duct that is located within a lobule, with no more connective tissue intervening between ducts and secretory units (i.e., acini or tubules) than between adjacent secretory units. Intercalated and striated ducts are intralobular" [http://www.siumed.edu/~dking2/intro/glands.htm]
