[Term]
id: UBERON:0035095
name: extensor caudae lateralis muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "A muscle that originates via a robust tendon from a tuberosity on the cranial aspect of the iliac crest and via fleshy fibers from the caudoventral aspect of the pelvis, the lateral aspects of the transverse processes of Ca2-8 or 9, and the horizontal intramuscular septum." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22753107]
synonym: "extensor caudae lateralis" EXACT []
