[Term]
id: UBERON:0035180
name: sigmoid artery
namespace: uberon
def: "The sigmoid arteries, two or three in number, run obliquely downward and to the left behind the peritoneum and in front of the Psoas major, ureter, and internal spermatic vessels. Their branches supply the lower part of the descending colon, the iliac colon, and the sigmoid or pelvic colon; anastomosing above with the left colic, and below with the superior hemorrhoidal artery." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigmoid_arteries]
