id: UBERON:0036148
name: orovelar muscle
namespace: uberon
def: "." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1264]
is_a: UBERON:0001630 ! muscle organ

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036149
name: suprapubic skin
namespace: uberon
def: "Area of skin in the hypoastric region of the abdomen." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1272]
synonym: "hypogastric skin" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0001416 ! skin of abdomen
relationship: part_of UBERON:0013203 ! hypogastrium

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036150
name: skin appendage follicle
namespace: uberon
def: "An organ subunit in the skin that gives rise to cutaneous appendage." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1266, UBERON:cjm]
synonym: "cutaneous appendage follicle" EXACT []
synonym: "follicle" BROAD []
synonym: "skin follicle" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000063 ! organ subunit
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000014 ! zone of skin

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036151
name: diffuse placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which the chorionic sac meets the uterine endometrium over its entire surface. The villi of the chorion are distributed evenly throughout the surface of the chorion, and they extend into processes in the uterine endometrium." [http://www.luckyhit.net/goats001.htm, http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: structure_notes "Almost the entire surface of the allantochorion is involved in formation of the placenta" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "horses, pigs" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036152
name: cotyledonary placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which the villi clumped together into circular patches called cotyledons. The fetal cotyledon meets with maternal regions called caruncles to form the placentome where maternal-fetal exchanges take place." [http://www.luckyhit.net/goats001.htm, http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: structure_notes "Multiple, discrete areas of attachment called cotyledons are formed by interaction of patches of allantochorion with endometrium. The fetal portions of this type of placenta are called cotyledons, the maternal contact sites (caruncles), and the cotyledon-caruncle complex a placentome" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "common to ungulates such as cows, deer, goat, and giraffes" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036153
name: zonary placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which the chorionic villi have aggregated to form a broad band that circles about the center of the chorion. Such zones may be complete circles (such as those in dogs and cats) or incomplete (such as those in bears and seals). It is thought that zonary placentae form from diffuse placentae in which the villi at the ends regress, leaving only those in the center to function. At the edges of the zonary placenta is the hemophagous organ, which is green. The color is due to the degradation of hemoglobin into bilivirdin. This green organ provides iron for the developing fetus." [http://www.luckyhit.net/goats001.htm, http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: structure_notes "The placenta takes the form of a complete or incomplete band of tissue surrounding the fetus" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "characteristic of carnivores" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036154
name: discoid placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which part of the chorion remains smooth, while the other part interacts with the endometrium to form the placenta. The maternal blood cells are in direct contact with the fetal chorion." [http://www.luckyhit.net/goats001.htm, http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: structure_notes "A single placenta is formed and is discoid in shape" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "seen in numerous groups -- humans, mice, insectivores, rabbits, rats, and monkeys" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036161
name: epitheliochorial placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which all three maternal layers are retained." [http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: taxon_notes "Horses, swine, ruminants" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036162
name: endotheliochorial placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which the only maternal layer retained is the uterine endothelium." [http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: taxon_notes "dogs, cats" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036163
name: hemochorial placenta
namespace: uberon
def: "A placenta in which no maternal layers are retained." [http://www.vivo.colostate.edu/hbooks/pathphys/reprod/placenta/structure.html]
is_a: UBERON:0001987 ! placenta
property_value: taxon_notes "humans, rodents" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036164
name: ambient gyrus
namespace: uberon
def: "a rostral part of the parahippocampal gyrus." [NeuroNames:2072]
synonym: "AG" RELATED ABBREVIATION [DHBA:12166]
