[Term]
id: UBERON:2002122
name: pouch scale
namespace: uberon/phenoscape-anatomy
def: "Scale that forms part of the posterior border of the caudal-fin organ. Pouch scales are usually hypertrophied." [TAO:wd]
comment: Definition reference: Weitzman SH, Menezes NA. 1998. Relationships of the tribes and genera of the Glandulocaudiinae (Ostariophysi: Characiformes: Characidae), with a description of a new genus. In: Malabarba LR, Reis RE, Vari RP, Lucena ZMS, Lucena CAS, editors. Phylogeny and Classification of Neotropical Fishes. Porto Alegre: EDIPUCRS. p 171-192.
