[Term]
id: UBERON:4300151
name: pelvic intercleithral cartilage
def: "Cartilage element that lies between processes of the cleithrum and pelvic girdle in gobioid fishes. Posterodorsal to the ventral end of each cleithrum is a posteriorly projecting process. The pelvic intercleithral cartilage (an unpaired, median structure) forms a bridge between the processes (From Springer, 1983)." [http://www.sil.si.edu/smithsoniancontributions/Zoology/pdf_hi/SCTZ-0390.pdf]
