def: "The 11th somite located posterior to the head." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: UBERON:0005598 ! trunk somite

[Term]
id: XAO:0000422
name: tail somite 14 (Xenopus)
def: "The 12th somite located posterior to the head. This somite is resorbed at metamorphosis." [XAO:EJS]
synonym: "trunk somite 14" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0009621 ! tail somite

[Term]
id: XAO:0000423
name: tail somite 15 (Xenopus)
def: "The 13th somite located posterior to the head. This somite is resorbed at metamorphosis." [XAO:EJS]
synonym: "trunk somite 15" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0009621 ! tail somite

[Term]
id: XAO:0000424
name: tail somite 16 (Xenopus)
def: "The 14th somite located posterior to the head. This somite forms at NF stage 28, by which time head somite 1 has degenerated, and it is resorbed at metamorphosis." [XAO:curators]
synonym: "trunk somite 16" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0009621 ! tail somite

[Term]
id: XAO:0000425
name: tail somite 17 (Xenopus)
def: "The 15th somite located posterior to the head. This somite is resorbed at metamorphosis." [XAO:EJS]
synonym: "trunk somite 17" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0009621 ! tail somite

[Term]
id: XAO:0000439
name: filter chamber (Xenopus)
def: "The structure that enables tadpoles, which are suspension feeders, to trap food particles. The palatoquadrate, ceratohyal and the connecting muscles are responsible for the irrigation and ventilation of the filter apparatus." [XAO:curators]
synonym: "coelom" RELATED []
synonym: "coelomic filter chamber" RELATED []
synonym: "filter apparatus" EXACT []
synonym: "peribranchial chamber" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000464 ! anatomical space
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003081 ! lateral plate mesoderm

[Term]
id: XAO:0000441
name: infraorbital lateral line primordium (Xenopus)
def: "Lateral line primordium which migrates ventrad along the posterior and ventral margin of the eye." [PMID:2652193]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: XAO:0004411 ! lateral line primordium (Xenopus)
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0009128 ! lateral line placode

[Term]
id: XAO:0000443
name: trunk lateral line (Xenopus)
def: "A lateral line that is present on the trunk of the organism." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: UBERON:0010202 ! lateral line

[Term]
id: XAO:0000460
name: hyomandibular lateral line (Xenopus)
def: "Lateral line complex that radiates on the ventral side of the head from a point between the eye and the base of the larval tentacle." [PMID:2652193]
is_a: UBERON:0010202 ! lateral line
relationship: develops_from XAO:0000441 ! infraorbital lateral line primordium (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0000461
name: trunk placode (Xenopus)
def: "Thickened plate of ectoderm that contributes to the formation of the dorsal, middle, or ventral lateral line." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from XAO:0000320 ! sensorial layer (Xenopus)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000924 ! ectoderm

[Term]
id: XAO:0000464
name: ventral lateral line (Xenopus)
def: "Ventrally located lateral line that runs over the abdomen." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: UBERON:0010202 ! lateral line
relationship: develops_from XAO:0000461 ! trunk placode (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0000470
name: unicellular gland (Xenopus)
def: "Any of the large number of glands of the larval skin, particularly common in the fins and adjacent skin of the trunk; also formed in the former frontal gland area on the upper jaw." [ISBN:0815318960]
is_a: UBERON:0003102 ! surface structure
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from XAO:0000320 ! sensorial layer (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0000471
name: xanthophore (Xenopus)
def: "A type of colored melanophore (mobile pigment cells of the dermis and epidermis) that contain fat-soluble carotenoids (obtained from the diet) and pteridines (synthesized from the cell) which are stored in pterinosomes. Their color depends on the pattern of carotenoids and pteridines. They are rarely found in pre-metamorphic larvae." [CL:0000430, ISBN:0226557634]
is_a: XAO:0003014 ! pigment cell (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0000472
name: iridophore (Xenopus)
def: "A pigment cell derived from the neural crest. The cell contains flat light-reflecting platelets, probably of guanine, in stacks called reflecting platets or iridisomes. The color-generating components produce a silver, gold, or iridescent color." [AAO:0010318]
synonym: "guanophore" RELATED []
is_a: XAO:0003014 ! pigment cell (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0001012
name: Stirnorgan (Xenopus)
def: "Structure that is part of the pineal system, is located in the skin on the dorsal surface of the head, and is exposed continuously to ambient illumination." [DOI:dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF00663609]
synonym: "frontal organ" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0000073 ! regional part of nervous system
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0010314 ! structure with developmental contribution from neural crest
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0001905 ! pineal body
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002104 ! visual system

[Term]
id: XAO:0001014
name: melanophore (Xenopus)
def: "A pigment cell that contains melanin (a brownish-black pigment), is derived from the neural crest, and is patchily distributed in the epidermis of the tadpole." [XAO:CJZ]
synonym: "melanocyte" RELATED []
is_a: XAO:0003014 ! pigment cell (Xenopus)
relationship: develops_from XAO:0004510 ! melanoblast (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0001016
name: abdominal myoblast (Xenopus)
def: "The myoblast that forms the muscles of the anterior abdominal walls." [AAO:0010314]
synonym: "abdominal musculature" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: XAO:0003015 ! myoblast (Xenopus)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003082 ! myotome

[Term]
id: XAO:0001018
name: anterior lymph sac (Xenopus)
def: "The protrusion of mesenchymal tissue of the anterior cardinal vein which forms lymph sacs." [PMID:17062017]
synonym: "rostral lymph sac" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0001919 ! endothelium of vein
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002465 ! lymphoid system

[Term]
id: XAO:0001021
name: notochordal epithelium (Xenopus)
def: "Outer layer of cells of the differentiating notochord, which give rise to the elastica externa and interna." [WEB:dev.biologists.org/content/1/4/411.abstract]
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
is_a: UBERON:0012275 ! meso-epithelium
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002328 ! notochord

[Term]
id: XAO:0001102
name: second pancreatic bud (Xenopus)
def: "Second of two pancreatic primordia that give rise to a ventral pancreatic bud." [XAO:EJS]
synonym: "pancreas" BROAD []
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0001041 ! foregut
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001007 ! digestive system

[Term]
id: XAO:0003003
name: unspecified (Xenopus)
def: "Unspecified Xenopus anatomical entity." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: UBERON:0001062 ! anatomical entity

[Term]
id: XAO:0003007
name: anatomical entity in vitro (Xenopus)
def: "An experimentally manipulated tissue or portion of the developing embryo, that can be culture alone (in vitro)." [XAO:curators]
is_a: UBERON:0001062 ! anatomical entity

[Term]
id: XAO:0003008
name: activin-induced ectoderm (Xenopus)
def: "Ectoderm section that has been dissected from the embryo, and treated with activin, and maintained in vitro." [PMID:14061885]
is_a: XAO:0003007 ! anatomical entity in vitro (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0003009
name: disaggregated/reaggregated ectoderm treated with activin (Xenopus)
def: "NF stage 8 ectoderm of Xenopus laevis embryos that have been cut and disaggregated. The cells have been treated with activin at a concentration to induce endodermal tissue. Afterwards the reaggregated cells have been cultured until control sibling embryos reach stage 12/13." [WEB:www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/UniGene/library.cgi?ORG=Xl&LID=1962]
is_a: XAO:0003007 ! anatomical entity in vitro (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0003014
name: pigment cell (Xenopus)
def: "Cell type that contains a deposition of coloring matter, the first of which differentiate during late tailbud stage, and that by NF stage 56 has produced a fully differentiated larval pigmentation pattern." [ISBN:0815318960, NLM:pigment+cell]
synonym: "chromatophore" RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
is_a: UBERON:0010313 ! neural crest-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0003083 ! trunk neural crest
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002097 ! skin of body

[Term]
id: XAO:0003015
name: myoblast (Xenopus)
def: "Embryonic (precursor) cell of the myogenic lineage that develops from the mesoderm." [CL:0000056]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003016
name: blastoderm cell (Xenopus)
def: "An undifferentiated cell produced by early cleavages of the fertilized egg (zygote)." [CL:0000353]
synonym: "blastomere" EXACT []
