def: "Individual secretory cells of the hatching gland that secrete an enzyme that dissolves or weakens the egg jelly and facilitates hatching." [XAO:curators]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
is_a: UBERON:0004121 ! ectoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0010314 ! structure with developmental contribution from neural crest
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002538 ! hatching gland

[Term]
id: XAO:0003252
name: keratin accumulating cell (Xenopus)
def: "A cell that is specialized to accumulate keratins, a family of fibrous structural proteins." [WEB:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keratin]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003253
name: ligament cell (Xenopus)
def: "Type of cell that is capable of generating and maintaining the fibrous connective tissue of the ligament." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000211 ! ligament

[Term]
id: XAO:0003254
name: Merkel cell (Xenopus)
def: "A modified epidermal cell located in the stratum basale. They are found mostly in areas where sensory perception is acute." [CL:0000242]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003255
name: mesodermal cell (Xenopus)
def: "A cell of the middle germ layer of the embryo." [CL:0000222]
synonym: "mesoderm cell" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000926 ! mesoderm

[Term]
id: XAO:0003256
name: mucus secreting cell (Xenopus)
def: "A type of epithelial cell, found in the epidermis and digestive system, whose function is to secrete mucin, which dissolves in water to form protective mucus." [WEB:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mucus]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003257
name: myelin accumulating cell (Xenopus)
def: "A cell that is specialized to accumulate myelin." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003258
name: neuromast mantle cell (Xenopus)
def: "A non-sensory cell type surrounding the neuromast support cells and neuromast hair cells, separating the neuromast from the epidermis, and secreting cupula in which the ciliary bundles of all the hair cells are embedded." [CL:0000851]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002097 ! skin of body

[Term]
id: XAO:0003259
name: neuromast support cell (Xenopus)
def: "A non-sensory cell of the neuromast that extends between the sensory hair cells from the basement membrane to the apical surface; neuromast support cells are surrounded by neuromast mantle cells." [CL:0000852]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002097 ! skin of body

[Term]
id: XAO:0003260
name: nucleate erythrocyte (Xenopus)
def: "An erythrocyte having a nucleus." [CL:0000562]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003261
name: olfactory epithelial support cell (Xenopus)
def: "A non-ciliated columnar cell that extends from the epithelial free margin to the basement membrane of the olfactory epithelium." [CL:0000853]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005725 ! olfactory system

[Term]
id: XAO:0003262
name: oxygen accumulating cell (Xenopus)
def: "A cell that is specialized to accumulate oxygen." [XAO:EJS]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003263
name: paracrine cell (Xenopus)
def: "A secretory cell that secretes an agonist into intercellular spaces in which it diffuses to a target cell other than that which produced it." [CL:0000512]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003264
name: pericyte (Xenopus)
def: "A slender, contractile, mesenchymal-like cell found in close association with capillary walls. They are relatively undifferentiated and may become fibroblasts, macrophages, or smooth muscle cells." [CL:0000669]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: XAO:0003265
name: somatic stem cell (Xenopus)
def: "A stem cell that can give rise to cell types of the body other than those of the germ-line." [CL:0000723]
is_a: XAO:0003054 ! stem cell (Xenopus)

[Term]
id: XAO:0003268
name: cardiac progenitor cell (Xenopus)
def: "Type of presumptive precardiac cell which lie as paired primordia 30 to 45 degrees on either side of the dorsal midline of the embryo. As gastrulation proceeds, these migrate laterally, eventually fusing at the anterior ventral midline, where they differentiate into cardiac tissue. They give rise to the linear heart tube of the fused heart primordium and derive from the cardiac crescent." [PMID:17194606, PMID:2340810]
synonym: "CPC" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003084 ! heart primordium

[Term]
id: XAO:0004023
name: craniofacial skeleton (Xenopus)
