[Term]
id: ZFA:0005707
name: lGx (Danio)
def: "Group of glomerulus located in the lateral region of the olfactory bulb. The  glomeruli that compose lGx are smaller than the lG1-6 and varied in shape, sizes, and locations between olfactory bulbs of the same and different animals. The lGx were located either along the ventral edge of the lateral group or below the lateral olfactory bulb surface." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120516-14]
