[Term]
id: ZFA:0005730
name: cranial motor neuron (Danio)
def: "Motor neuron that innervate muscles that control eye, jaw, and facial movements of the vertebrate head and parasympathetic neurons that innervate certain glands and organs." [ZFA:CVS]
synonym: "cranial motoneuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000100 ! motor neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000033 ! head

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005731
name: branchiomotor neuron (Danio)
def: "Cranial motor neuron which innervates muscles derived from the branchial (pharyngeal) arches." [PMID:14699587, ZFA:CVS]
synonym: "branchi motor neuron" EXACT []
synonym: "special visceral motor neuron" EXACT []
is_a: ZFA:0005730 ! cranial motor neuron (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005732
name: visceromotor neuron (Danio)
def: "Cranial motor neurons are found in the hindbrain, and innervate parasympathetic neurons that innervate tear glands, sweat glands, and the smooth muscles and glands of the pulmonary, cardiovascular, and gastrointestinal systems." [PMID:14699587, ZFA:CVS]
synonym: "general visceral motor neuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: ZFA:0005730 ! cranial motor neuron (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002028 ! hindbrain

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005733
name: somatomotor neuron (Danio)
def: "Cranial motor neurons found in the midbrain and hindbrain that innervates muscles that control eye and tongue." [PMID:14699587, ZFA:CVS]
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: ZFA:0005730 ! cranial motor neuron (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001891 ! midbrain
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002028 ! hindbrain

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005734
name: lacunocanalicular system (Danio)
def: "A system of osteocytes connected through canals within the vertebra.  Osteocytes extend processes through canals within ossified bone.  The lacunocanalicular system is poorly developed in zebrafish with most  osteocytes having one or two cytoplasmic processes." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-22629-14]
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002412 ! vertebra
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002481 ! bone tissue

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005735
name: lacunocanalicular canal (Danio)
def: "Anatomical space, part of the lacunocanalicular system that connects lacuna within bone tissue allowing osteocyte projections to connect." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-11518-14]
is_a: UBERON:0010276 ! space in vertebral column
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005734 ! lacunocanalicular system (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005736
name: lacuna (Danio)
def: "Anatomical space a small cavity, in the matrix of bone tissue. Part of the lacunocanalicular system." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: UBERON:0010276 ! space in vertebral column
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005734 ! lacunocanalicular system (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005737
name: intestinal rod (Danio)
def: "Multicellular structure composed of endodermal cells that forms a continuous rod along the anterior-posterior axis of the embryo in contact with the YSL.  This rod will give rise to the endodermal components of the alimentary canal and its connected organs: liver, gall bladder pancreas and swim bladder. Does not have part pharyngeal endoderm." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-030115-26]
synonym: "endodermal rod" RELATED [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-030115-26]
synonym: "intestinal anlage" RELATED [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050120-6.]
is_a: UBERON:0000481 ! multi-tissue structure
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005738
name: intestinal bulb primordium (Danio)
def: "Portion of the intestinal rod that loops to left between 26-30hpf and gives rise to the intestinal bulb and liver and anterior pancreatic primordium.  The endoderm at this stage is a compact mass of cells with little to no polarization." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-031103-19]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from ZFA:0005737 ! intestinal rod (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005739
name: pancreatic acinar cell (Danio)
def: "A secretory cell found in pancreatic acini that secretes digestive enzymes and mucins. This cell is a typical zymogenic cell, has a basal nucleus and basophilic cytoplasm consisting of regular arrays of granular endoplasmic reticulum with mitochondria and dense secretory granules." [GOC:tfm, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
is_a: CL:0000622 ! acinar cell
is_a: CL:1001599 ! pancreas exocrine glandular cell
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005741 ! pancreatic acinar gland (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005740
name: pancreatic centroacinar cell (Danio)
def: "A cuboidal epithelial cell that is continuous with the lining of intercalated ducts that drain the acinus. This cell type secretes a high pH solution to aid in activation of zymogens, and can differentiate into endocrine and exocrine pancreatic cell types." [GOC:tfm, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
synonym: "CAC" EXACT [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
is_a: CL:0000075 ! columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell
is_a: CL:1001433 ! epithelial cell of exocrine pancreas
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005741 ! pancreatic acinar gland (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005741
name: pancreatic acinar gland (Danio)
def: "Portion of exocrine pancreas that is comprised of polarized cells containing apical zymogen granules that store digestive enzymes such as trypsin and chymotrypsin and abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum and mitochondria." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-070310-3]
synonym: "exocrine glands pancreas" EXACT []
synonym: "pancreatic acini" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005753 ! pancreatic lobule (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005742
name: pancreatic PP cell (Danio)
def: "Polypeptide producing cell located in the islets of the pancreas." [GOC:tfm]
synonym: "pancreatic F cells " RELATED []
synonym: "pancreatic polypeptide-secreting cell" EXACT []
synonym: "PP cell of pancreatic islet" EXACT []
synonym: "PP-cell of pancreatic islet" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000083 ! epithelial cell of pancreas
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000016 ! endocrine pancreas

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005743
name: pancreatic D cell (Danio)
def: "A D cell located in the pancreas. Peripherally placed within the islets like type A cells; contains somatostatin." [CL:tfm]
synonym: "D-cell of pancreatic islet" EXACT []
synonym: "delta cell of islet" EXACT []
synonym: "pancreatic delta cell" EXACT []
synonym: "somatostatin-secreting pancreatic cell" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000173 ! pancreatic D cell
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005744
name: notochord outer sheath cell (Danio)
def: "Cells that  form an epithelial-like sheath around the vacuolated inner notochord cells. Outer cells secrete a thick extracellular perinotochordal basement membrane." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130322-23]
synonym: "notochord sheath cell" RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000066 ! epithelial cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002328 ! notochord

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005745
name: structural cell (Danio)
def: "A cell whose primary function is to provide structural support, to provide strength and physical integrity to the organism." [TAIR:sr]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005746
name: notochord inner cell (Danio)
def: "Structural cell of notochord that contain one large fluid-filled intracellular vacuole that occupies most of the cell volume." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130322-23]
synonym: "chordocytes" EXACT []
is_a: ZFA:0005745 ! structural cell (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002328 ! notochord

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005747
name: supraintestinal lymphatic vessel (Danio)
def: "Lymph vessels that are located on either side of the PCV in the posterior region of the intestine." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120529-43]
synonym: "SIL" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004536 ! lymph vasculature

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005748
name: intrapancreatic duct (Danio)
def: "Digestive duct within the pancreas.  The pancreatic duct carries inactive digestive enzymes to the intestine." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101201-32]
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:0007329 ! pancreatic duct

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005749
name: intercalated duct pancreas (Danio)
def: "The portion of the intrapancreatic duct leading from the pancreatic acinar gland to the intralobular duct." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
is_a: ZFA:0005748 ! intrapancreatic duct (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005750
name: pancreatic intralobular duct (Danio)
def: "Intrapancreatic duct within a pancreatic lobe that connects all the  intercalated duct with an interlobular duct.  The intralobular duct is lined with cuboidal cells." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
is_a: ZFA:0005748 ! intrapancreatic duct (Danio)
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005753 ! pancreatic lobule (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005751
name: pancreatic interlobular duct (Danio)
def: "Intrapancreatic duct that connects the intralobular duct to the main pancreatic duct." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: ZFA:0005748 ! intrapancreatic duct (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005752
name: main intrapancreatic duct (Danio)
def: "Intrapancreatic duct that connects to the interlobular ducts and drains into the extrapancreatic duct.  The main duct may not be present in all larva and may develop in a segmented fashion." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-070310-3]
is_a: ZFA:0005748 ! intrapancreatic duct (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005753
name: pancreatic lobule (Danio)
def: "Cluster of acinar glands surrounding an intralobular duct." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
synonym: "exocrine lobule" EXACT [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-050623-3]
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0000477 ! anatomical cluster
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000017 ! exocrine pancreas

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005754
name: primary islet (Danio)
def: "The primary islet is the first islet to develop." [ZFA:CVS]
synonym: "principal islet" EXACT []
is_a: ZFA:0005755 ! islet (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005755
name: islet (Danio)
def: "Portion of tissue composed of a group of cells in the pancreas producing insulin, glucagon and somatostatin. Part of the endocrine pancreas." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: UBERON:0000077 ! mixed endoderm/mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000016 ! endocrine pancreas

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005756
name: secondary islet (Danio)
def: "Islet that develops after the primary islet." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: ZFA:0005755 ! islet (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005757
name: mid diencephalic organizer (Danio)
def: "Portion of tissue composed of the signal-generating cells within the zona limitans intrathalamica." [ZFA:CVS, ZFA:DF, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-100621-4, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120105-73]
synonym: "MDO" EXACT []
synonym: "mid-diencephalic organizer" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of UBERON:0009848 ! zona limitans intrathalamica

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005758
name: pancreatic fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue interspersed within the pancreatic acini." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue
is_a: UBERON:0003586 ! trunk connective tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005753 ! pancreatic lobule (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005759
name: visceral fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue on the surface of the organs within the pleuroperitoneal cavity. Visceral adipocytes were observed posterior to the swim bladder and lining the visceral cavity." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
synonym: "visceral fat deposit" RELATED []
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue
is_a: UBERON:0003586 ! trunk connective tissue
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
relationship: part_of UBERON:2002224 ! pleuroperitoneal cavity

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005760
name: cranial fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue in the cranium. Cranial adipocytes are located within the ventral wall of the cranium, situated between the brain and the esophagus." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue
is_a: UBERON:0003566 ! head connective tissue

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005761
name: periorbital fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue surrounding the eye." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: ZFA:0005760 ! cranial fat (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001697 ! orbit of skull

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005762
name: subcutaneous fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue between muscle and integument." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-111012-7]
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005763
name: esophageal fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue surrounding the esophagus." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue
is_a: UBERON:0003566 ! head connective tissue

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005764
name: mandibular fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue deposited along the mandible." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
synonym: "jaw fat deposit" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0001013 ! adipose tissue
is_a: UBERON:0003566 ! head connective tissue
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003278 ! skeleton of lower jaw

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005766
name: pectoral fin plate fat (Danio)
def: "Adipose tissue that forms at the base of the pectoral fin." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-090417-9]
synonym: "pectoral fin plate deposit" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: ZFA:0005762 ! subcutaneous fat (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000151 ! pectoral fin

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005767
name: caudal fin fat (Danio)
def: "Subcutaneous adipose tissue deposit at the base of the caudal fin." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-101011-51]
synonym: "tail fin fat" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0003599 ! tail connective tissue
is_a: ZFA:0005762 ! subcutaneous fat (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:4000164 ! caudal fin

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005768
name: trigeminal sensory neuron (Danio)
def: "Sensory neuron that extends a single axon shaft along the lateral white matter of the hindbrain and spinal cord. Numerous medially projecting branches are later formed and innervate a series of target nuclei along the anteroposterior axis of the hindbrain and spinal cord.  The highly branched axons innervate the integument of the head.  There are several subtypes with different afferent branching morphologies." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120106-15]
is_a: CL:0000101 ! sensory neuron

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005769
name: spermatid (Danio)
def: "A male germ cell that develops from the haploid secondary spermatocytes. Without further division, spermatids undergo structural changes and give rise to spermatozoa." [CL:editor]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: develops_from CL:0000017 ! spermatocyte
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000473 ! testis

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005770
name: crypt neuron olfactory support cell (Danio)
def: "Specialized olfactory support cell that surrounds crypt olfactory sensory neurons.   There are one or two support cells for each crypt neuron.  The cytoplasm of crypt neuron olfactory support cells is less electron dense then other support cells.  They also bear numerous microvilli at their apical rim. When two supporting cells are present, they interdigitate with each other  Mitochondria in crypt supporting cells are larger than those in the common supporting cells." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-060724-7]
is_a: CL:0000630 ! supportive cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005771
name: ectomesenchyme (Danio)
def: "Portion of tissue that develops from the cranial neural crest and which cells populate a series of pharyngeal arches from which develops the support skeleton of the jaw and gills." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-110609-14, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120517-11]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
is_a: UBERON:0010313 ! neural crest-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0003099 ! cranial neural crest

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005772
name: fertilized egg (Danio)
def: "Diploid cell produced by the fusion of sperm cell nucleus and egg cell." [GOC:tjm]
synonym: "zygote " EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005773
name: embryonic blood vessel endothelial progenitor cell (Danio)
def: "An endothelial progenitor cell that participates in angiogenesis during development." [GOC:tjm]
is_a: CL:0000222 ! mesodermal cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005774
name: atrial epicardium (Danio)
def: "The external layer of the atrium bounding the atrial myocardium." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-100112-31]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002348 ! epicardium

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005775
name: enteric neuron (Danio)
def: "Neuron that is part of the enteric nervous system." [CL:MAH]
is_a: CL:0007011 ! enteric neuron
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005776
name: parasympathetic neuron (Danio)
def: "Parasympathetic neurons are part of the parasympathetic nervous system and the cell bodies lie in the brain and sacral region of the spinal cord. The neurons are mainly cholinergic." [ISBN:0080923437]
is_a: CL:0000107 ! autonomic neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000011 ! parasympathetic nervous system

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005777
name: sympathetic neuron (Danio)
def: "Sympathetic neurons are part of the sympathetic nervous system and are primarily adrenergic producing the neurotransmitter noradrenalin along with other neuropeptides." [ISBN:0080923437]
is_a: CL:0000107 ! autonomic neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000013 ! sympathetic nervous system

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005778
name: hypocretin-secreting neuron (Danio)
def: "A neuron that releases hypocretin as a neurotransmitter." [PMID:23848055]
synonym: "orexin secreting neuron " RELATED []
is_a: CL:0000540 ! neuron

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005780
name: immature thymic epithelium (Danio)
def: "Epithelium of the thymus primordium composed of cells of immature morphology. The immature thymic epithelium is continuous with the pharyngeal epithelium.  The immature thymic epithelium is composed of electron-lucent epithelial cells of irregular or polygonal shape and contain numerous ribosomes, large electron-lucent mitochondria, and rough endoplasmic reticulum. Nascent desmosomes join these primitive epithelial cells together." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-990414-60]
is_a: UBERON:0010313 ! neural crest-derived structure
is_a: UBERON:0010371 ! ecto-epithelium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005562 ! thymus primordium

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005784
name: striated muscle cell (Danio)
def: "Muscle cell which has as its direct parts myofilaments organized into sarcomeres." [GOC:tfm, ISBN:0721662544]
is_a: CL:0000187 ! muscle cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005785
name: esophageal striated muscle (Danio)
def: "Striated muscle of the esophogus. Permits voluntary swallowing." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130709-61]
is_a: UBERON:0003832 ! esophagus muscle
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005786
name: cleft cell (Danio)
def: "Wedge-shaped epidermal cell positioned along the apex of the developing fin fold. Each cleft cell retains a wedge-shaped form during fold formation and develops a basal cleft-shaped invagination. Invaginations are aligned in neighboring cleft cells so that these cells cap the distal boundary of the subepidermal space where collagenous extracellular fibres called actinotrichia run anteroposteriorly along the length of the fin fold." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-195]
is_a: CL:0000362 ! epidermal cell
relationship: part_of UBERON:2000040 ! median fin fold

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005787
name: hypophyseal artery (Danio)
def: "Artery that runs along the midline from anterior to posterior regions of the hypothalamus and splits into two capillary branches (hyc). The formation of the artery is initiated at the hypophysis itself and extends anteriorly until it connects with the palatocerebral arteries at day 2.5." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-111027-47, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130222-26]
is_a: UBERON:0001637 ! artery
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
is_a: UBERON:0003496 ! head blood vessel
is_a: UBERON:0003499 ! brain blood vessel

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005788
name: hypophyseal vein (Danio)
def: "Vein thats tarts posterior of the hypophysis and drains the hypophyseal capillaries.  It empties into the primary head sinus." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130222-26]
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
is_a: UBERON:0003496 ! head blood vessel
is_a: UBERON:0003499 ! brain blood vessel
is_a: UBERON:0009141 ! craniocervical region vein

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005789
name: preopticohypophyseal tract (Danio)
def: "Axon tract originating  from the two hemispheres of the neurosecretory preoptic areas  converging into the midline and terminating at the ventral part of the hypothalamus at the presumed location of the pituitary. Analogous to the supraopticohypophyseal tract in mammals." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-111027-47]
synonym: "preopticohypophyseal axon tract" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0002316 ! white matter

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005790
name: hypophyseal capillary (Danio)
def: "Pair of capillaries that bilaterally encompass the hypophysis starting at the anterior aspect of the hypophysis (pituitary).   Directly posterior to the pituitary, the two capillaries fuse with the hypophyseal vein." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-130222-26]
is_a: UBERON:0001982 ! capillary
is_a: UBERON:0002616 ! regional part of brain
is_a: UBERON:0003496 ! head blood vessel
is_a: UBERON:0003499 ! brain blood vessel
is_a: UBERON:0003714 ! neural tissue

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005791
name: breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Surface structure that is a keratinized epidermal appendages that is a contact organ and secondary sex organ." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140519-1]
is_a: UBERON:3000961 ! external integument structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005792
name: jaw flap (Danio)
def: "Surface structure that is a protrusion from the rostral end of the jaw, supported by the mandibular projection." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140519-1]
synonym: "lateral projections lower jaw" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0003102 ! surface structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005793
name: superficial layer of breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Layer of smooth cells composing the outer layer of the breeding tubercle.  Cells in this layer have a high keratin content, lamellar bodies, and condensed chromosomes.  This layer is repeatedly shed and regenerated." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005794
name: second tier layer of breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Cell layer that lies underneath the superficial layer of the breeding tubercle.  Characterized by tight junctions within the layer." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005795
name: spinous layer of breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Intermediate layer of the breeding tubercles characterized by cells with  loose spinous organization connected to each other via desmosomes, but with wide extracellular spaces in between." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29]
synonym: "spinous keratinocyte layer" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005796
name: basal layer breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Layer of breeding tubercle proximal to basal lamina of the integument." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! simple tissue
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005797
name: pectoral fin breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Breeding tubercles along the surface of the pectoral fin lepidotrichium of males." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140519-1]
is_a: UBERON:0004120 ! mesoderm-derived structure
is_a: ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000151 ! pectoral fin
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003101 ! male organism

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005798
name: jaw row breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Surface structures composed of breeding tubercles arranged in a double row in the medial region on each side of the lower jaw." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140519-1]
is_a: ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005799
name: jaw flap breeding tubercle (Danio)
def: "Breeding tubercles that cover the surface of the jaw flap." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140519-1]
is_a: ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005800
name: extracellular lipid lamellae (Danio)
def: "Portion of organism substance that is located between the cap and second tier layers of the breeding tubercles.  The lipid lamellae is composed of lipids." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-140317-29]
is_a: UBERON:0000463 ! non-tissue substance
relationship: part_of ZFA:0005791 ! breeding tubercle (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005801
name: interrenal vessel (Danio)
def: "The interrenal vessel (IRV) is the blood vessels supplying the interrenal gland. It is formed by sprouting from the dorsal aorta.  The development of the IRV is temporally and spatially correlated with the initiation interrenal gland formation.  After traversing the interrenal tissue, the IRV connects  to the posterior end segment of the anterior mesenteric artery where two branches of swim bladder arteries branched out.  Angiogenic sprout is visible between 34 and 48 hpf with blood flow by 3dpf." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120905-5]
synonym: "IRV" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0003517 ! kidney blood vessel
relationship: develops_from ZFA:0005802 ! interrenal  angiogenic sprout (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006856 ! interrenal gland

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005802
name: interrenal  angiogenic sprout (Danio)
def: "Sprout from the dorsal aorta that develops into the interrenal vessel." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-120905-5]
is_a: UBERON:0005291 ! embryonic tissue
is_a: ZFA:0005604 ! angiogenic sprout (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006857 ! interrenal primordium

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005803
name: cupula (Danio)
def: "Gelatinous substance surrounding the kinocila of the neuromast." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-768]
is_a: UBERON:0000463 ! non-tissue substance
relationship: part_of UBERON:0008904 ! neuromast

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005804
name: rhombencephalic efferent neurons to the lateral line (Danio)
def: "Efferent neuron where the cell body is located in the hindbrain reticular formation immediately adjacent to the medial longitudinal fascicle at the rostrocaudal level between the MiDl and the CaD and adjacent to the descending Mauthner axon.  RELL dendrites are large and extend bilaterally into the ventrolateral neuropil.  The ipsilateral dendrite reaches into a single area of the ventrolateral neuropil whereas the contralateral dendrite branches and extends into two different levels of the same rostrocaudal column of the ventrolateral neuropil. The axon emerges from the ventral part of the perikaryon courses a short distance rostrally to the level of the ROLE  cells and then turns laterally from the CNS accompanying the root of the posterior lateral line nerve." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-768]
synonym: "RELL neuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000527 ! efferent neuron
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: CL:2000032 ! peripheral nervous system neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002028 ! hindbrain
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002540 ! lateral line system

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005805
name: rhombencephalic octavola-teral efferent neuron (Danio)
def: "Efferent neuron located in the hindbrain.  The axon of ROLE cells travels rostrally near the ipsilateral medial longitudinal fascicle to the level of the Mauthner cell where it turns laterally to exit with the eighth nerve.  Outside the brain the  axon continues ventrally  to the base of the saccular macula in the ear then turns caudally to ender the ganglion of the posterior lateral line.   A branch of the axon  turns ventrally before the main axon enters the LLG.  The branch goes ventrally along the wall of the otic capsule." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-768]
synonym: "ROLE neuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000527 ! efferent neuron
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001891 ! midbrain

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005806
name: diencephalic efferent neurons to the lateral line (Danio)
def: "Efferent neurons located ventrally in the diencephalon.  The dendrites extend into a large area of the diencephalic neuropil rostral, caudal, lateral and ventral to the cell body.  The axon courses dorsally and then caudally through the midbrain.   As the axon descends through the brain it gives off branches at several levels.   One branch usually exits the brain with the posterior lateral line nerve.  The axon can be traced into the cervical spinal cord." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-768]
synonym: "DELL neuron" EXACT []
is_a: CL:0000527 ! efferent neuron
is_a: CL:2000029 ! central nervous system neuron
is_a: CL:2000032 ! peripheral nervous system neuron
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001894 ! diencephalon
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002540 ! lateral line system

[Term]
id: ZFA:0005815
name: T interneuron (Danio)
def: "Hindbrain interneurons that are part of the reticular formation.  The T interneurons receive synaptic input from the  Mauthner neuron.  The axon is T-shaped the proximal segment courses to the midline of the  brain and near the midline bifurcates to form an ascending rostral segment and a descending caudal segment.  The rostral and caudal segments join the dorsal component of the MLF.  The T interneurons are located caudal to CaD and appear to be bilaterally paired." [ZFA:CVS, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-588]
synonym: "T shaped reticular neuron " RELATED []
synonym: "T-interneuron" EXACT []
is_a: ZFA:0005209 ! hindbrain interneuron (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0006000
name: intermediate hypothalamus (Danio)
def: "Brain structure that lies perpendicular to the longitudinal axis of the embryonic neural tube, is continuous with the rostral hypothalamic proliferation and whose most lateral extent is deflected dorsally within the inferior lobe." [ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-001018-1, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-020730-6, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-081114-19]
synonym: "Hi" EXACT []
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001898 ! hypothalamus

[Term]
id: ZFA:0007056
name: pillar of the posterior semicircular canal (Danio)
def: "Pillar of the semicircular canal around whose perimeter runs the posterior semicircular canal." [ZFA:YMB, ZFIN:ZDB-PUB-961014-383]
synonym: "horizontal hub" RELATED []
synonym: "posterior hub of the semicircular canal" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior pillar" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior pillar of the semicircular" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:2002223 ! pillar of the semicircular canal
relationship: develops_from UBERON:2000232 ! lateral semicircular canal primordium
relationship: develops_from UBERON:2000412 ! posterior semicircular canal primordium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001842 ! posterior semicircular canal

[Term]
id: ZFA:0007069
name: otic squamous epithelium (Danio)
def: "Is an otic epithelium composed of cells with a squamous morphology." [ISBN:019514502X, ZFA:YMB]
is_a: UBERON:0003249 ! epithelium of otic placode

[Term]
id: ZFA:0007070
name: otic sensory epithelium (Danio)
def: "Is an otic epithelium that is a neuroepithelium which is pseudostratified and senses sound." [ZFA:YMB]
is_a: UBERON:0003249 ! epithelium of otic placode

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009372
name: duct epithelial cell (Danio)
def: "Epithelial cell part of duct." [ZFA:CVS]
is_a: CL:0000068 ! duct epithelial cell

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009379
name: intrahepatic bile duct epithelial cell (Danio)
def: "An epithelial cell of the intrahepatic portion of the bile duct." [GOC:tfm]
is_a: ZFA:0009372 ! duct epithelial cell (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003704 ! intrahepatic bile duct

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009380
name: pancreatic ductal cell (Danio)
def: "Epithelial cell found in the ducts of the pancreas." [GOC:tfm]
is_a: CL:1001433 ! epithelial cell of exocrine pancreas
is_a: ZFA:0009372 ! duct epithelial cell (Danio)
relationship: part_of UBERON:0007329 ! pancreatic duct

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009383
name: endo-epithelial cell (Danio)
def: "An epithelial cell derived from endoderm." [GOC:tfm]
is_a: CL:0000066 ! epithelial cell
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009397
name: cholangiocyte (Danio)
def: "An epithelial cell that is part of the bile duct. Cholangiocytes contribute to bile secretion via net release of bicarbonate and water. They are cuboidal epithelium in the small interlobular bile ducts, but become columnar and mucus secreting in larger bile ducts approaching the porta hepatis and the extrahepatic ducts." [PMID:16550043, PMID:18356246]
synonym: "bile duct cells" RELATED []
synonym: "epithelial cell of bile duct" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
is_a: ZFA:0009372 ! duct epithelial cell (Danio)
relationship: develops_from ZFA:0009398 ! hepatoblast (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009398
name: hepatoblast (Danio)
def: "Multi fate stem cell that gives rise to both hepatocytes and cholangiocytes as descendants." [PMID:18356246, PMID:20483998, ZFA:CVS]
is_a: CL:0000048 ! multi fate stem cell
is_a: UBERON:0004119 ! endoderm-derived structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0003894 ! liver primordium

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009399
name: intestinal epithelial cell (Danio)
def: "An epithelial cell of the intestine." [GOC:tfm]
is_a: CL:0002563 ! intestinal epithelial cell
is_a: ZFA:0009383 ! endo-epithelial cell (Danio)

[Term]
id: ZFA:0009400
name: epithelial cell of esophagus (Danio)
def: "An epithelial cell of the esophagus." [GOC:tfm]
is_a: CL:0002252 ! epithelial cell of esophagus
is_a: ZFA:0009383 ! endo-epithelial cell (Danio)

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002375
name: in branching relationship with
def: "A relationship that holds between two material entities in a system of connected structures, where the branching relationship holds based on properties of the connecting network." []
is_a: part_of ! part_of

[Typedef]
id: action_notes
name: actions_notes
namespace: uberon
def: "Notes on how instances of this class functon biomechanically." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
xref: UBPROP:0000014
property_value: editor_note "This annotation property may be replaced with an annotation property from an external ontology such as IAO" xsd:string
is_metadata_tag: true

[Typedef]
id: ambiguous_for_taxon
name: ambiguous_for_taxon
namespace: uberon
def: "S ambiguous_for_taxon T if the class S does not have a clear referent in taxon T. An example would be the class 'manual digit 1', which encompasses a homology hypotheses that is accepted for some species (e.g. human and mouse), but does not have a clear referent in Aves - the referent is dependent on the hypothesis embraced, and also on the ontogenetic stage." [PHENOSCPAE:asilomar_mtg]
xref: RO:0002173
is_metadata_tag: true
is_class_level: true

[Typedef]
id: appendage_segment_number
name: appendage segment number
namespace: uberon
def: "x appendage_segment_number N if and only if (i) x is a appendage_segment, and (ii) x is appendage_segment number N in a series of appendage_segments repeated along an proximo-distal axis, with appendage_segment_number 1 being the proximalmost appendage_segment (in tetrapods this would be the stylopod, as we do not classify girdles as appendage segments)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
comment: Examples: in dropsphila coxa=1, trochanter=2, femur=3, tibia=4, tarsal segments 1-5=5-9, pretarsus=10
xref: UBPROP:0000110
property_value: is_count_of UBERON:0010758
property_value: preceding_element_is BSPO:0000100
is_metadata_tag: true

[Typedef]
id: axiom_lost_from_external_ontology
name: axiom_lost_from_external_ontology
namespace: uberon
def: "A textual description of an axiom loss in this ontology compared to an external ontology." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
comment: This annotation property may be replaced with an annotation property from an external ontology such as IAO
xref: UBPROP:0000002
is_metadata_tag: true

[Typedef]
id: bounding_layer_of
name: bounding layer of
namespace: uberon
def: "X outer_layer_of Y iff:\n. X :continuant that bearer_of some PATO:laminar\n. X part_of Y\n. exists Z :surface\n. X has_boundary Z\n. Z boundary_of Y\n\nhas_boundary: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002002\nboundary_of: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002000" []
comment: A relationship that applies between a continuant and its outer, bounding layer. Examples include the relationship between a multicellular organism and its integument, between an animal cell and its plasma membrane, and between a membrane bound organelle and its outer/bounding membrane.
xref: RO:0002007
is_a: part_of ! part_of

[Typedef]
id: branching_part_of
name: branching part of
name: branching_part_of
namespace: uberon
def: "x is a branching part of y if and only if x is part of y and x is connected directly or indirectly to the main stem of y" []
xref: RO:0002380
property_value: editor_note "we need to check if FMA branch_of implies part_of. the relation we intend to use here should - for example, see vestibulocochlear nerve" xsd:string
is_a: part_of ! part_of
is_a: RO:0002375 ! in branching relationship with
inverse_of: has_branching_part ! has branching part

